INSERT_UPDATE Presenter; code[unique = true]                  ; name[lang = en]                                               ; biography[lang = en]; websiteUrl; image(code, $contentCV)
                       ; 8b7d9ab5-ea5e-43ff-95da-83873fc45899 ; James Munro, ND                                               ; James Munro, ND, graduated from the National University of Natural Medicine in Portland, OR, with a doctorate in naturopathic medicine. Initially serving as the director of clinical services at XYMOGEN, Dr. Munro is the medical director and senior director of innovation for XYMOGEN and WholeScripts, helping develop and produce exclusive professional formulas that provide quality supplements to healthcare practitioners. His dedication to providing top-quality care, especially in chronic diseases related to the gut–brain axis, has led him to take the social media world by storm as he imparts his wealth of knowledge. Dr. Munro shares his wisdom on LinkedIn, Twitter, YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, and Facebook and writes his own series of motivational blog posts on jamesistrying.com. ; ; munro-cutout-1
                       ; 36066998-d75e-4e22-83bd-53a416b5e22f ; Richard Horowitz, MD                                          ; Richard Horowitz, MD, is a board-certified internist in private practice in Hyde Park, NY, and the medical director of the Hudson Valley Healing Arts Center. Dr. Horowitz has treated over 13,000 chronic Lyme disease patients and is a founding member of the International Lyme and Associated Diseases Society. He is the author of the New York Times best-selling books Why Can’t I Get Better? Solving the Mystery of Lyme and Chronic Disease and Can I Get Better? Dr. Horowitz is a popular TV and radio guest, highly sought-after lecturer, and Tick-Borne Disease Working Group member, which reviews federal activities and research related to tick-borne diseases and provides recommendations to Congress for changes or improvements. ; https://lymeconnection.org/ ; horowitz
                       ; 02c47856-112f-4567-9d21-942c48d63b83 ; Jaquel Patterson, ND, MBA                                     ; Jaquel Patterson, ND, MBA, is a nationally recognized naturopathic physician, success coach, best-selling author, and sought-after speaker. She founded of Fairfield Family Medicine, a multidisciplinary medical practice in Fairfield, CT, offering naturopathic medicine, nutrition, internal medicine, physical therapy, and acupuncture. Her clinical expertise is in autoimmune conditions, Lyme disease, anxiety/depression, and childhood developmental disorders. Dr. Patterson is a conference presenter and television and radio guest. She has been published in Forbes, New York Magazine, USA Today, Real Simple, Under Armour, Fitness Pal, Natural Practitioner, and Naturopathic Doctor News and Review. Dr. Patterson is the medical advisor for ZyCal Bioceuticals Healthcare and Vermont Hemp Health. ; https://www.fairfieldfamilyhealth.com ; jaquel_patterson
                       ; b5e27efe-449c-42f9-b81e-bdb03652783a ; William Davis, MD                                             ; William Davis, MD, is a cardiologist and #1 New York Times bestselling author of the Wheat Belly series of books and, more recently, Super Gut. Recent human clinical trials that Dr. Davis conducted have revealed that losing (fat) weight while preserving muscle is possible, thereby preventing weight regain and enjoying improved body composition. Dr. Davis is also the Chief Medical Officer at Realize Therapeutics Corp., which he cofounded to explore the new science of the microbiome to improve health and appearance, including body composition. ; https://drdavisinfinitehealth.com/ ; william-cutout
                       ; a740df2b-a3d2-4727-aa18-91fff4a31c25 ; Jerry Simons, PA                                              ; Gerald Simons, PA, has more than 25 years of experience in managing patients with complex autoimmune and infectious diseases. He is a recipient of the Tick Borne Disease Alliance (now Global Lyme Alliance) National Humanitarian Award. In addition to clinical practice, he is an assistant professor at Stony Brook University in Stony Brook, NY. Jerry was awarded the top national award for skills as a surgical physician assistant, has won more than 12 state and national awards as a medical educator, and has lectured internationally. ; https://healthprofessions.stonybrookmedicine.edu/gerald_simons ; jerry_simons
                       ; 5622754d-67b5-43af-b3b0-910d50847c2a ; Regina Druz, MD, FACC, IFMCP                                  ; Regina Druz, MD, FACC, IFMCP, is a physician, an executive, and a digital health expert. Dr. Druz is the Director of Integrative Cardiology at St. Francis Hospital, a certified practitioner through the Institute for Functional Medicine (IFMCP), and the creator of Fit in Your GENES, an integrative cardiology program based on functional medicine principles. Her vision is to transform healthcare through digital health and integrative practice innovation, empowering every patient and practitioner to collaborate for optimal health and wellness. She holds leadership positions with the American College of Cardiology and is a digital health expert for the Food and Drug Administration. ; https://holisticheartcenters.com/fit-in-your-genes-weighless/ ; reginadruz
                       ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; Cheryl Burdette, ND                                           ; Cheryl Burdette, ND, is the director of education and the naturopathic residency program at Progressive Medical: the founder and educational director of a functional laboratory, Precision Point Diagnostics: a partner at TheraDura: and the director of education for XYMOGEN. She is also involved in study design and translational research and has lectured extensively internationally. Dr. Burdette’s passions are teaching the practices of integrative and naturopathic medicine and increasing awareness of evidence-based natural therapies. ; https://xymogen.com/ ; cheryl_burdette
                       ; 6ff089f5-8193-4321-a405-2f38d70a26cc ; Milton Bastidas, DC                                           ; Milton Bastidas, DC, is the founder of True Lifelong Wellness Center, the vice president for the College of Integrative Medicine, and the director of research and development at Transformation Enzyme Corporation. He is also an expert in using laboratory analysis and enzyme nutrition as part of a functional and natural approach to well-being. As a lead researcher in Transformation Enzyme Corporation’s research and development team, Dr. Bastidas has codirected 2 clinical studies showing the benefits of enzyme supplementation on systemic inflammation and gastrointestinal dysfunction and a recent pilot study on the effects of enzyme therapy on Glyphosate detoxification. He is currently involved in developing specific treatment protocols depending on the patient’s biochemical individuality. ; https://www.transformationenzymes.com/ ; milton_bastidas
                       ; 91a3754c-d5ff-48f1-88f0-801e4eba3657 ; Will Cole, DC, DNM, IFMCP                                     ; Will Cole, DC, DNM, IFMCP, received his doctorate from the Southern California University of Health Sciences and postdoctorate education and training in functional medicine and clinical nutrition. He is a leading functional medicine expert who consults people worldwide via webcam, having started one of the world’s first functional medicine telehealth centers. Named one of the top 50 functional and integrative doctors in the nation, Dr. Cole specializes in clinically investigating underlying factors of chronic disease and customizing a functional medicine approach for thyroid issues, autoimmune conditions, hormonal imbalances, digestive disorders, and brain problems. He is also the host of the popular “The Art of Being Well” podcast and bestselling author of Ketotarian, Gut Feelings, The Inflammation Spectrum, and the New York Times bestseller Intuitive Fasting. ; https://www.drwillcole.com ; will_cole

                       ; 8cd4190d-dc84-435d-aa6f-88ad239be9df ; Gregory Kelly,ND                                              ; Gregory Kelly, ND, graduated with his Doctor of Naturopathic Medicine degree from the Southwest College of Naturopathic Medicine & Health Sciences (now Sonoran University of Health Sciences) in Tempe, Arizona. He is the senior director of product development at the Neurohacker Collective. Dr. Kelly is the author of the book Shape Shift, has been a guest on leading health and performance podcasts, including Dave Asprey’s The Human Upgrade and Jim Kwik’s Kwik Brain, and has taught courses on advanced clinical nutrition. ; https://neurohacker.com ; gregory-kelly
                       ; 4d7259d8-ca86-4d0b-a93c-9f592541f227 ; Tracy Harrison                                                ; Tracy Harrison holds 3 degrees from the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, is certified by The Institute for Functional Medicine, and is the founder of The School of Applied Functional Medicine™, a well-respected, accredited continuing education program rooted in the science and practical application of functional medicine.  Tracy is passionate about transforming healthcare with the powerful combination of functional medicine and savvy clinical partnership. Her vision is for a Good Medicine Movement™, honoring allopathic disease care and establishing a true healthcare system with proactive, preventive, patient-centric, personalized, systems-driven, root cause medical science and partnerships that minimize the disease care burden. ; https://schoolafm.com/ ; tracy_harrison
                       ; 692cad63-c2bd-487d-9254-4ee35284cc01 ; Alyson Evans                                                  ; Alyson Evans, DC, has dedicated the last 20 years to combining her passions for healthcare and education with pursuing her purpose of building and serving a team. She has helped grow multiple businesses by prioritizing professional education and product innovation. Dr. Evans is the Owner and Founder of Fringe, a company blending yesterday’s medicine with today’s science, grounded by its dedication to improving how we live and how we learn. ; https://fringeheals.com/ ; alyson_evans
                       ; 63caae5f-cb97-43a3-83b5-faffc84eb8b0 ; Laurel Sterling, MA, RDN, CDN                                 ; Laurel Sterling, MA, RDN, CDN, is a registered dietitian-nutritionist and certified dietary nutritionist. She has worked in the natural products industry since 2000 as a counselor and educator. Laurel has a genuine passion for informing, educating, and empowering the public on health and nutrition through her lectures, articles, blogs, and radio and podcast appearances. She regularly attends various medical, dietetic, and integrative health conferences to stay current with the latest information in science and research. Laurel has been a national educator for Carlson Labs for the past 7 years. ; https://carlsonlabs.com/ ; sterling-headshot-dsc_9864
                       ; 51704180-2d86-4cac-b21e-519a5ce93f13 ; Alessandro Perra, Scientific Director of Guna Biotherapeutics ; Alessandro Perra is the scientific director of Guna Inc. He is a member of the international advisory committee for the “Scientific Proofs of the Efficacy of Homeopathy” project and the International Workshop on Physiological Regulating Medicine. Alessandro is a researcher in low-dose cytokine effects on cell and animal models and an international speaker and teacher of physiological regulating medicine and low-dose pharmacology. He is also the author of more than 100 scientific papers on homeopathy, homotoxicology, and physiological regulating medicine. ; https://gunainc.com/ ; alessandro_perra
                       ; cfa9edee-2cdd-4905-ae8c-9f70df8ec93f ; Christopher Shade, PhD                                        ; Christopher Shade, PhD, founder and CEO of Quicksilver Scientific, continues to be a driving force of development and innovation in Functional and Integrative Medicine. Dr. Shade founded the only clinical lab in the world offering mercury speciation analysis and has designed cutting-edge dietary supplements and protocols for detoxification, immune and foundational wellness, and longevity. He regularly speaks worldwide as an educator on mercury, environmental toxicities, neuroinflammation, immune dysregulation, and the human detoxification system. ; https://www.quicksilverscientific.com/ ; christopher_shade
                       ; 8abb211c-4939-410b-8ae8-efd3f0114d8c ; Devin Stone, ND                                               ; Dr. Devin Stone, ND, graduated from the University of California, Riverside with a degree in medical biology, a master's level education in regenerative medicine from The University Utrecht in The Netherlands as well as other certificates in fields such as nutrition, cancer biology, alternative medicine, drugless medicine, and more. Dr. Stone graduated with his medical degree focusing on naturopathic medicine from Bastyr University in Kenmore, WA, and now focuses on oncology and regenerative medicine. Dr. Stone serves as a medical advisor to Haelan Products, Inc. helping educate others on their flagship product, Haelan 951. ; https://haelan951.com/ ; devin_stone
                       ; aa39042f-0876-4488-871e-1c95fecc53db ; Michaël Friedman, ND                                          ; Michaël Friedman, ND, is a naturopathic physician and the founder of the Association for the Advancement of Restorative Medicine and the Journal of Restorative Medicine. He also formulates herbal and nutritional supplements for and is cofounder and president of the Restorative Formulations. He authored the book There’s No Pill for This: A Naturopathic Physician’s Personal Prescription for Managing Multiple Sclerosis and the medical textbook Fundamentals of Naturopathic Endocrinology and is a contributing author of Evidence-Based Approach to Restoring Thyroid Health and co-author of Healing Diabetes. ; https://www.restorativeformulations.com/ ; michael_friedman
                       ; ab80b818-7c33-405c-88de-d439bdbd448b ; Justine Stenger, IFM, FMCA                                    ; Justine Stenger, IFM, FMCA, is an Institute for Functional Medicine–certified and a Functional Medicine Coaching Academy–certified practitioner who completed her training at the Institute for Functional Medicine in Federal Way, WA. She has a bachelor’s degree in nutrition and physical education from the University of Alberta in Edmonton, Alberta, Canada, and has pursued a Holistic Nutrition/Therapeutic Chef certification from Bauman College in Emeryville, CA. Justine is also a trained Bredesen (RECODE) practitioner specializing in cell membrane medicine and works primarily with patients suffering from neurological conditions, mast cell activation syndrome, Lyme disease, and autoimmune disease. Justine has worked beside Dr. Bruce Hoffman for the past 10 years and has supported hundreds of Dr. Hoffman’s chronic, complex illness patients nutritionally. ; https://bodybio.com/ ; justine-stenger-ifm-fmca
                       ; 3ab95545-4046-4c08-9c00-31c9f15f63ea ; Lisa Ganora, BA                                               ; Lisa Ganora, BA, earned her bachelor’s degree in biology and chemistry from the University of North Carolina at Asheville and currently works as the chief formulator at Wellena. She founded the Colorado School of Clinical Herbalism and authored a popular textbook on phytochemistry, Herbal Constituents, 2nd Ed. Lisa has served as an adjunct professor and presented at global conferences. ; https://wellena.com/ ; lisa_ganora
                       ; a88141df-4401-4e99-82ba-6c5b529589b4 ; Shawn Wells, MPH, RD, CISSN, FISSN                            ; Shawn Wells, MPH, RD, CISSN, FISSN, is a nutritional biochemist, registered dietitian, certified sports nutritionist, and a Fellow of the International Society of Sports Nutrition. Shawn is a notable leader in the dietary supplement industry, formulating more than 1000 products and holding patents on more than 20 ingredients. His areas of expertise also encompass biohacking, anti-aging, and health optimization. Shawn has authored several publications, including his 2021 book, The Energy Formula: Six Life Changing Ingredients to Unleash Your Limitless Potential. Shawn has been featured in 4 globally recognized documentaries, has spoken on conference stages worldwide, and regularly contributes to popular podcasts and news segments. ; https://www.endur.com/ ; shawn_wells
                       ; dba90ff0-9908-4616-acf0-75e65f3f0fa7 ; Deanna Minich, MS, PhD, CNS, IFMCP                            ; Deanna Minich, MS, PhD, CNS, IFMCP, is a nutrition scientist, international lecturer, teacher, and author with over 20 years of experience in the food and dietary supplement industries. She is the chief science officer at Symphony Natural Health, where she leads the medical team, oversees scientific communications, and provides educational leadership for the company’s plant-derived natural products. Dr. Minich has been active as a functional medicine clinician in clinical trials and in her practice, Food & Spirit™, which has now become oriented toward groups, workshops, and retreats. She has authored 6 wellness-related consumer books, 4 book chapters, and 50 scientific publications. ; https://deannaminich.com/ ; deanna_minich
                       ; fba9495b-9723-4726-8649-09d9e4bfde37 ; Don Moxley                                                    ; Don Moxley is the director of applied science and brand development at Longevity Labs Inc. He draws from his experience as an athlete, a sports scientist, and an educator to lead and instruct on the science of autophagy and longevity. Focusing his work on the cell renewal benefits of spermidine supplementation, Don is a regarded longevity science leader known for making the complex simple. Through his interviews, speaking engagements, and presentations, Don makes the science of adding more life to our years immediately understandable. ; https://www.longevitylabs.io/ ; don_moxley
                       ; 2588a0ac-0a77-4ef9-b95a-2ad04b1cff69 ; Lisa Curtis                                                   ; Lisa Curtis is the founder and CEO of Kuli Kuli, the leading brand pioneering the sustainably sourced superfood moringa. Lisa began working with Kuli Kuli in the Peace Corps in Niger, West Africa, where she learned the nutritional challenges faced in villages and how moringa can help address them. Lisa has been recognized as a Forbes 30 Under 30 leader, Udall Scholar, and “dedicated humanitarian” by the Muhammad Ali Center. ; https://www.kulikulifoods.com/ ; lisa-curtis
                       ; d7a98abe-d03b-4968-b112-2591852877c3 ; Jed Fahey, ScD                                                ; Jed Fahey, ScD, is a nutritional biochemist with an extensive plant and human nutrition and phytochemistry background. Dr. Fahey taught at Johns Hopkins Medical School, where he directed the Cullman Chemoprotection Center, a leading center for studying and developing plant-based protective agents. He also spent 15 years in agricultural biotechnology research and industrial process development. Dr. Fahey consults with Kuli Kuli and other socially responsible companies and foundations. ; https://www.kulikulifoods.com/ ; jed-fahey
                       ; 0b1e0a7f-7976-46a8-8614-764224a37ba0 ; Kenn Israel                                                   ; Kenn Israel is the founder of Innovation Nutrition Consulting, a California-based boutique product development and innovation consultancy serving US and European dietary supplement, functional food, and nutraceutical ingredient firms. Kenn is also a co-founding partner at BeyondBrands, a New York-based business development agency that helps build and grow progressive, sustainable, plant-based, and mission-driven enterprises in the beverage, food, dietary supplement, cosmetic, and wellness categories. A member of the Natural Products Association, Kenn has served on the Committee for Product and Label Integrity for over 15 years. Kenn is the leading nutrition formulator for Zahler. ; https://zahlers.com/ ; kenn_israel
                       ; d14775a7-ab27-46c1-a4cd-12e4d314016b ; Yousef Elyaman, MD                                            ; Yousef Elyaman, MD, graduated from the University of Melbourne, Australia, and is a board-certified internist with a cross-specialization in pediatrics. He is also one of the first functional medicine–certified practitioners worldwide. As the founder and medical director of Absolute Health, he has successfully integrated an insurance-based functional medicine approach into his practice. Dr. Elyaman serves as the medical director of Humann, the integrative and functional medicine director of The Guest House, and a teaching faculty member at the Institute for Functional Medicine. ; https://humann.com/ ; yousef-elyaman
                       ; 7757fa5b-9b4e-4f3a-a612-37d982da03de ; Chris D. Meletis, ND                                          ; Chris D. Meletis, ND, is an educator, international author, and lecturer. His personal mission is changing the world’s health one person at a time, and he believes that when a person becomes educated about their body, this is the moment when change begins. Dr. Meletis has authored over a dozen books and more than 200 national scientific articles in journals and magazines, such as Natural Health, Alternative and Complementary Therapies, Townsend Letter, Life Extension, and Natural Pharmacy. He has written and lectured on the science and clinical utility of engaging the endogenous endocannabinoid system. ; ; chris-meletis
                       ; 21e67f57-9ead-4d2e-b5e5-ce6d9f3498cf ; Nick Bitz, ND                                                 ; Nick Bitz, ND, received his Doctor of Naturopathic Medicine from Bastyr University in Kenmore, WA. He specializes in Ayurvedic medicine and is a leading voice in the natural products industry. Dr. Bitz currently serves as the senior vice president of product development at the Neurohacker Collective. His areas of expertise include nootropics, anti-aging medicine, biohacking, herbology, nutrition, and dietary supplements. ; https://neurohacker.com/ ; nick-bitz
                       ; 1317feb9-9b4a-41ed-9fd3-68a059c0ad08 ; David Winston, RH (AHG)                                       ; David Winston, RH (AHG), is a registered herbalist, an ethnobotanist, and a founding/professional member of the American Herbalist Guild with 54 years of training in Chinese, Western/Eclectic, and Southeastern herbal traditions. He has been in clinical practice for 47 years and is an herbal consultant to physicians, herbalists, and researchers throughout the United States, Europe, and Canada. David is the founder/director of the Herbal Therapeutics Research Library and the dean of David Winston’s Center for Herbal Studies. He is also the president of Herbalist & Alchemist, Inc., an herbal product manufacturer that blends the art and science of the world’s great herbal traditions. David is a published author and an internationally known lecturer who frequently teaches at medical schools, professional symposia, and herb conferences. ; https://www.herbalist-alchemist.com/ ; david-winston
                       ; cf9312e5-896b-4bf9-b6aa-31f595a8bba8 ; Linda Matteoli, DO                                            ; Linda Matteoli, DO, has revolutionized the art of a membership-based practice. After growing her membership to a waitlist in nine months, providers began to ask her for help with their practices. To help meet this demand, she founded Origins Incubator, a nationally recognized practice management and implementation program. A graduate from Lake Erie College of Osteopathic Medicine, Dr. Matteoli is board-certified in family medicine and holds a master’s degree in nutrition. Her own health challenges, coupled with a lack of answers from conventional medicine, propelled Dr. Matteoli to seek out education at the Institute for Functional Medicine. She was determined to become the type of physician she would want to see. Dr. Matteoli is passionate about helping her colleagues find the same success she has in helping patients and growing a thriving practice. ; ; linda-matteoli
                       ; a1c92d00-bbe8-4563-8cbb-e58d39824a56 ; Scott Rattigan, JD                                            ; Scott Rattigan, JD, is a nationally recognized attorney, author, speaker, and business coach for functional medicine practitioners. He helps functional medicine doctors establish solid business and legal plans to protect themselves and grow their businesses so that they can practice with confidence and security to change the lives of their patients. Scott is the founder of Functional Lawyer and co-founder of Origins Incubator. ; ; scott-rattigan
                       ; ec2a5050-996d-4531-8564-94c82fe89006 ; Alan D. Snow, PhD                                             ; Alan D. Snow, PhD, received his doctorate in pathology from Queen’s University in Kingston, Ontario, Canada. He is the founder and CEO of Cognitive Clarity, Inc. and an expert in brain aging, memory loss, Alzheimer’s disease, Parkinson’s disease, and other misfolding-protein disorders. His knowledge and theories about brain plaque and tangle formation as key targets for memory loss have been at the forefront of brain-aging research for over 30 years. He is an inventor with over 350 patents on new drugs, nutraceuticals, and screening technologies, including Percepta® products. He has founded 2 different biotech/nutraceutical companies–the first developing small molecule drugs for Alzheimer’s/ Parkinson’s disease and misfolded protein disorders, and the second developing breakthrough nutraceuticals for the aging brain. ; https://perceptabrain.com/ ; alan_snow
                       ; eb992c1b-fb50-435e-ab7e-d834ba016b07 ; Stephanie Nishek, ND                                          ; Stephanie Nishek, ND, received her Doctor of Naturopathic Medicine degree from the Southwest College of Naturopathic Medicine & Health Sciences. She has spent 12 years in clinical practice, specializing in fertility, hormone balance, PCOS, endometriosis, and perimenopause. Her tenure has been dedicated to developing and implementing naturopathic root cause strategies to address various health and wellness concerns. Dr. Nishek uses evidence-based and traditionally rooted approaches, diagnostic and functional laboratory analysis, nutrition, botanicals, acupuncture, and mind–body strategies to support her patient population. Her passion for assisting those pursuing healthy conception and reproductive goals is fueled by a vested interest in building healthier communities with an “it takes a village” mentality. ; https://wisewomanherbals.com/ ; stephanie_nishek
                       ; c436ed42-920c-49bb-aa0d-6d6232a52a36 ; Julie Hawkes, CHC, CLC, CSNA                                  ; Julie Hawkes, CHC, CLC, CSNA, is Certified in Healthcare Compliance, a Certified Lactation Consultant, and a Certified Sports Nutrition Advisor. Julie has over 25 years in the natural health arena and is a team nutrition and product educator for Barlean’s, a national nutritional supplement company located in Ferndale, Washington. Julie also uses her extensive experience promoting health and wellness to help individuals achieve their personal goals as a Health and Life Coach. In addition to her work in natural health, Julie is a Certified Paralegal with a passion for child advocacy and has previously volunteered as a Child Advocate for Child Protective Services in Bellingham, Washington. ; www.barleans.com ; julie_hawkes
                       ; 2d9e3be0-f57c-43dd-84ef-7fd101996682 ; Matt Hand, DO                                                 ; Matt Hand, DO, received his Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine from the Chicago College of Osteopathic Medicine at Midwestern University. He is one of the industry’s most highly regarded pediatric nephrologists, specializing in pediatric integrative medicine at Children’s Hospital at Dartmouth (CHAD). He also partners with DaVinci® Laboratories, lending his expertise to the Little DaVinci® line of supplements for kids. National news programs have sought out his expertise, and he has previously been seen on Oprah and in season 2 of Emmy-nominated Tomorrow’s World Today. ; https://www.davincilabs.com/ ; matt_hand
                       ; fc9fe8d3-b4fc-4396-808f-c327d66e1a5f ; Kyl Smith, DC                                                 ; Kyl Smith, DC, is a pioneer in the world of natural medicine. After receiving his Doctor of Chiropractic in 1993, he has engaged in ongoing nutrition and natural medicine research, has become a multi-patented inventor, noted researcher, lecturer, and scientist, and is known as the inventor of “America’s #1 Brain Health Supplement.” Dr. Kyl is the author of the acclaimed Brighter Mind book series and a popular speaker who provides continuing education programs for doctors. Most notably, Dr. Kyl received the James Lind Scientific Achievement Award for his FDA-approved health claim petition filing for the brain-nutrient phosphatidylserine, representing the first and only nutrient-based qualified health claim approval for cognitive function in the FDA’s history. ; https://www.progressivelabs.com/bio_drkyl.php ; kyl_smith_dc
                       ; 6896d481-8cfd-4191-b0e2-6235e15e7ecc ; Amy Rawls, MS, RDN, LDN                                       ; Amy Rawls, MS, RDN, LDN, is a registered and licensed dietician nutritionist and a therapeutic lifestyle healthcare practitioner with certifications in integrative and functional medical nutritional therapy and gastrointestinal nutrition. She completed her master’s degree with a dietetic residency and has over 10 years of experience in applying functional nutrition practices to metabolic clinical states. As director of education and clinical services at Transformation Enzyme Corporation, Amy has consulted with and trained practitioners all over the world on enzyme therapy. She is an active clinician in Transformation’s research clinic and is responsible for the company’s webinar series training on enzyme protocols, including the Thrive in 63 wellness program based on an enzyme therapy and diet plan designed to restore gut health in 63 days. ; https://www.transformationenzymes.com/ ; amy_rawls
                       ; 2ecf7d93-2f1d-4234-8eb4-a4987236287d ; Christy Sutton, DC                                            ; Christy Sutton, DC, received her Doctorate of Chiropractor from Parker University in Dallas, TX. In her practice, Sutton Chiropractic and Nutrition – Applied Kinesiology, Dr. Sutton integrates kinesiology, nutrigenomics, functional medicine, applied neurology, and precision-based medicine to identify the root cause of conditions versus masking their symptoms. She also specializes in diagnosing hemochromatosis, or iron overload, using genetic and lab testing. She is a pioneer within the medical community regarding what she refers to as “the silent epidemic of high iron.” Dr. Sutton wrote Genetic Testing: Defining Your Path to a Personalized Health Plan and created the Genetic Detoxification report accompanying her book. In 2023, Dr. Sutton will expand on hemochromatosis through a webinar series and the book The Iron Curse. ; http://drsuttonchiropracticandnutrition.com/ ; dr-christy-sutton-dc-240x300
                       ; 1c59e7f9-6e8c-42c5-beec-66dabe381cbf ; Yael Joffe, PhD, RD, FACN                                     ; Yael Joffe, PhD, RD, FACN, is founder and CSO of 3X4 Genetics, a genetics-based foundational health company that provides comprehensive insights and wellness recommendations based on an individual’s genetic profile. Starting as a dietitian, she later obtained a PhD in nutrigenomics from the University of Cape Town, exploring the genetics of obesity. She was part of the team that built the first nutrigenomic genetic test in 2000 in the United Kingdom, three years before the final sequencing mapping of the human genome. Dr. Joffe teaches nutrigenomics at Rutgers University and Maryland University of Integrative Health, and she co-authored It’s Not Just Your Genes and Genes to Plate, a gene-based recipe book. ; ; yael-joffe
                       ; 72f91c7f-3fdc-40ee-b8eb-42ef56858b09 ; Kim Stevens                                                   ; Kim Stevens is the senior manager of sales operations and business partnerships for Intelligence of Nature, commonly called ION*. As the daughter of a chiropractor, Kim’s dedication to holistic and natural health has been her way of life from the start. Before her time at ION*, she studied herbalism, worked within the health food space, and spent time as an independent representative for another supplement line. She has been with ION* for more than 6 years serving in various roles from customer support to managing sales and education for their network of practitioners. Currently, she supports the company’s sales operations and key relationships. She is passionate about knowledge and the mission of ION* to reawaken connections through its products and science. ; https://intelligenceofnature.com/ ; kimstevens
                       ; 0ea4e61e-bcc5-40fc-8769-5c012807b3cf ; James Doherty                                                 ; James Doherty, general manager at Innate Response Formulas, brings 18 years of experience in the natural products industry to his webinars. Delving into the complex science of whole foods and whole-food supplements and translating it into practical applications for the practitioner, James examines the benefits of whole-food supplementation and reinvigorates the definition of whole foods as dynamic and evolving sets of interacting food constituents. James has presented the benefits of whole-food supplements at chiropractic and naturopathic conventions and universities. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; 16f199c5-5039-47f4-9d6b-71de752f9c9c ; Tom Malterre                                                  ; Tom Malterre, MS, CN, began his love affair with nutrition at age 10 when his family doctor taught his family how to heal with dietary recommendations alone. He has since attained two degrees in nutritional sciences from Bastyr University, worked for 7 years as a medical affairs member at Thorne Research, trained physicians across North America on functional medicine, and co-authored The Elimination Diet. Tom is the director of education at Seeking Health where he educates practitioners about the power of combining gene analysis with nutraceutical therapies to accomplish optimal clinical outcomes. ; ; tom-malterre
                       ; 49ede820-c9d2-4ecd-8c93-44b96f26474f ; Robb Wolf                                                     ; Robb Wolf is a former research biochemist, a two-time New York Times/Wall Street Journal best-selling author of The Paleo Solution and Wired to Eat, and co-founder of the electrolyte drink mix brand LMNT. Robb has transformed the lives of a considerable number of people around the world via his books, seminars, and a popular podcast. He has served as a review editor for the journal Nutrition & Metabolism (BioMed Central) and as a consultant for the Naval Special Warfare Resiliency program. Robb serves on the board of directors/advisors for SpecialtyHealth, Inc., The Chickasaw Nation’s Unconquered Life initiative, and several innovative start-ups that focus on health and sustainability. He has a purple belt in Brazilian jiu-jitsu and is a former California State Powerlifting Champion. Robb has presented seminars in nutrition, strength, and conditioning to NASA, Naval Special Warfare, the Canadian Light Infantry, and the U.S. Marine Corps. He lives in Texas with his wife and daughters. ; ; robb-wolf
                       ; 4ef5dbac-4db2-4f00-87b3-e9737ee98ed3 ; Joseph M. Raffaele, MD                                        ; Joseph M. Raffaele, MD, received his medical degree from Hahnemann University School of Medicine. He trained at New York Hospital-Cornell Medical Center and was a clinical assistant professor of medicine at Dartmouth Medical School while in practice at the Hitchcock Clinic. Board-certified in internal medicine, a member of the Endocrine Society, and a diplomate of the American Board of Anti-Aging Medicine, Dr. Raffaele co-founded PhysioAge Medical Group in 1997 and practiced age management medicine, focusing on personalized hormone optimization and physiological age assessment. In 2007, he co-founded PhysioAge Systems, a biomarker data collection and reporting system used by age management practices to assess, monitor, and communicate to patients the effectiveness of their treatments. Since 2009, Dr. Raffaele has been involved in clinical telomere biology research and has published three studies on the effect of oral telomerase activators on normal aging adults. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; cff2f519-c82b-4892-a40b-199060e09dbf ; Judith Smith, PharmD                                          ; Judith A. Smith, PharmD, is a professor and the director of the Women’s Health Integrative Medicine Research Program in the Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Sciences at UTHealth Houston McGovern Medical School. Board certified in oncology pharmacy, Dr. Smith is an oncology clinical pharmacy specialist at the UTHealth-Memorial Hermann Cancer Center and the Children’s Memorial Hermann Hospital. She received her Doctor of Pharmacy degree from Union University Albany College of Pharmacy and completed her residency in oncology pharmacy practice at the National Institutes of Health followed by a fellowship in clinical pharmacology at the University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center. Dr. Smith’s research mission is to advance the safe and effective use of nutritional and herbal supplements with pharmacologic modalities in the areas of women’s health, wellness, and cancer prevention. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; fa87ec35-2395-4a2e-b611-c163397e0310 ; Ayla Barmmer, MS, RD                                          ; Ayla Barmmer, MS, RD, is a registered dietitian who owns and operates Boston Functional Nutrition, an integrative and functional nutrition practice in Boston that specializes in women’s health and infertility. She founded FullWell, a fertility wellness brand, and she also founded the Women’s Health Nutrition Practice Group, where she serves as a teacher and mentor. Ayla co-founded the Women’s Health Nutrition Academy, which offers continuing education courses devoted to women’s health. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; a1db3739-0503-426d-b0d6-846044d1ad8a ; Jake Kocinski, RD                                             ; Jake Kocinski, RD, graduated from the University of Dayton with a bachelor’s degree in dietetics and is a registered dietitian. As the account manager for healthcare practitioners at Vital Proteins, Jake uses his background and core passion for nutrition, fitness, and wellness to educate people about the science-based benefits of collagen supplementation. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; df9468eb-3258-4dd0-957f-4d1c148b7be3 ; Mark J. Kaylor PhD, MH, CN                                    ; Mark J. Kaylor, PhD, MH, CN, is a master herbalist and certified nutritionist. For over 40 years, he has worked in many areas of the natural products industry, including retail, manufacturing, formulating, and private practice. Mark has studied a variety of traditional healing approaches, such as Eastern and Western herbalism, naturopathy, nutrition, shamanism, and more. He brings an eclectic perspective to the conversation with an emphasis on the importance of education and a truly holistic orientation. He recently started the Radiant Health Project, a not-for-profit organization that focuses on maximizing health and vitality rather than emphasizing symptomatic relief and disease. Mark currently consults with Mushroom Wisdom, Inc. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; 6b606cef-fb7b-40a7-a147-c4c13b61b7b5 ; Aumatma Shah, ND                                              ; Aumatma Shah, ND, a naturopathic doctor and nutritionist, has been in practice for over 15 years and specializes in women’s health. She is the author of Fertility Secrets: What Your Doctor Didn’t Tell You About Baby-Making and a sought-after speaker on topics related to women’s health and women’s empowerment. Dr. Shah was awarded the Best Alternative Medicine Practitioner award in the Bay Area in 2015 and 2020 and is regularly featured on TV and podcasts. She is the host of her own podcast Egg Meets Sperm and runs a training program for practitioners who want to specialize in fertility. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; 3e3161ac-9c93-4ad9-87b6-337fac1d406f ; Itamar Raz, MD                                                ; Itamar Raz, MD, one of the top diabetologists in the world, is the head of the Israel National Council of Diabetes, which is responsible for formulating national policies regarding diabetes, and founder and head of the National Diabetes Prevention and Care Plan in Israel. He received his medical degree from the Hebrew University Hadassah Medical School in Jerusalem and is board-certified in and a professor of internal medicine. He headed the diabetes unit at Hadassah University Hospital from 2000 to 2015. Professor Raz is president of D-Cure (diabetes care to cure), which promotes and funds scientific research in Israel for finding a cure and better treatments for diabetes. He serves in an editorial capacity for many journals and has over 320 publications in peer-reviewed journals. He is the medical advisory board chairman for CuraLife, a company that blends modernized ancient Ayurveda principles with modern-day science and technology. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; 63ac594d-4507-4917-9f43-4d9eaf8f67f7 ; Penny Kris-Etherton, PhD, RD                                  ; Penny Kris-Etherton, PhD, RD, is an Evan Pugh University professor of nutritional sciences at Penn State University and a fellow of the American Heart Association (AHA), the American Society for Nutrition, and the National Lipid Association. Her research focuses on understanding the effect of diet on cardiovascular disease (CVD) risk. Dr. Kris-Etherton served on the advisory committee for the 2005 Dietary Guidelines for Americans, on the macronutrients panel for the 2002 National Academies Dietary Reference Intakes, on the clinical expert panel for the American College of Cardiology Expert Consensus Decision Pathway on risk reduction for patients with atherosclerotic CVD, and as past chair of the AHA Lifestyle Council and the AHA Nutrition Committee. She has published over 440 papers and received numerous awards from many societies for her scholarly contributions. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; d9315525-11e2-46e4-9e70-d743f018e260 ; Allan Warshowsky, MD                                          ; Allan Warshowsky, MD, FACOG, ABIHM, is a board-certified OB/GYN and a graduate of SUNY Downstate Medical Center. He founded the Women’s Program at the Beth Israel Continuum Center for Health and Healing in New York City and served as a physician there for two years. In his successful private practice in Rye, NY, Dr. Warshowsky integrates nutritional therapy, bioidentical hormone therapy, and lifestyle changes. He is the author of Healing Fibroids: A Doctor’s Guide to a Natural Cure and a contributor to Integrative Medicine, 2nd edition. Dr. Warshowsky presented the 2011 XYMOGEN series Vanguard Endocrinology and continues to train physicians nationwide. He is a founding diplomate and director emeritus of the American Board of Integrative Holistic Medicine and a fellow of the American College of Obstetrics and Gynecology. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; 3de92961-2ccd-4883-8c45-2c1bf8b61f5e ; Jeffrey S. Bland, PHD, FACN, FACB, CN                         ; Jeffrey S. Bland, PHD, FACN, FACB, CN, is known worldwide as the founder of the functional medicine movement, an evolving care model that is grounded in systems biology and informed by research to address the underlying causes of disease. His pioneering work has led to creating the Personalized Lifestyle Medicine Institute and co-founding the Institute for Functional Medicine, the global leader in functional medicine education. Among his many other accomplishments, Dr. Bland has written several books about nutritional medicine and is the principal author of over 120 peer-reviewed research publications. Dr. Bland serves on the Vital Proteins Medical Advisory Board. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; ce91b804-90e4-4ac2-b93a-23da1eebf272 ; Robert Scott Bell                                             ; Robert Scott Bell received a diploma in clinical homeopathy from the American Academy of Clinical Homeopathy in 1994. He is a homeopathic practitioner, an author, and a member of the medical advisory board for Argentyn 23®, a practitioner brand of silver therapeutics. As a keynote speaker, lecturer, and radio show host, he shares his holistic experience with a broad range of audiences from wellness professionals and industry colleagues to consumers. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; d6abc4e5-0cfc-4bc7-a945-9308b8ef1640 ; Carly Stein, Founder and CEO of Beekeeper’s Naturals          ; Carly Stein, Founder and CEO of Beekeeper’s Naturals, has a mission to improve the health of humans, bees, and the planet, which is why she left her job on the trading floor at Goldman Sachs to launch Beekeeper’s Naturals in 2016. Beekeeper’s Naturals utilizes natural remedies from the beehive to craft science-driven wellness solutions. As a beekeeper and advocate for the preservation of the waning global bee population, Carly is dedicated to using her company as a platform to raise awareness for the bee cause. Carly was recognized as a game-changing entrepreneur on the 2019 Forbes 30 Under 30 list. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; 17040002-5680-4356-8d1c-bf25169ff2ef ; Philip Rouchotas, MSc, ND                                     ; Philip Rouchotas, MSc, ND, practices at the Bolton Naturopathic Clinic in Bolton, Ontario. His areas of clinical focus include metabolic syndrome, autoimmune conditions, mental health concerns, and autism. He is also an associate professor at the Canadian College of Naturopathic Medicine (CCNM) and is responsible for the assimilation and delivery of the second-year curriculum in clinical nutrition. He graduated from CCNM in 2004, preceded by an honours undergraduate degree and a Master of Science degree in nutritional sciences from the University of Guelph. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; 1847bb71-dc65-46c4-bccf-b17787aa1912 ; Dominique Ostrander                                           ; Dominique Ostrander has worked for Jarrow Formulas since 2006 and is currently a territory manager and educator. She completed a bachelor’s degree in writing and holds graduate degrees in exercise science and pharmacology rehabilitation with a specialty in cardiac rehabilitation. For over 25 years, Dominique has worked with moderately to morbidly obese patients. She has a particular interest in combining traditional allopathic medicine with proper supplementation. Dominique was one of the original Step Reebok national instructors and led thousands of instructors to become nationally certified to teach Step Reebok classes in the United States. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; da4fe670-8950-47a8-8435-f1bee00fc690 ; Martin Milner, ND                                             ; Martin Milner, ND, is the CEO, founder, and medical director of the Center for Natural Medicine (CNM) in Portland, OR. This integrated healthcare facility has been designated a Tier 4 Patient-Centered Primary Care Home, a top-level recognition of clinical excellence bestowed by the State of Oregon. Dr. Milner completed his degree in naturopathic medicine at the National University of Natural Medicine (NUNM) and continued at NUNM for 31 years as a professor of cardiovascular and pulmonary medicine training medical students in the classroom while training interns and residents in primary and cardiopulmonary care at CNM. Dr. Milner’s interest in hormones has also led him to contribute guest lectures to the NUNM endocrinology curriculum on thyroid, adrenal, and male and female health. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; 661575fb-7ce1-4216-a83a-c95fc2307e9a ; Nirala Jacobi, ND                                             ; Nirala Jacobi, ND, naturopathic doctor and internationally recognized expert on small intestinal bacterial overgrowth (SIBO), created the SIBO Bi-Phasic Diet, a resource that has helped thousands of SIBO sufferers around the world. She is the host of The SIBO Doctor Podcast and founder of The SIBO Doctor, an online educational platform that includes a practitioner certification program. Dr. Jacobi is also the medical director of SIBOtest, an Australian company that provides innovative SIBO and IBS (irritable bowel syndrome) testing options. Dr. Jacobi received her naturopathic degree from Bastyr University and brings more than two decades of clinical experience to the Biome Clinic, a practice she founded in the Northern Rivers region of New South Wales, Australia, that specializes in systematically and effectively diagnosing and treating SIBO and other functional digestive disorders. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; d4ad9563-f016-411f-8e87-8fc7aceafec9 ; Michael Nelson, DC                                            ; Michael Nelson, DC, a national board-certified chiropractor, has dedicated his nearly four-decade career to helping others improve their lives. After earning an undergraduate degree in respiratory science and a doctor of chiropractic degree at the University of Western States, Dr. Nelson started his medical career as a neonatal respiratory therapist in a level 3 nursery and developed a passion for holistic medicine. He has completed over 1,500 hours of post-graduate training through the Institute for Functional Medicine, the American Academy of Anti-Aging Medicine, and the Integrative Medicine for Mental Health. Dr. Nelson founded the Sierra Tahoe Wellness Center in Reno, NV, is the CEO of Sierra Nevada Bioscience LLC, and is at the helm of two nutraceutical companies, Brain Bean and Life Enhancement. A sought-after speaker, Dr. Nelson has presented at the Cancer Control Society, the American Osteopathic Society of Rheumatic Diseases, and the Integrative Health Alliance. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; bd43aa90-eb51-47fb-aa73-4fe0e15ac1e6 ; Todd A. Born, ND, CNS                                         ; Todd A. Born, ND, CNS, is a naturopathic physician, certified nutrition specialist, and co-owner and medical director of Born Integrative Medicine Specialists, PLLC. In addition, Dr. Born is the director of product development and the scientific advisor for Allergy Research Group and a medical wellness advisor for the International Medical Wellness Association. After graduating from Bastyr University in Seattle, WA, he completed his residency at the Bastyr Center for Natural Health with rotations in the emergency departments of EvergreenHealth and Harborview medical centers as well as in Virginia Mason Hospital’s Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Spine Clinic. Dr. Born’s clinical focus is utilizing integrative medicine to treat family members of all ages who have complex chronic diseases combined with a strong interest in difficult and refractory cases of any condition and age. ; ; todd-born
                       ; 6bee80ff-990a-4b5a-a312-7950fd0a000f ; Jill Carnahan, MD, ABIHM, ABOIM                               ; Jill Carnahan, MD, ABIHM, ABOIM, is dually board-certified in family medicine and integrative holistic medicine. She uses functional medicine to help patients find the root cause of their illness and identify nutritional and biochemical imbalances that may be contributing to their symptoms. Dr. Carnahan completed her residency at the University of Illinois Family Medical Residency in Peoria, IL, and received her medical degree from Loyola University Stritch School of Medicine in Chicago. Over a 12-year period, Dr. Carnahan faced and recovered from aggressive breast cancer and achieved clinical remission following a Crohn’s disease diagnosis. These are a testament to her belief that the human body is capable of enduring treatment and regaining health. In her practice at Flatirons Functional Medicine, Dr. Carnahan is passionate about teaching patients how to live well and thrive in the midst of complex and chronic illness. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic
                       ; af2261d6-4822-4d75-bce3-baf25a2be9fc ; Sarah Morgan, Founder & CEO of Even                           ; Sarah Morgan, MS, CEO of Even, has an extensive background in nutritional science and a master’s degree in clinical nutrition. For over 13 years, she ran a clinical practice in Denver, CO, where she consulted with a wide variety of patients. Even was born from Sarah’s observations that medication compliance was directly related to side effects and M.I.N.D. (medication-induced nutrient depletions). Even products have been formulated to meet the unique nutritional needs of individuals taking common prescription medications, enabling them to feel good while receiving the benefits of their medications. ; ; sarah-morgan
                       ; c8f9abd7-e6f5-4fb9-9945-9e3dbc6c8c8e ; Jocelyn Strand, ND                                            ; Jocelyn Strand, ND, completed her doctorate in naturopathic medicine at Bastyr University in 2005. After her graduation, Dr. Strand established a practice in Seattle and worked at Pharmaca Integrative Pharmacy as well as in a gastrointestinal specialty clinic. She returned to her home state of Minnesota with a vision of increasing the availability, affordability, and awareness of naturopathic medicine. She opened Lake Superior Natural Medicine, a private practice in which she specialized in GI system disorders, Lyme disease, and autoimmune conditions as a primary care provider through the Minnesota Board of Medical Practice. In 2019, Dr. Strand became the director of clinical education at Bio-Botanical Research, Inc., where she is thrilled to participate in research and lecture around the world. ; www.biocidin.com ; jocelyn_strand
                       ; 1e09d66f-4b45-408a-ae6a-17cba309b59a ; Blake Ebersole, BS, MBA                                       ; Blake Ebersole, BS, MBA, is the founder and president of NaturPro Scientific LLC, an independent consulting firm that provides expertise in the development of dietary supplements. Blake’s background includes experience as a technical advisor in the research, production, and quality assurance of key ingredients sold in established turmeric products in the U.S. and globally. He supports product development and advises on regulatory compliance and quality assurance efforts for numerous firms subject to the most stringent global quality requirements. Blake also contributes to several technical committees, serves on expert panels, and is a member of multiple industry organizations, including the American Herbal Product Association, ASTM International, AOAC International, and the U.S. Hemp Roundtable. ; http://naturproscientific.com/ ; blake_ebersole_-68x68
                       ; 970c92be-1c64-437a-adcb-79e9c40c8c2f ; Matthew Anthony Stanizzi, MD                                  ; Matthew A. Stanizzi, MD, graduated from Brandeis University with a Bachelor of Science in neuroscience and biology. He received his medical degree from Mount Sinai School of Medicine in 2003, then he completed his internship in surgery and his residency in urology at Mount Sinai Hospital. Dr. Stanizzi has over 12 years of clinical experience as a board-certified urologist with expertise in robotic surgery and hormone replacement. He served at Southern New Hampshire Medical Center as the department chair for surgery for many years and is the hospital’s laser safety officer. Dr. Stanizzi is currently the medical director of BioRestore Health and operates and practices in BioRestore’s New Hampshire location. ; https://biorestorehealth.com/ ; matthew-anthony-stanizzi
                       ; e6693e9a-5611-42f7-a515-b9ba15397739 ; Magdalena Wszelaki, CH, HHC                                   ; Magdalena Wszelaki, CH, HHC, is a certified herbalist, certified health coach, and the founder of Wellena, a clean supplement line designed to naturally restore women’s hormonal balance. She’s the author of Cooking for Hormone Balance and Overcoming Estrogen Dominance. Magdalena is also an entrepreneur, endocrine nutrition expert, and chef. ; https://wellena.com/ ; magdalena_wszelaki
                       ; 622b703f-beff-401b-9fbd-cc5310e16461 ; Daniel Clark, BS                                              ; Daniel Clark, BS, earned his Bachelor of Science degree with a specialization in kinesiology from Laurentian University in Sudbury, Ontario, in 2018. Daniel’s undergraduate research projects prompted him to submit for publication his research on the effect of exogenous ketone salts and whole-body cooling on exercise metabolism and performance, which appeared in the July 2021 issue of Frontiers in Nutrition. While pursuing his naturopathic medicine degree at the Southwest College of Naturopathic Medicine (SCNM), Daniel has been responsible for co-founding a large project investigating the activity of propolis against antibiotic-resistant bacteria. ; ; webinar-presenter-thumbnail-generic

