INSERT_UPDATE Webinar; code[unique = true]                  ; title[lang = en]                                                                                                                                                                        ; shortDescription[lang = en]                                                                                                                                                                                                             ; description[lang = en]; duration(code); isFeatured; videoImage(code, $contentCV); video(code, $contentCV); videoStatus(code); sponsorImageUrl; sponsorImage(code, $contentCV); sponsorImageAltText; sponsorName; presenter(code); webinarCategoryTag(code); webinarVideoUrl; webinarCaptionsUrl; category(code, $catalogVersion)
                     ; bbec5cdd-a075-4381-9c03-4d65b858f64f ; Enhanced Immune Support: Synergistic Approaches to Optimize Defense                                                                                                                     ; In this post-pandemic era, immune challenges have become a year-round concern for most people. Join Dr. James Munro as he navigates how to integrate a nutrition plan to synergistically support the immune function of your patients.  ; <p>Post-pandemic, we live in a time where immune challenges are a year-round concern, and it is in our and our patient’s best interests to do everything possible to optimize our defenses. Wisely integrating a nutritional plan that synergistically supports immune function is paramount to protecting our patients from seasonal, stress-related, and environmental insults that may impact their health.</p><br><p>In this informative webinar, naturopathic physician James Munro will give an overview of the multiple mechanisms for which nutrients work to support immune function. Highlights will include:</p><br> <ul><li>Key nutrients that are essential to immune function and how to optimize their synergy</li><li>Nutrition for a healthy oral and gut microbiome and its influence on immune health</li><li>Understanding and applying supplement protocols to enhance immune response</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; enhanced-immune-support-munro ; munro-cutout-1 ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 8b7d9ab5-ea5e-43ff-95da-83873fc45899 ; 100 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Enhanced Immune Support__MunroWebinarShare0924.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/XYMOGEN_Spotlight_-_Infectious_Diseases_Webinar_Series,_Part_IV_(XYMOGEN)_080820.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13
                     ; a6910870-3024-4d06-a2af-8eb9dca87680 ; XYMOGEN Spotlight, Infectious Disease Webinar Series Part 4: Clinical Efficacy of High-Dose Dapsone Combination Therapy for Chronic Lyme Disease and Coinfections, including Bartonella ; Treating chronic diseases in people with compromised immunity can pose unique challenges. Dr. Richard Horowitz examines the underlying treatment principles of providing optimal care to patients with acute illness and Lyme disease.  ; <p>From individuals with Lyme disease to people with histamine intolerance and cardiometabolic conditions, those with underlying health conditions are at an increased risk for acquiring acute infections. Infectious disease rates are on the rise and are influenced by varying factors. With an ever-widening range of symptoms, it is often difficult for clinicians to pinpoint a diagnosis and design a treatment plan. In this must-see, 5-part webinar series, attendees will learn about the latest approaches from top experts who will share their clinical successes and cutting-edge strategies for addressing infections in those with underlying conditions.</p> <p><b>Part 2: Clinical Efficacy of High-Dose Dapsone Combination Therapy for Chronic Lyme Disease and Coinfections, including Bartonella</b><br> Understanding the nuances between chronic diseases like Lyme disease and acute illness is critical to providing responsive care that incorporates the whole, unique individual—a hallmark of integrative medical practice. In Part 4 of this 5-part webinar series, Dr. Horowitz examines common pathophysiologic links and applies similarly adapted treatment principles to help participants gain an understanding of how to best support unique circumstances of compromised immunity in patients with Lyme disease.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; webinar-thumbnail-generic-white ; munro-cutout-1 ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 36066998-d75e-4e22-83bd-53a416b5e22f ; 115, 104 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/XYMOGEN Spotlight - Infectious Diseases Webinar Series, Part IV (XYMOGEN) 08082024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/XYMOGEN_Spotlight_-_Infectious_Diseases_Webinar_Series,_Part_III_(XYMOGEN)_08012.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; ed27cd73-9341-471c-a7aa-afc9e0abb471 ; XYMOGEN Spotlight, Infectious Disease Webinar Series Part 3: Women and Lyme: The Intricate Relationship Between Hormones, Lyme Disease, and Other Tick-Borne Infections                 ; Female hormones can complicate the treatment and ongoing management of Lyme disease in women. Jaquel Patterson, ND, uncovers the gender disparity in the treatment and diagnosis of tick-borne infections in female patients.           ; <p>From individuals with Lyme disease to people with histamine intolerance and cardiometabolic conditions, those with underlying health conditions are at an increased risk for acquiring acute infections. Infectious disease rates are on the rise and are influenced by varying factors. With an ever-widening range of symptoms, it is often difficult for clinicians to pinpoint a diagnosis and design a treatment plan. In this must-see, 5-part webinar series, attendees will learn about the latest approaches from top experts who will share their clinical successes and cutting-edge strategies for addressing infections in those with underlying conditions.</p> <p><b>Part 2: Women and Lyme: The Intricate Relationship Between Hormones, Lyme Disease, and Other Tick-Borne Infections</b><br> Tick-borne infections affect all people and come with a vast range of symptoms, making diagnosis and treatment challenging. For women, in particular, the intricate relationship with female hormones adds another layer of difficulty in ongoing care management. In Part 3 of this 5-part webinar series, Jaquel Patterson, ND, shares her wealth of knowledge about the gender disparity surrounding the diagnosis and treatment of Lyme disease in women.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; webinar-thumbnail-generic-white ; munro-cutout-1 ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 02c47856-112f-4567-9d21-942c48d63b83,36066998-d75e-4e22-83bd-53a416b5e22f ; 100,101,102,105,108,109,113,119,115 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/XYMOGEN Spotlight - Infectious Diseases Webinar Series, Part III (XYMOGEN) 08012024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/XYMOGEN_Spotlight_-_Infectious_Diseases_Webinar_Series,_Part_II_(XYMOGEN)_072520.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; eff27139-13f7-4fba-87b5-a7423c04a951 ; Microbiome Determinants of Shape and Body Composition                                                                                                                                   ; Rates of overweight and obese individuals in the US have risen to epidemic levels, leaving clinicians searching for solutions. Tune in to explore body composition determinants and long-term weight management strategies.             ; <p>The prevalence of overweight and obese individuals in the US has accelerated rates of cardiovascular and metabolic issues to epidemic proportions. Yet, conventional approaches to weight loss, such as restricted calorie diets, medications, and surgical procedures that limit calorie intake, typically result in lean muscle mass loss, negatively impacting overall health and the success of long-term weight management. A shift from reducing caloric intake to means that could preserve body composition may be a key component for successful long-term weight management.</p><br> <p>Join renowned cardiologist and bestselling author William Davis, MD, for an insightful webinar exploring the determinants of body composition. Dr. Davis will give an overview of recent research, suggesting how losing weight while preserving lean muscle is possible, thereby promoting healthy body composition and sustainable weight management.</p><br><p>Highlights of this presentation will include:</p><br> <ul><li> How conventional weight management solutions impair health</li><li> The preferential targeting of visceral fat to preserve muscle</li><li> The role of Lactobacillus reuteri in the modification of body composition</li><li> Collagen, hyaluronic acid, and carotenoids as determinants of body composition\</li><li> Clinical insights discerned from pilot research and future pursuits exploring the restoration of factors that may positively impact body composition</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; william ; william-cutout ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; b5e27efe-449c-42f9-b81e-bdb03652783a ; 103 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Microbiome Determinants of Shape and Body Composition (XYMOGEN) 01162025.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Gut_Feelings_-_Healing_the_Microbiome-Mind_Connection_(XYMOGEN)_11212022.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_24, Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_25,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_29,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_22,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26,
                     ; 8514f8c6-f192-4580-887c-148dc6347c31 ; XYMOGEN Spotlight Part 1: The Polymicrobial Nature of Long Haulers and Reactivation of Coinfections                                                                                     ; The symptomology of Lyme disease can overlap with other long-term, acute illnesses, such as COVID-19, Babesiosis, and Epstein-Barr. Tune in to discover diagnostic tools and treatment options for these elusive pathogens.             ; <p>From individuals with Lyme disease to people with histamine intolerance and cardiometabolic conditions, those with underlying health conditions are at an increased risk for acquiring acute infections. Infectious disease rates are on the rise and are influenced by varying factors. With an ever-widening range of symptoms, it is often difficult for clinicians to pinpoint a diagnosis and design a treatment plan. In this must-see, 5-part webinar series, attendees will learn about the latest approaches from top experts who will share their clinical successes and cutting-edge strategies for addressing infections in those with underlying conditions.</p> <p><b>Part 1: The Polymicrobial Nature of Long Haulers and Reactivation of Coinfections</b><br> Persistent symptoms of Lyme disease, including fatigue, brain fog, and pain, are remarkably like those of long-haul COVID-19, and questions about the cause of these overlapping symptoms are also similar. Another parallel is that latent illnesses, such as Babesiosis and Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) in the case of Lyme disease, can become reactivated with acute illness. Jerry Simons, PA, kicks off Part 1 of this 5-part webinar series with a discussion of the diagnostic tools and treatments used to address challenges posed by the coexistence of these elusive pathogens.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; webinar-thumbnail-generic-white ; jerry_simons ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; a740df2b-a3d2-4727-aa18-91fff4a31c25 ; 100,102,105,108,109,113,115,117,118,119,121 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/XYMOGEN Spotlight - Infectious Diseases Webinar Series, Part I (XYMOGEN) 07182024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Spotlight_on_XYMOGEN_Series_-_Part_V_(XYMOGEN)_06272024.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; 3b569b96-c3c5-42df-b7f0-17ede4a8cb9a ; XYMOGEN Spotlight Part 2: Applying a Cardiometabolic Lens to Infectious Cardiac Conditions                                                                                              ; Certain infections can severely impact cardiovascular health. Dr. Druz discusses how these infections can aggravate cardiac conditions and what preventive measures can be taken to optimize cardiovascular well-being.                 ; <p>From individuals with Lyme disease to people with histamine intolerance and cardiometabolic conditions, those with underlying health conditions are at an increased risk for acquiring acute infections. Infectious disease rates are on the rise and are influenced by varying factors. With an ever-widening range of symptoms, it is often difficult for clinicians to pinpoint a diagnosis and design a treatment plan. In this must-see, 5-part webinar series, attendees will learn about the latest approaches from top experts who will share their clinical successes and cutting-edge strategies for addressing infections in those with underlying conditions.</p> <p><b>Part 2: The Polymicrobial Nature of Long Haulers and Reactivation of Coinfections</b><br> Understanding the link between cardiometabolic health and infections can prevent cardiovascular complications. In Part 2 of this 5-part webinar series, Regina Druz, MD, explores genetic, lifestyle, and proactive factors that influence heart health, how certain infections can exacerbate cardiac conditions, and how adopting preventive measures can help maintain cardiovascular well-being.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; webinar-thumbnail-generic-white ; reginadruz ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/a0rp0vca/holisticheartcenters.png ; ; Sponsor logo image for Holistic Heart Centers ; Holistic Heart Centers ; 5622754d-67b5-43af-b3b0-910d50847c2a ; 101,102,103,105,108,111,112,119 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/XYMOGEN Spotlight - Infectious Diseases Webinar Series, Part II (XYMOGEN) 07252024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/XYMOGEN_Spotlight_-_Infectious_Diseases_Webinar_Series,_Part_I_(XYMOGEN)_0718202.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_01,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_16,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_24,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; b72994c2-5e0c-4f41-8082-3f2b7b3cc7ac ; Spotlight on XYMOGEN: Gut–Skin Connection: New Strategies for Dermatology                                                                                                               ; Both the skin and gut microbiome play integral roles in dermatological health. Learn nutritional strategies to help eliminate various types of dermatitis and provide hormone and adrenal support without the typical side effects.     ; <p>Join Dr. Cheryl Burdette, naturopathic physician and XYMOGEN’s director of education, for informative sessions highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will discuss scientific insights into dietary ingredients and review the clinical applications for various formulas across different health categories. Attendees will also learn how to best use individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results. Tune in for these informative clinical training sessions featuring best-selling and new XYMOGEN formulas.</p><br> <p>Session 5: Gut–Skin Connection: New Strategies for Dermatology Dermatological issues, such as eczema, psoriasis, rosacea, and acne, can be difficult to treat without allopathic interventions that carry multiple side effects. These conditions can be largely gut-based, meaning the gut microbiome is a primary interventional target for natural solutions. As with the gut, the skin microbiome must also be addressed. In the final webinar of this 4-session series, Dr. Burdette will take a fresh look at these conditions and the functional strategies that address the gut and skin microbiomes. The role of vasculitis in reddening and increased inflammation will also be discussed with an emphasis on specific phytonutrients that help reduce inflammatory−cell migration in the skin. A thorough evaluation of other nutritional strategies to eliminate dermatitis of various types, including hormone and adrenal support, will also be explored. Discover a new paradigm in treating dermatological issues that delivers better patient outcomes without the side effects.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; webinar-thumbnail-generic-white ; cheryl_burdette ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 100,102,104,105,108,110,111,112,113,100,115,116,117,118,119 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Spotlight on XYMOGEN Series - Part V (XYMOGEN) 06272024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Beyond_Digestion_-_Unlocking_the_Hidden_Potential_of_Enzymes_for_Systemic_Applic.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_24,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26,
                     ; 5fcf09f6-cbc5-428b-b13d-e2ec44cf86d6 ; Beyond Digestion: Unlocking the Hidden Potential of Enzymes for Systemic Applications                                                                                                   ; Proteolytic enzymes have been used as an adjunct therapy in traditional medicine for years. Tune in to learn how to maximize the benefits of enzyme therapy and potential clinical applications for various long-term conditions.       ; <p>Proteases are widely known for their role in protein digestion. But unbeknownst to some, proteolytic enzymes also work throughout the body providing protection from environmental toxins, stress, inflammation, and chronic disease. Proteolytic enzymes have been used therapeutically for centuries, and the evidence base for their modern use as an adjunct therapy for various conditions continues to grow.</p> <p>Join Doctor of Chiropractic Medicine Milton Bastidas to explore the probable mechanism of action and potential clinical applications for systemic enzyme therapy. Highlights will include:</p><br> <ul><li>Protease biology and prospective mechanism of action</li><li>The historic use of proteolytic enzymes</li><li>The impact of proteolytic enzymes on various conditions</li><li>An update on systemic enzyme clinical research</li><li>A sneak peek at the results of a recent prostate health case study</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; webinar-thumbnail-generic-white ; milton_bastidas ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/dthnxzmu/transformation-logo.png ; transformation-logo ; Sponsor logo image for TransFormation ; TransFormation ; 6ff089f5-8193-4321-a405-2f38d70a26cc ; 100,103,105,109,110,112,113,115,116,119 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Beyond Digestion - Unlocking the Hidden Potential of Enzymes for Systemic Applications (Transformation Enzymes) 06072024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Spotlight_on_XYMOGEN_Series_-_Part_IV_(XYMOGEN)_05162024.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_07,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_10,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19
                     ; f21ef1d3-2c13-45b4-b501-2bf09e3902d6 ; Spotlight on XYMOGEN: Mastering Sleep, Winding Down, and Turning Off                                                                                                                    ; Restorative sleep is necessary for the brain and body to operate optimally however, insomnia plagues 30% of the US population. Tune in to examine the root causes of insomnia and learn ways to help promote healthy sleep hygiene.     ; <p>Join Dr. Cheryl Burdette, naturopathic physician and XYMOGEN’s director of education, for informative sessions highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will discuss scientific insights into dietary ingredients and review the clinical applications for various formulas across different health categories. Attendees will also learn how to best use individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results. Tune in for these informative clinical training sessions featuring best-selling and new XYMOGEN formulas.</p><br> <p>Session 4: Mastering Sleep, Winding Down, and Turning Off</p><br> <p>Insomnia affects people of all ages and plagues 30% of the US population, eroding cognitive and physical well-being. Its far-reaching consequences can present as poor focus, weakened immune function, and weight gain. It can even contribute to arterial plaques. Sleep is needed for brain tissue detoxification, memory consolidation, and synaptic plasticity, and the body produces melatonin to support sleep and antioxidant protection. When sleep declines, so does melatonin production, increasing health risks—even cancer. In part 2 of this 4-part series, Dr. Burdette will examine the causes of insomnia, including hormonal imbalances, inflammation, stress responses, and poor neurotransmitter production. Emphasis will be given to establishing circadian rhythms associated with better sleep−wake functions and good sleep hygiene. By looking at the root causes, practitioners can select more directed and individualized interventions to help patients get restorative sleep.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; webinar-thumbnail-generic-white ; cheryl_burdette ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 102,115 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Spotlight on XYMOGEN Series - Part IV (XYMOGEN) 05162024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/What’s_in_Your_Mushroom_Supplement_(Mushroom_Wisdom)_04122022_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_24,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; e4e4267e-cff3-40f6-b345-f6747d7df2ee ; Mold Exposure and the Continuum of Care                                                                                                                                                 ; As mold-related illnesses become more prevalent, your patients can be at risk of living in potentially unsafe environments. Tune in to learn about physiological challenges and possible solutions to help patients impacted by mold.   ; <p>The existence of widespread systemic illness attributable to mold has historically been denied the standard of care. In recent years, there has been an uptick in the awareness of illness caused by mold, but treatments still remain elusive, with recommendations falling just short of moving into a new home and getting rid of potentially contaminated belongings. If the environment in which our patients live becomes potentially unsafe for their health, what else can be done?</p><br> <p>Join naturopathic physician Cheryl Burdette on an information-filled journey to help participants identify physiological challenges and manage solutions for patients affected by mold exposure. Highlights will include:</p><br> <ul><li> Mold toxicity, prevalence, and health consequences</li><li> Calming and restoring an overactive immune response to molds</li><li> Detoxification and protection of cellular health in the face of mold toxicity</li><li> Managing hormones that may be impaired by mold</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; cheryl_burdette2 ; cheryl_burdette ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 102,115 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Mold Exposure and the Continuum of Care (XYMOGEN) 10172024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Enhanced_Immune_Support__MunroWebinarShare0924.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_16,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19
                     ; abc3740e-4193-413a-8f66-c06ceaf8e102 ; Gut Feelings: Healing the Microbiome–Mind Connection                                                                                                                                    ; Comprehending the connection between physical and emotional health is paramount to the foundation of health and wellness. Join Will Cole, DC, to examine where the body and mind meet and how imbalances in one can impact the other.   ; <p>Understanding the link between physical and emotional health is critical to providing the framework that supports overall health and wellness. Experiencing shame, trauma, and emotional stress can weaken that framework and profoundly influence the gut microbiome, inducing the imbalances that are known to be the root cause of many systemic health conditions.</p><br> <p>Join functional medicine expert Dr. Will Cole for a rich exploration of the interventional nuances that can help to heal the microbiome–mind connection and support a healthy relationship between food and your patient for robust clinical outcomes along their wellness path. Key discussion points will include:</p><br> <ul><li> How stress, trauma, and shame may sabotage health through “Shameflammation”</li><li> Gut problems that present as mood swings, anxiety, and food cravings</li><li> Functional medicine protocols and somatic practices for gut–brain healing</li><li> Tips for building a healthy relationship between food and the body</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; gut-feelings-healing-the-microbiome-mind-connection_cole ; will_cole ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 91a3754c-d5ff-48f1-88f0-801e4eba3657 ; 104, 102 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Gut Feelings - Healing the Microbiome-Mind Connection (XYMOGEN) 11212022.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Mold_Exposure_and_the_Continuum_of_Care_(XYMOGEN)_10172024.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_01,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_29,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; ae9e1252-7edf-4c65-84cc-5890c6b78e50 ; Heart-Centered Care: A Functional Medicine Approach                                                                                                                                     ; Cardiovascular diseases are the worldwide leading cause of death, yet the current standard of care appears inadequate. Join Dr. Cheryl Burdette as she shares a multifaceted functional medicine approach to cardiovascular care.       ; <p>Cardiovascular diseases (CVDs) are the leading cause of death worldwide. In recent years, rates of CVD have remained steady despite the advent of improved interventions that lower risk factors, like elevated blood pressure and cholesterol. It is clear that reliance on a one-size-fits-all approach to cardiovascular care is inadequate and that a shift from standard treatment options may be warranted.</p><br> <p>In this engaging presentation, Dr. Cheryl Burdette will merge evidence-based research with extensive clinical experience to provide unique perspectives and practical strategies that support heart-centered patient care. Attendees will gain an understanding of the necessity for a multi-faceted functional medicine approach to cardiovascular care, with emphasis on:</p> <ul><li> The impact of lifestyle interventions on CVD risk factors</li><li> The critical connection between gut health and cardiometabolic health</li><li> Dietary and supplemental recommendations that influence markers associated with cardiovascular health</li><li> Enhancing heart-centered care with an epigenetic approach based on optimizing systems of the body</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; cheryl_burdette2 ; cheryl_burdette ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 115,104 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Heart-Centered Care - A Functional Medicine Approach (XYMOGEN) 02062025.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Microbiome_Determinants_of_Shape_and_Body_Composition_(XYMOGEN)_01162025.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19

                     ; c005ed87-af4a-4499-9e1b-b10652c5c301 ; Optimizing Patient Gut–Brain Responses                                                                                                                                                  ; The gut─brain axis can impact all aspects of mental, emotional, and physical health. Tune in to discover the crucial role this bidirectional communication system plays in the body and interventions to best support patient health.   ; <p>The gut–brain axis is a bidirectional communication system that influences mental, emotional, and physical health. Its crucial role in overall well-being makes it an essential focus for holistic healthcare professionals. Understanding this axis and optimizing its function can lead to groundbreaking discoveries for patient health maintenance.</p><br> <p>Don’t miss this important and unique gut–brain discussion, which will include research on a novel prebiotic–probiotic–postbiotic blend and end with an interactive Q&A session.</p><br> <p>The focus of this presentation will be on:</p> <ul><li>The impact of the gut–brain axis on various areas of health</li><li>How prebiotics, postbiotics, and digestive enzymes impact the gut–brain axis</li><li>Using FODMAP-friendly fibers, resistant starches, and psychobiotics</li><li>Suggestions for assessing gut–brain responses to interventions</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; optimizing-patient-gut-brain-responses ; optimizing-patient-gut-brain-responses ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/dfupthdy/brand-logo-neurohacker.png ; brand-logo-neurohacker ; Sponsor logo image for NeuroHacker ; NeuroHacker ; 8cd4190d-dc84-435d-aa6f-88ad239be9df ; 111,112,115 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Optimizing Patient Gut–Brain Responses (Neurohacker Collective) 05092024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Optimizing_Nitric_Oxide-Related_Clinical_Outcomes_(HumanN)_08222023.vtt" ;
                     ; da67beb7-e799-49b1-8620-a09cbd547590 ; Mayhem and Misconceptions in the Upper GI Tract                                                                                                                                         ; Gut dysbiosis is often only attributed to lower GI issues, but the upper GI tract plays a significant role. Tune in to learn how upper GI dysfunction contributes to downstream problems and practical clinical tools for treatment.    ; <p>Dysfunction in the upper GI (gastrointestinal) tract can frequently contribute to problems downstream, yet many functional medicine GI protocols focus on lower GI tract treatment. Beginning with the mouth, then onto the esophagus, the stomach, and finally the duodenum, the upper GI has the critical role of initiating the digestive process and preparing food for the lower GI to further process and facilitate nutrient absorption. Upper GI malfunctions can manifest in symptoms like difficulty swallowing, excessive burping, acid reflux, and gastritis—all contributors to gut dysbiosis.</p><br><p>Join functional medicine expert Tracy Harrison for this perspective-shifting discussion of how upstream GI issues can be a root cause of GI dysbiosis and practical clinical guidance for treatment. Highlights include:</p><br> <ul><li>Common missteps regarding Helicobacter pylori eradication</li><li>Expanding the gut boundary and how those unexpected cavities are implicated in dysbiosis</li><li>Hypochlorhydria prevalence and contribution to GI dysfunction</li><li>Root cause resolution for acid reflux relief</li><li>Systemic conditions with upper GI root causes</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; mayhem-and-misconceptions-in-the-upper-gi-tract ; mayhem-and-misconceptions-in-the-upper-gi-tract ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/b0m…nd-logo-school-of-applied-functional-medicine.png ; brand-logo-school-of-applied-functional-medicine ; Sponsor logo image for the school of applied functional medicine ; the school of applied functional medicine ; 4d7259d8-ca86-4d0b-a93c-9f592541f227 ; 113,100,115 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Mayhem and Misconceptions in the Upper GI Tract (The School of Applied Functional Medicine) 05012024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Managing_Mood_Disorders_(Allergy_Research_Group)_09162021_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19
                     ; 147c0021-b530-418a-bd86-065e0bf9b792 ; Exploring the Promise of Red Light Therapy                                                                                                                                              ; It has long been believed that different wavelengths of light have healing properties. Join Dr. Alyson Evans as she explores the potential clinical applications of red light therapy and discusses its potential healing benefits.     ; <p>The concept that light can heal is not new. More than 100 years ago, a Danish physician was awarded the Nobel Prize in Physiology for treating a cutaneous form of tuberculosis with light therapy. Flash forward to the present, where red light therapy (RLT, aka photobiomodulation) is evolving in the scientific community as a practice with the potential to be used in a wide range of conditions.</p><br> <p>Join Doctor of Chiropractic Medicine Alyson Evans for an exploration into the plausible mechanism of action and potential clinical applications for RLT. Topics covered will include:</p><br> <ul><li> What is RLT, and how does it work in the body?</li><li>Evidence-based indications for RLT use</li><li>Optimal treatment parameters for a safe and effective RLT dosage</li><li>The key differences between LED and laser RLT</li><li>Safety precautions</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; exploring-the-promise-of-red-light-therapy-evans ; exploring-the-promise-of-red-light-therapy-evans ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/u2xm2nos/fringe.png ; ; Sponsor logo image for Fringe ; Fringe ; 692cad63-c2bd-487d-9254-4ee35284cc01 ; 112,117,118,125 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Exploring the Promise of Red Light Therapy (Fringe) 04252024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Evaluating_Non-Pharmacological_Approaches_to_Children’s_Health_(DaVinci_Laborato (1).vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_20,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_29
                     ; 47ba5450-840c-4cf4-8ebf-5b6f915b3b18 ; Spotlight on XYMOGEN: Natural Support for Endothelial Health                                                                                                                            ; A decrease in endothelial function impacts the body’s ability to make nitric oxide (NO) and can lead to elevated blood pressure and plaque formation. Discover natural remedies that can help support NO production.                    ; <p>Join Dr. Cheryl Burdette, naturopathic physician and XYMOGEN’s director of education, for 3 informative sessions highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will discuss scientific insights into dietary ingredients and review the clinical applications for various formulas across different health categories. Attendees will also learn how to best use individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results. Tune in for these informative clinical training sessions featuring best-selling and new XYMOGEN formulas.</p><br> <p>Session 3: Natural Support for Endothelial Health</p><br> <p>Impaired endothelial function affects both the ability to make nitric oxide (NO), resulting in elevated blood pressure, and an increase in adherence of white blood cells and platelets, leading to plaque formation. Symptomatic-based medicine is typically focused on lowering plaque formation and blood pressure: complementary therapies can be added to support tissue health. In Part 3 of this 3-part webinar series, Dr. Burdette will review the evidence-based potential of vitamin K, diosmin, and bergamot, amla, olive, and grapeseed extracts in supporting endothelial function.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; natural-support-for-endothelial-health ; natural-support-for-endothelial-health ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 102,104,105,108,117,118,119 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Spotlight on XYMOGEN Series - Part III (XYMOGEN) 03282024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Spotlight_on_XYMOGEN_Series_-_Part_II_(XYMOGEN)_02082024.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_16,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; 089b9b6b-0d0f-4113-a690-8b67ba95b645 ; Live Stronger, Longer                                                                                                                                                                   ; Sarcopenia has long been considered a by-product of aging. Join Laurel Sterling, MA, RDN, CDN, for a discussion on how sarcopenia starts at a younger age and how to help your patients slow the natural progression of muscle loss.    ; <p>Sarcopenia is typically known as an age-related loss of muscle mass, but researchers are discovering that it starts younger than people realize. Vanity aside, muscle loss means greater weakness and less mobility with advancing age, which increases fall and fracture risk. More and more people want to stay active, energized, and vibrant far into their golden years, and healthcare practitioners can help them do that.</p><br> <p>Join Laurel Sterling, MA, RDN, CDN, for a comprehensive exploration of specific dietary interventions that slow the natural progression of lean body mass loss and support healthy body composition at every age. Highlights include a look at current paradigms for healthy aging. Don’t miss this opportunity to gain valuable and actionable insights and protocols to help patients live stronger, longer.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; live-longer-stronger ; live-longer-stronger ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/odhfdnlp/brand-logo-carlson-labs.png ; brand-logo-carlson-labs ; Sponsor image for Carlson Labs ; Carlson Labs ; 63caae5f-cb97-43a3-83b5-faffc84eb8b0 ; 105,126,104,100,111,112,110 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Live Stronger, Longer (Carlson Labs) 04052024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Laboratory_&_Genetic_Testing_of_Iron_Overload,_Hemochromatosis,_and_Anemia_of_In.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_10,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; 82bd5ff2-2187-417a-a0a8-201c379eb76c ; The “Allergic Puzzle” in Modern Times                                                                                                                                                   ; As food allergies become a prominent topic in modern health discussions, understanding how and why the immune system targets certain substances is imperative. Tune in to learn how the body navigates these allergic responses.        ; <p>Embark on a journey through the mysterious landscape of food allergies, an increasingly prevalent concern in modern health discussions. Gain a deeper understanding of what happens when the immune system’s protective mechanisms misidentify benign substances as threats, why allergies are on the rise, and where and how practitioners can intervene.</p><br> <p>Join Alessandro Perra, Scientific Director of Guna Biotherapeutics, as he delves into the underlying mechanisms that orchestrate allergic responses, highlighting the complex interplay of cells within the immune system. Special focus will be given to:</p><br> <ul><li>How allergies resemble a dynamic puzzle with continuously shifting pieces</li><li>TH1 and TH2 balance and the switch that occurs in allergy</li><li>Solutions for acting on the atopic condition from exposure to symptomatology</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; the-allergic-puzzle-in-modern-times ; the-allergic-puzzle-in-modern-times ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/5cjfixjv/guna-logo.png ; guna-logo ; Sponsor logo image for Guna Biotherapeutics ; Guna Biotherapeutics ; 51704180-2d86-4cac-b21e-519a5ce93f13 ; 100,121,109,126 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/The “Allergic Puzzle” in Modern Times (Guna Biotherapeutics) 03212024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/The_Acclaim_of_Soy_as_a_Superfood_(Haelan_Products,_Inc.)_01182024.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15
                     ; b92835a3-5fe2-476d-acc9-91a7b44a23b2 ; Disease Begins in the Gut, But Often Doesn’t Stay There                                                                                                                                 ; Gut imbalances may be the root cause of many systemic health conditions. Tune in as functional medicine expert Tracy Harrison explores the inner workings of the gut and how dysbiosis can impact your patient's health and wellness.   ; <p>Hippocrates was onto something when he was quoted as saying: “All disease begins in the gut.” Imbalances in the gut are linked to the root cause of many systemic health issues, and if not originated in the gut, many disorders are exacerbated there through a host of varying mechanisms.</p><br> <p>Join functional medicine expert Tracy Harrison for a rich exploration of the often-overlooked connections and interventional nuances that can help facilitate dramatically improved clinical outcomes in your patients. Topics will include:</p><br> <ul><li>Two-sided pancreatic insufficiency</li><li>The gut–brain axis and neuroinflammation</li><li>Multifactorial consequences of cholecystectomy</li><li>Common medications and potential downstream dysfunction</li><li>Mucosal degradation and systemic inflammation</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; disease-begins-in-the-gut_-but-often-doesn-t-stay-there ; disease-begins-in-the-gut_-but-often-doesn-t-stay-there ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/b0m…nd-logo-school-of-applied-functional-medicine.png ; brand-logo-school-of-applied-functional-medicine ; Sponsor logo image for The School of Applied functional Medicine ; The School of Applied functional Medicine ; 4d7259d8-ca86-4d0b-a93c-9f592541f227 ; 115, 108,113,100,121,109,117,118,102,111 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Disease Begins in the Gut, But Often Doesn’t Stay There (The School of Applied Functional Medicine) 03202024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Dihydroberberine_-_Pharmacology_and_Therapeutic_Benefits_(Endurance_Products_Com.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_25,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; a3cc81dd-4028-4cf1-a9c8-37cc76dc476d ; Cellular Senescence and the Anti-Aging Power of Senolytics                                                                                                                              ; The accumulation of senescent cells is linked to many age-related health concerns. This webinar will showcase how senolytics can induce apoptosis of senescent cells, leading to improved overall health and wellness.                  ; <p>Senescent cells no longer replicate or function, yet they do not go through apoptosis. Their accumulation impacts the aging and function of healthy cells in their microenvironment and is linked to many health concerns. What can be done to promote their removal? Enter senolytics—small molecules that selectively induce apoptosis of senescent cells and can improve cellular health.</p><br> <p>Don’t miss naturopathic physicians Nick Bitz and Gergory Kelly as they provide a revealing look at cellular senescence, its connection to age-related health concerns, such as brain and joint health, and how to counter senescent cell accumulation. Topics will include:</p><br> <ul><li>Theories of aging and why senescent cells accumulate</li><li>Diet and lifestyle factors for senescent cell management</li><li>How to use senolytic compounds effectively, including fisetin, quercetin, piperlongumine, and validated ingredient blends</li><li>Research on a novel senolytic blend</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; cellular-senescence-and-the-anti-aging-power-of-senolytics ; cellular-senescence-and-the-anti-aging-power-of-senolytics ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/dfupthdy/brand-logo-neurohacker.png ; brand-logo-neurohacker ; sponsor logo image for Neurohacker Collective ; Neurohacker Collective ; 8cd4190d-dc84-435d-aa6f-88ad239be9df,21e67f57-9ead-4d2e-b5e5-ce6d9f3498cf ; 112,111,125 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Cellular Senescence and the Anti-Aging Power of Senolytics (Neurohacker Collective) 02162024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Cell-to-Cell_Chatter_-_Communication_and_Its_Role_in_Human_Health_(ION)_10272022.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_20,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; 2db3e6f0-15f7-4fec-83e3-f04f72fc55c9 ; Spotlight on XYMOGEN: Brain Health: Sulforaphane and Myrosinase and Cognitive Function                                                                                                  ; Studies show oxidative stress in the brain can negatively impact overall cognitive health. Tune in as Dr. Burdette discusses how sulforaphane and myrosinase can help support brain health and promote optimal cognition.               ; <p>Join Dr. Cheryl Burdette, naturopathic physician and XYMOGEN’s director of education, for 3 informative sessions highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will discuss scientific insights into dietary ingredients and review the clinical applications for various formulas across different health categories. Attendees will also learn how to best use individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results. Tune in for these informative clinical training sessions featuring best-selling and new XYMOGEN formulas.</p><br> <p><b>Session 2: Brain Health: Sulforaphane and Myrosinase and Cognitive Function</b><br> Studies have demonstrated a connection between oxidative stress in the brain and a decrease in cognitive function and mental stability. While it is understood that neurotransmitters are critical to thought processes, focus, and concentration, it is equally important that they have a healthy environment to function optimally. In Part 2 of this 3-part webinar series, Dr. Burdette will discuss the unique ability of sulforaphane to cross the blood–brain barrier and increase Nrf2 transcription factors, which are directly implicated in brain health. A focal point of this lecture will be the synergy between sulforaphane and myrosinase, an enzyme that greatly enhances sulforaphane absorption for improved clinical outcomes.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; brain-health-sulforaphane-and-myrosinase-and-cognitive-function ; brain-health-sulforaphane-and-myrosinase-and-cognitive-function ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 102,101,105,116,108,109,112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Spotlight on XYMOGEN Series - Part II (XYMOGEN) 02082024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Spermidine_-_A_Key_Component_to_Cellular_Longevity_(Longevity_Labs)_10262023.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_01,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; ce6af67b-2c07-47c0-95b5-b6113d512ac6 ; Bioidentical Hormones: Empowering the Menopause Transition                                                                                                                              ; The menopause transition can negatively impact sleep, energy, confidence, and the overall wellness of your patients. Tune in for a discussion on how to best support your patients in navigating this natural hormone decline.          ; <p>Is the menopause transition robbing your patients of sleep, energy, confidence, and control of their health? This natural hormone decline is estimated to affect 1.1 billion women globally by 2025, with some women spending up to 10 years struggling with hormone imbalance symptoms. Adding hormone replenishment to an already healthy lifestyle can help fuel a more comfortable menopausal journey.</p><br> <p>In this webinar, Christopher Shade, PhD, will dive into the complexity of female hormones, considering important factors to help women take control of their health and navigate the menopausal transition.</p><br> <p>Highlights of the discussion will include:</p><br> <ul><li> Female steroidal hormones 101</li><li>Common signs and symptoms accompanying female hormone patterns</li><li>Addressing the fear and myths surrounding hormone therapy</li><li>Bioidentical hormone replacement</li><li>Clinical insights from a pilot study using liposomal DHEA to convert steroidal hormones</li><li>Preview of a literacy course designed to provide practitioners with the tools and expertise to support women through the menopausal transition</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; bioidentical-hormones-empowering-the-menopause-transition ; bioidentical-hormones-empowering-the-menopause-transition ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/l4kdfpvl/brand-logo-quicksilver.png ; brand-logo-quicksilver ; Sponsor logo image for Quicksilver Scientific ; Quicksilver Scientific ; cfa9edee-2cdd-4905-ae8c-9f70df8ec93f ; 117,112,103,104,116 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Bioidentical Hormones - Empowering the Menopause Transition  (Quicksilver Scientific) 02012024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver_12-Part_Series_-_The_Multifaceted_Biological_Role_of_Enzym.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_07,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_22
                     ; 3c79648f-636d-4508-89e4-49eadb0b78c7 ; Spotlight on XYMOGEN: Unraveling Trauma and PTSD: Natural Adjuncts of Support                                                                                                           ; Emotional trauma and stress can severely impact overall health and wellness. Join Dr. Burdette to unravel the mysteries behind natural remedies that may help release stored stress and increase resilience in your patients.           ; <p>Join Dr. Cheryl Burdette, naturopathic physician and XYMOGEN’s director of education, for 3 informative sessions highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will discuss scientific insights into dietary ingredients and review the clinical applications for various formulas across different health categories. Attendees will also learn how to best use individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results. Tune in for these informative clinical training sessions featuring best-selling and new XYMOGEN formulas.</p><br> <p><b>Session 1: Unraveling Trauma and PTSD: Natural Adjuncts of Support</b><br> The understanding of how emotional trauma impacts healing has moved significantly forward in recent years. Complementing primary interventions, such as counseling and meditation, with dietary supplements and lifestyle interventions is now understood to play a role in the emotional change necessary for physical change. In Part 1 of this 3-part webinar series, Dr. Burdette will give an overview of vagal nerve pathophysiology and adrenal health and discuss natural remedies to support the body in releasing stored stress and increasing resilience.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; unraveling-trauma-and-ptsd-natural-adjuncts-of-support ; unraveling-trauma-and-ptsd-natural-adjuncts-of-support ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 127,112,113,125 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Spotlight on XYMOGEN Series - Part I (XYMOGEN) 01252024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Spotlight_on_XYMOGEN_Series_-_Part_III_(XYMOGEN)_03282024.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_31,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_29,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; 4e1e6100-d193-4f18-a96e-038e12bfcb6c ; Unraveling the Link: Tick-Borne Infections and Mental Health                                                                                                                            ; There is a link between tick-borne infections and mental health. This webinar delves into the nuances between these infections, neuroinflammation, and psychiatric conditions and how to create personal care plans for your patients.  ; <p>Tick-borne infections can present with a vast range of symptoms, making diagnosis and treatment challenging. The dynamic interplay between tick-borne infections, neuroinflammation, and psychiatric conditions adds layers of difficulty to ongoing care management. Understanding these nuances is critical for providing an individualized care plan that can empower individuals in their quest for better mental health.</p><br> <p>In this enlightening webinar, Jaquel Patterson, ND, will examine the complex pathophysiologic links between tick-borne infections and the initiation or exacerbation of psychiatric conditions. Participants will glean valuable insights for merging integrative and conventional care into a personalized strategic treatment plan. Highlights include:</p><br> <ul><li>Systemic health complications from tick-borne infections</li><li>The impact of neuroinflammation on specific brain regions</li><li>Pathophysiology of neurotransmitter dysregulation</li><li>Diet, lifestyle, and supplements for patient support</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; jaquel_patterson ; jaquel_patterson ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 02c47856-112f-4567-9d21-942c48d63b83 ; 112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Unraveling the Link - Tick-Borne Infections and Mental Health (XYMOGEN) 03272025.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Heart-Centered_Care_-_A_Functional_Medicine_Approach_(XYMOGEN)_02062025.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_29,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; 11125dd3-8744-44e0-b3e1-148ea137b536 ; The Acclaim of Soy as a Superfood                                                                                                                                                       ; For centuries, soybeans have been used as a superfood to benefit and support overall health and wellness. Join Dr. Devin Stone in uncovering how GMO-altered soy can change health benefits and which products remain false superfoods. ; <p>Soybeans and foods derived from them have been part of the human diet for centuries and, in modern times, have been billed as superfoods. Even though there is no legal definition for a superfood, foods that boast exceptional nutritional attributes commonly claim superfood status. The designation of soy as a superfood could be credited to the powerful compounds it contains that have been extensively studied for their beneficial effects on health, which include support for immune function, hormone balancing, and healthy inflammatory response.</p><br> <p>In this informative webinar, naturopathic doctor Devin Stone will deep dive into important factors to consider when selecting soy products worthy of superfood status and how these factors might alter soy’s therapeutic benefits.</p><br> <p>Highlights of the discussion include:</p><br> <ul><li>Historical use of soy</li><li>Genetic modification and alteration in health benefits of soy</li><li>Impact of growing conditions and fermentation on the quality and efficacy of soy products</li><li>How to discern different therapeutic benefits among soy products</li><li>Clinical applications for soy superfoods</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; the-acclaim-of-soy-as-a-superfood ; the-acclaim-of-soy-as-a-superfood ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/kuvn3bnu/haelan-logo.png ; haelan-logo ; Sponsor logo image for Haelan 951 ; Haelan 951 ; 8abb211c-4939-410b-8ae8-efd3f0114d8c ; 102,116,108,100,119 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/The Acclaim of Soy as a Superfood (Haelan Products, Inc.) 01182024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/The_Acclaim_of_Soy_as_a_Superfood_(Haelan_Products,_Inc.)_01182024.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_07,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_08,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13
                     ; 1d2125c9-b7ac-42a1-b7b3-d80fa926e39d ; Managing Blood Pressure and Cardiac Rhythm With Herbal Medicine                                                                                                                         ; Hypertension is a common condition that impacts nearly half of US adults and can lead to heart disease and stroke. Listen in as Dr. Michaël Friedman discusses herbal remedies to help manage hypertension more naturally.              ; <p>Hypertension is a common problem seen in clinical practice: in fact, nearly half of US adults suffer from this condition. Having hypertension puts patients at risk for heart disease and stroke—the leading causes of death. Hypertension is typically managed with life-long drug therapy, but with proper training, it can potentially be managed naturally.</p><br> <p>Join Dr. Michaël Friedman for this important examination of natural, efficacious hypertension interventions that will surely raise clinician confidence. Attendees will leave with a deepened knowledge of and practical strategies associated with:</p><br> <ul><li>Evidence-based botanicals for supporting individuals with hypertension, hypotension, tachycardia, and arrhythmia</li><li>Major physiological pathways wherein herbs can impact vascular tension</li><li>Using herbs adjunctively with pharmaceutical hypotensives</li><li>Stepwise implementation of alternatives to allopathic interventions</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; managing-blood-pressure-and-cardiac-rhythm-with-herbal-medicine ; managing-blood-pressure-and-cardiac-rhythm-with-herbal-medicine ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/fwibvxv5/restorativeformulations-logo.png ; restorativeformulations-logo ; Sponsor logo image for Restorative Formulations ; Restorative Formulations ; aa39042f-0876-4488-871e-1c95fecc53db ; 105 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Managing Blood Pressure and Cardiac Rhythm With Herbal Medicine (Restorative Formulations) 01112024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Live_Stronger,_Longer_(Carlson_Labs)_04052024.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06
                     ; 7f05b54a-b9e1-47eb-a18d-1ac318239c5c ; Navigating Mold Toxicity and Revolutionizing Recovery                                                                                                                                   ; Mold toxicity can have a detrimental impact on physiological health and overall wellness. Listen in to discover how Lipid Replacement Therapy could be a potential solution to restoring cellular health and improving symptoms.        ; <p>Explore the hidden threats of mold toxicity and innovative recovery strategies in this insightful webinar. The deep and pervasive impacts of mold on physiological health and the subtle yet potent ways mold toxicity can compromise cellular function and overall wellness will be illuminated. The webinar will pivot from challenges to solutions, introducing Lipid Replacement Therapy as a promising approach to restore cellular health and ameliorate symptoms.</p><br> <p>Join Justine Stenger, BodyBio clinical educator, on a transformative journey from identifying challenges posed by mold toxicity to acquiring viable solutions. Participants will gain an in-depth understanding of:</p><br> <ul><li>Mold toxicity, prevalence, and health consequences</li><li>BodyBio’s intricate approach to mold toxicity</li><li>The role of cellular health in managing mold toxicity</li><li>Advanced lipid formulations designed to fortify cell membranes and enhance detoxification pathways</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; navigating-mold-toxicity-and-revolutionizing-recovery ; navigating-mold-toxicity-and-revolutionizing-recovery ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/u45ipddo/bodybio-logo.png ; bodybio-logo ; Sponsor logo image for Bodybio ; Bodybio ; ab80b818-7c33-405c-88de-d439bdbd448b ; 116,109,100,121,112,105,103,115,119,102 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Navigating Mold Toxicity and Revolutionizing Recovery (BodyBio) 01042024.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Natural_Therapies_and_Male_Hormones_-_The_Untapped_Potential_(XYMOGEN)_05192022_.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_07,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18
                     ; bac18df5-744a-4be7-a44f-c759cee21dba ; Nitric Oxide and the Gut Lining—A Novel Gut Based Strategy                                                                                                                              ; Nitric oxide (NO) is significant in supporting overall gastrointestinal health. Join Dr. Burdette for the final part of this 6-session series to examine natural alternatives to promote NO production to benefit gut health.           ; <p>Focusing on the gut barrier is recognized as one of the primary functional medicine tools to address a healthy inflammatory response and stabilize gastrointestinal (GI) health. Dietary and nutritional support that influences the gut microbiome is a critical component of a gut-based strategy. Additionally, nitric oxide (NO) is considered significant for maintaining the integrity of the gastric epithelium and the mucus barrier because of its vasodilatory role in mediating gastric blood flow. In the final webinar of this 6-session series, Dr. Burdette will look at natural alternatives to promote NO production in the gut and its effect on the gut lining.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; nitric-oxide-and-the-gut-lining-a-novel-gut-based-strategy ; nitric-oxide-and-the-gut-lining-a-novel-gut-based-strategy ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 102,101,105,115,118,112,127,111 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Nourishing Fertility - An Expert’s Secrets Revealed (Restorative Formulations) 04072022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver,_How_XYMOGEN_Sharpens_Your_Aim_-_Part_II_(XYMOGEN)_1221202.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_01,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_16,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; f72d8437-5412-4e04-a5c7-b18818e1fa21 ; Causes and Solutions for Noncancerous Breast Conditions                                                                                                                                 ; Not all breast pain or masses automatically point to cancer. Join Magdalena Wszelaki and Lisa Ganora to better understand breast-related conditions and the natural solutions that can help support individualized care.                ; <p>Noncancerous yet painful breast conditions prompt many people to seek the help of healthcare practitioners. Fibrocystic breasts, benign cysts, and cyclical and noncyclical breast pain and swelling each affect patients differently and call for individualized care, wherein natural solutions can play a significant role.</p><br> <p>Join Magdalena Wszelaki and Lisa Ganora for this insightful presentation exploring the etiology of noncancerous breast conditions, including hormonal changes, inflammation, and lymphatic stagnation. Leave equipped with a deeper understanding of the biology and physiology involved, traditional uses of natural ingredients, and modern research that can assist healthcare practitioners in helping patients afflicted with these conditions.</p><br> <p>Practitioners will receive practical information and protocols, including:</p><br> <ul><li>Topical herbs and oils combined with oral supplements to support breast health</li><li>Key herbs as possible breast pain relief options</li><li>Lymphatic breast massage technique</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; causes-and-solutions-for-noncancerous-breast-conditions ; causes-and-solutions-for-noncancerous-breast-conditions ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/iqlbl4ml/brand-logo-wellena.png ; brand-logo-wellena ; Sponsor logo image for Wellena ; Wellena ; 3ab95545-4046-4c08-9c00-31c9f15f63ea,e6693e9a-5611-42f7-a515-b9ba15397739 ; 121,117 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Causes and Solutions for Noncancerous Breast Conditions (Wellena) 11202023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Enzymes_-_Catalysts_for_Transforming_Wellness_(Transformation_Enzyme)_12152022_1 (1).vtt" ;
                     ; 2d07f43b-5284-4114-a57b-6c72d45aa658 ; Dihydroberberine: Pharmacology and Therapeutic Benefits                                                                                                                                 ; Do your patients experience GI upset from taking berberine? Tune in as nutritional biochemist Shawn Wells discusses the potential benefits of dihydroberberine, from pharmacology to anti-aging to potential clinical applications.     ; <p>Berberine is well-established in the literature as a plant alkaloid with glycemic control benefits. However, a lesser-known fact is that berberine is not well absorbed by the body and may cause gastrointestinal upset. A metabolite of berberine known as dihydroberberine (DHB) has greater bioavailability, is gentler on the stomach, and has equally, or perhaps even more, beneficial effects than the standard berberine alkaloid.</p><br> <p>In this informative webinar, renowned nutritional biochemist Shawn Wells will deep dive into the pharmacology, anti-aging benefits, and potential clinical applications of DHB.</p><br> <p>Highlights of the discussion will include:</p><br> <ul><li>The significant differences between DHB and standard berberine</li><li>The mechanism of DHB in anti-aging via reducing glycation end-products</li><li>The potential role of DHB in supporting healthy weight management</li><li>Clinical protocols and dosing recommendations for optimal clinical outcomes</li></ul> <p>Don’t miss this opportunity to learn more about this fascinating compound from one of the foremost industry experts on DHB.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; dihydroberberine-pharmacology-and-therapeutic-benefits-wells ; dihydroberberine-pharmacology-and-therapeutic-benefits-wells ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/gypp2o4f/enduranceproducts-logo.png ; enduranceproducts-logo ; Sponsor logo image for Endurance Products ; Endurance Products ; a88141df-4401-4e99-82ba-6c5b529589b4 ; 102,119,103,105,116,108,100,126,112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Dihydroberberine - Pharmacology and Therapeutic Benefits (Endurance Products Company) 11162023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Dietary_Nitrates,_Nitric_Oxide,_and_Heart_Health_(HumanN)_03222022_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_07,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_08,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18
                     ; 4b1c747b-aa41-45fb-8fe7-7ad7dfd04ccb ; Phytoestrogens and Phytoprogestins, What Do We Know?                                                                                                                                    ; Hormone imbalances are at the root cause of many health issues. Tune in as Dr. Burdette reviews the history of botanical use, with a focus on phytoestrogens and phytoprogestins as part of hormone management treatment plan.          ; <p>Research continues to support the efficacy and safety of phytoestrogens—those with estrogenic activity—for use in hormonal management. Although less prominent in the research, phytoprogestins—those with progestogenic effects—also have a valuable place in hormonal treatment plans. In Session 5 of this 6-session webinar series, Dr. Burdette will discuss the eclectic history of botanicals used to manage hormonal imbalances and suggest current applications for their use as part of a comprehensive hormonal management and treatment plan.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; phytoestrogens-and-phytoprogestins ; phytoestrogens-and-phytoprogestins ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 117,118,112,105,101 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver, How XYMOGEN Sharpens Your Aim - Part II (XYMOGEN) 11092023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver, How XYMOGEN Sharpens Your Aim - Part II (XYMOGEN) 11092023.mp4" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_01,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_30,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_16,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18
                     ; 1513b879-f033-4777-ad84-6b362a6ccc8b ; Melatonin: Beyond Sleep                                                                                                                                                                 ; Can melatonin be used for more than just a sleep aid? Tune into this educational webinar and discover the mechanisms of melatonin and why this dietary supplement is gaining popularity.                                                ; <p>Melatonin, primarily recognized as a chronobiotic and sleep aid, has emerged as a highly sought-after dietary supplement with a growing list of health applications. Melatonin acts as a hormone with widespread, systemic effects, and its popularity is reflected by a doubling of supplement sales since 2017. However, the trend toward greater use of melatonin raises concerns about its safety, including application in particular populations (eg, children), high doses, and long-term use.</p><br> <p>In this webinar, Dr. Minich will discuss topics covered in her published paper “Is Melatonin the ‘Next Vitamin D’?: A Review of Emerging Science, Clinical Uses, Safety, and Dietary Supplements.” Special attention will be given to:</p><br> <ul><li>Melatonin’s expanding roles as a potent antioxidant, immunomodulatory agent, and mitochondrial regulator</li><li>Therapeutic considerations beyond sleep</li><li>Delivery systems, dosing, timing, and safety</li><li>Melatonin–nutrient combinations</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; melatonin-beyond-sleep ; melatonin-beyond-sleep ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/be0cjq4x/brand-logo-symphony.png ; brand-logo-symphony ; Sponsor logo image for Symphony Natural Health ; Symphony Natural Health ; dba90ff0-9908-4616-acf0-75e65f3f0fa7 ; 125,112,111,101 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Melatonin - Beyond Sleep (Symphony Natural Health) 11082023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Mayhem_and_Misconceptions_in_the_Upper_GI_Tract_(The_School_of_Applied_Functiona.vtt" ;
                     ; 5a3a9ad5-922a-40a1-98d5-b267651bf855 ; Spermidine: A Key Component to Cellular Longevity?                                                                                                                                      ; The body naturally produces a vital molecule that could help support youthful cell function and disease resistance. Dive into the science behind spermidine and learn how this compound can help promote health and longevity.          ; <p>What if there was a naturally occurring molecule that could help support youthful cell function and resistance to disease? Aging involves the systemic deterioration of eukaryotic cells in living organisms, such as animals, plants, fungi, and some unicellular organisms. All eukaryotic cells naturally contain a molecule called spermidine, which plays an integral role in cellular metabolism. Spermidine is thought to promote autophagy, a process by which damaged cells are cleared and healthy cells are regenerated, protecting against age-related diseases.</p><br> <p>In this thought-provoking webinar, Don Moxley, director of applied science and brand development at Longevity Labs, Inc., will delve into the science behind spermidine and explore the vital role of this compound in health and longevity.</p><br> <p>Key areas of the discussion will include:</p><br> <ul><li>The history and mechanistic role of spermidine</li><li>Advances in understanding spermidine and autophagy</li><li>Natural sources of spermidine</li><li>Dosing and application of spermidine to support longevity</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; spermidine-key-component-to-cellular-longevity ; spermidine-key-component-to-cellular-longevity ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/baoluo4h/brand-logo-spermidinelife.png ; brand-logo-spermidinelife ; Sponsor logo image for Spermidine Life ; Spermidine Life ; fba9495b-9723-4726-8649-09d9e4bfde37 ; 102,116,100,112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Spermidine - A Key Component to Cellular Longevity (Longevity Labs) 10262023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Solving_for_Antidepressant-Induced_Nutrient_Depletions_-_Science-Based_Solutions.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_07,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18
                     ; 158489a6-8e69-4ac2-b68c-00dfddaed150 ; Clinical Interventions for Food Sensitivities                                                                                                                                           ; Testing for food sensitivities is a common practice in functional medicine. Part 4 of this series examines patterns within the gut microbiome that can cause food sensitivities and how to alter those patterns.                        ; <p>Food sensitivity testing is commonplace in functional medicine practices, and treatment plans primarily focus on removing offending foods. But the best outcomes occur when food elimination is combined with interventions to decrease gut-based permeability and retrain the immune system to be less reactive. In Session 4 of this 6-session webinar series, Dr. Burdette will focus on specific patterns in the microbiome that can make people food sensitive and how to alter those patterns so that reactive foods might be better tolerated.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; clinical-interventions-for-food-sensitivities ; clinical-interventions-for-food-sensitivities ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 102,108,109,115,100,121,111,116 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver, How XYMOGEN Sharpens Your Aim - Part II (XYMOGEN) 10062023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Cellular_Senescence_and_the_Anti-Aging_Power_of_Senolytics_(Neurohacker_Collecti.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_25,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; 3c2d2cec-240d-417b-b8c8-59d9e00e410e ; Clinical Solutions Using Physiological Regulating Medicine                                                                                                                              ; How are practitioners preparing for the future of medicine? Join to examine a revolutionary branch of low-dose medicine—physiological regulating medicine—and discover the future of medical integration and innovative therapeutics.   ; <p>What is the future of medicine, and how can practitioners prepare for it? Physiological regulating medicine (PRM) is a revolutionary branch of low-dose medicine born from the convergence of molecular biology and psycho-neuro-endocrine-immunology. Discover how PRM seamlessly integrates Western conventional medicine with complementary and alternative medicine (CAM), offering cutting-edge therapeutic solutions.</p><br> <p>In this captivating webinar, Alessandro Perra, scientific director of Guna Pharmaceuticals, will provide an overview of PRM’s foundations and its role as a bridge between diverse therapeutic approaches. This is an opportunity to gain insights into the future of medical integration and harness the untapped potential of low-dose pharmacology.</p><br> <p>Key areas of the discussion will include:</p><br> <ul><li>Vital medications and their pivotal components</li><li>Pharmacological mechanisms from both homeopathic and molecular biology perspectives</li><li>PRM strategies for challenging conditions practitioners encounter daily</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; clinical-solutions-using-physiological-medicine ; clinical-solutions-using-physiological-medicine ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/5cjfixjv/guna-logo.png ; guna-logo ; Sponsor logo image for Guna Biotherapeutics ; Guna Biotherapeutics ; 51704180-2d86-4cac-b21e-519a5ce93f13 ; 109,100,126,121,103,117,112,125,118 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Clinical Solutions Using Physiological Regulating Medicine (GUNA Biotherapeutics) 09132023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver,_How_XYMOGEN_Sharpens_Your_Aim_-_Part_II_(XYMOGEN)_1006202.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_16,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_20
                     ; 3b4ab154-7151-423f-bce1-e79146c357c7 ; Holistic Management of Common Skin Conditions                                                                                                                                           ; The unique microbiome of the skin is susceptible to imbalances that can cause inflammatory-related skin conditions. Join Dr. Burdette to understand how dietary, supplemental, and lifestyle factors can influence skin health.         ; <p>The skin is the largest organ of the body and is generally a good indicator of one’s health. As the body’s external protective barrier, the skin is at risk for a wide range of problems. Inflammatory skin conditions, such as psoriasis, eczema, and dermatitis, are common yet can be difficult to treat. In Session 3 of this 6-session webinar series, Dr. Burdette will consider the nutrient status of patients with common skin conditions and how dietary, supplemental, and lifestyle factors can influence the unique microbiome of the skin.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; holistic-management-of-skin ; holistic-management-of-skin ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 108,110,119,112,117,115,103,105,100,113 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver, How XYMOGEN Sharpens Your Aim - Part II (XYMOGEN) 09072023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Histamine_Metabolism_Through_the_Lens_of_Gene_and_Nutrient_Panels_(Seeking_Healt.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_24,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; 0a96fa54-768f-4353-b619-4182342d1e7a ; Moringa the Miracle Tree: What is the Scientific Evidence?                                                                                                                              ; Moringa has been called the “miracle tree” in many cultures, but is it a false panacea? Join this educational webinar to learn the scientific evidence behind the nutritional and medicinal benefits of this superfood.                 ; <p>Moringa oleifera is a pantropical species known as the “miracle tree” in many cultures. Two decades of reputable research, showcased in mainstream scientific journals, highlight its extraordinary nutritional and medicinal properties. But is it the panacea some claim?</p><br> <p>In this presentation, Dr. Jed Fahey of Johns Hopkins University and Lisa Curtis of Kuli Kuli will separate fact from fiction and help practitioners understand which benefits of moringa are backed by rigorous scientific evidence. To harness the full potential of this superfood, attendees will also gain expert knowledge of:</p><br> <ul><li>Proper dosage levels of moringa for optimal results</li><li>How to identify high-quality moringa</li><li>Best practices for effectively incorporating moringa into patient diet plans</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; moringa-the-miracle-tree_fahey ; moringa-the-miracle-tree_fahey ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/bn5cyflv/brand-logo-kulikuli.png ; brand-logo-kulikuli ; Sponsor logo image for Kuli Kuli ; Kuli Kuli ; d7a98abe-d03b-4968-b112-2591852877c3,2588a0ac-0a77-4ef9-b95a-2ad04b1cff69 ; 102,103,108,111 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Moringa the Miracle Tree - What is the Scientific Evidence (Kuli Kuli) 08312023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Mood,_Mind,_and_Memory_-_The_Critical_Role_of_DHA_and_Lutein_in_Brain_Health_(Br.vtt" ;
                     ; 4d532c80-8db4-4e89-9520-2da8944f4ce2 ; Going Green: The Appeal of Phytonutrient-Rich Green Drinks                                                                                                                              ; Fruit and vegetable intake is associated with a healthy lifestyle, but most people aren't getting their recommended daily servings. Tune in to learn the potential benefits of adding a daily greens drink to a healthy diet.           ; <p>Many individuals do not consume the recommended daily servings of fruits and vegetables associated with better overall health. Adding a daily greens drink has been advocated as a convenient option to supplement a diet lacking from intake of these phytonutrient-rich food groups. But is drinking your fruits and veggies in the form of a greens drinks an adequate alternative to support a healthy lifestyle?</p><br> <p>Join Kenn Israel, a 30-year veteran of the natural products industry, for a presentation with unique insights into the efficacy of supplementing the diet with high-quality greens drinks. Using a popular example from Zahlerâ, a novel brand in the formulation of evidence-based dietary supplements, Kenn will highlight how phytonutrient-rich greens drinks may:</p></br> <ul><li>Support energy</li><li>Provide cellular protection</li><li>Promote a healthy gut microbiome and digestion</li><li>Boost overall health and well-being</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; going-green-israel-zahler ; going-green-israel-zahler ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/05ybufow/brand-logo-zahler.png ; brand-logo-zahler ; Sponsor logo image for Zahler ; Zahler ; 0b1e0a7f-7976-46a8-8614-764224a37ba0 ; 102,116,109,100,112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Going Green - The Appeal of Phytonutrient-Rich Green Drinks (Zahler) 08242023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver,_How_XYMOGEN_Sharpens_Your_Aim_-_Part_II_(XYMOGEN)_0816202.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_07,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18
                     ; c1191895-2ec3-4555-b901-2954b2fa99d6 ; Optimizing Nitric Oxide-Related Clinical Outcomes                                                                                                                                       ; Nitric oxide (NO) is a critical mediator of cellular communication, and its significance in improving clinical outcomes is often underappreciated. Join Dr. Elyaman and discover how to optimize NO production and bioavailability.     ; <p>Nitric oxide (NO) is a critical mediator of cell-to-cell communication with far-reaching implications for human health. NO is synthesized by the body, a process that can be affected by many factors, like aging or prior illness. Optimizing NO production is an important yet often overlooked clinical strategy for improving patient outcomes.</p><br> <p>In this engaging presentation, Dr. Yousef Elyaman merges research findings with his extensive clinical experience to provide unique perspectives and practical tips that can be seamlessly integrated into patient-care strategies. Attendees will gain a comprehensive understanding of NO, with emphasis on:</p><br> <ul><li>The 2 primary pathways of NO synthesis, how they operate, and how to optimize them</li><li>Strategies to bolster endothelial nitric oxide synthase (eNOS) activity</li><li>The NOꟷcardiovascular system connection</li><li>Useful strategies to enhance NO bioavailability</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; nitric-oxide-and-the-gut-lining-a-novel-gut-based-strategy ; nitric-oxide-and-the-gut-lining-a-novel-gut-based-strategy ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/o2xgr0i2/humann-logo.png ; humann-logo ; Sponsor logo image for Humann ; Humann ; d14775a7-ab27-46c1-a4cd-12e4d314016b ; 105,117,118,126,102,121,112,119,100 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Optimizing Nitric Oxide-Related Clinical Outcomes (HumanN) 08222023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Omega-3_Supplements_(Barlean's)_05182023_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_16,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18
                     ; 805d07de-97a7-4d83-8d96-3cc69fda6c3d ; Overfed Yet Undernourished - Optimizing Nutrient Intakes                                                                                                                                ; Americans are overfed yet undernourished, contributing to the risk of chronic disease. Join Chris D. Meletis, ND, to learn effective ways of incorporating critical nutrients using novel and patented nutraceuticals.                  ; <p>Americans are in a paradoxical state of being overfed yet undernourished. Modern farming practices, food processing, and other factors impact the vitamin, mineral, and phytonutrient content of the food supply. Over time, consuming these lower nutritional value foods heightens the risk for chronic conditions, including cardiovascular disease.</p><br> <p>In this webinar, esteemed researcher, author, and speaker Dr. Chris Meletis will equip clinicians with the evidentiary science behind this paradox and clinical pearls for augmenting patient nutritional status. Focal points will include:</p><br> <ul><li>The latest science on North American nutrient intakes</li><li>How undernourishment affects the epigenome</li><li>ow to How to maintain sufficient levels of critical nutrients, including iodine and 5-methyltetrahydrofolate (5-MTHF)</li><li>Exploration of novel, patented nutraceuticals for cardiac health and the strategic use of red yeast rice</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; overfed-undernourished-meletis-trugen ; overfed-undernourished-meletis-trugen ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/5a4mbu3f/brand-logo-trugen3.png ; brand-logo-trugen3 ; Sponsor logo image for TruGen3 ; TruGen3 ; 7757fa5b-9b4e-4f3a-a612-37d982da03de ; 105,100,126,112,125,127,103,104 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Overfed Yet Undernourished - Optimizing Nutrient Intakes (TruGen3) 08172023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Optimizing_Patient_Gut–Brain_Responses_(Neurohacker_Collective)_05092024.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_17,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_20
                     ; fd437f19-8f60-46d0-8765-70563d31bff9 ; Finding Nutritional Meaning in Standard Lab Work                                                                                                                                        ; It is not uncommon for patients to have lab results within normal limits and still feel unwell. In Part 2, Dr. Burdette examines the use of functional ranges to determine nutritional inferences from standard lab work.               ; <p>Join naturopathic physician and the education director for XYMOGEN, Dr. Cheryl Burdette, for 6 additional informative sessions highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will review the science and clinical applications for formulas in different health categories, informing attendees how to best use individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results.</p><br> <p>Your patient doesn’t feel well, yet according to their conventional doctor, their lab results are within “normal” ranges, indicating they are in good health. This is a familiar scenario for many practitioners whose patients have turned to functional medicine to find answers. Unbeknownst to many doctors, standard lab work can provide further insight into what is happening in the body. Signs of nutritional imbalance and patterns that can help get to the root of the problem can be revealed with the use of functional reference ranges. These ranges can also help practitioners evaluate the potential next steps in determining a patient’s treatment path. In Session 2 of this 6-session webinar series, Dr. Burdette will focus on chem screen and CBC markers and look at what nutritional inferences can be drawn from those results.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; finding-nutritional-menaning-in-lab-work-burdette ; finding-nutritional-menaning-in-lab-work-burdette ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/dev-webs-courteous-wombat/fz1ddqgb/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 101,117,118,112,125,105,121,100,104 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver, How XYMOGEN Sharpens Your Aim - Part II (XYMOGEN) 08162023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Finding_Balance_-_The_Power_of_Electrolytes_(LMNT)_07282022_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_01,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_29,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; afe5bcd3-aecd-4832-be4a-dae724e99bfa ; Harnessing Cellular Senescence                                                                                                                                                          ; The amount of senescent cells increases during aging, affecting the ability to withstand stress and illness. Tune in to this webinar to discover how suppressing cellular senescence may be the key to revitalizing aging tissues.      ; <p>The number of senescent cells increases with age and affects an individual’s ability to withstand stress and illness. Although senescent cells stop multiplying, they resist removal and secrete inflammatory compounds harming healthy cells and leading to a multitude of age-related conditions. Does harnessing cellular senescence hold the key to revitalizing aging tissues and decelerating biological aging?</p><br> <p>Join naturopathic physicians Nick Bitz and Gregory Kelly for an informative webinar that will explore the role senescent cells play in aging and what can be done to decrease their burden and make room for healthy, youthful cells. Topics discussed will include:</p><br> <ul><li>The theories and hallmarks of the aging process</li><li>Dietary and lifestyle factors that play a role in senescence</li><li>The emergence of “senolytics” as solutions to quell senescent cells</li><li>Clinical research supporting a novel, plant-based senolytic blend to optimize aging</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; harnessing-cellular-senescene ; harnessing-cellular-senescene ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/qqtnlyyi/neurohacker-logo.png ; brand-logo-neurohacker ; Sponsor logo image for Neurohacker Collective ; Neurohacker Collective ; 21e67f57-9ead-4d2e-b5e5-ce6d9f3498cf,8cd4190d-dc84-435d-aa6f-88ad239be9df ; 112,125,111 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Harnessing Cellular Senescence (Neurohacker Collective) 08032023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/The_Role_of_Dysbiosis_in_Pulmonary_Health_(Biocidin_Botanicals)_06102021_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_20,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; 62adccdb-14ea-4dff-94cc-9188acf2c293 ; Nutritional Interventions for Accelerated Aging: Slamming on the Brakes                                                                                                                 ; Biological aging is inevitable, but can it be slowed down? Join this educational webinar to learn more about anti-aging techniques and the nutritional approaches that may help support them.                                           ; <p>What accelerates biological aging, and how can it be slowed down? The need is rising for strategies that help slow biological aging by addressing the underlying causes of age-related functional changes, such as weak digestion, cognitive changes, decreased bone density, or loss of muscle strength. Being well-versed in current anti-aging modalities will help practitioners meet the needs of an increasingly aged population as well as patients searching to maximize youthfulness.</p><br> <p>In this insightful webinar, Laurel Sterling will explore crucial aspects of anti-aging science from an integrative standpoint, emphasizing the following key areas:</p><br> <ul><li>Biological aging accelerators, such as glycation, inflammation, and oxidation</li><li>Current scientific research on methods that may help slow biological aging</li><li>Nutritional approaches to help counter the effects of accelerated aging</li></ul>  <p>Join this webinar for a deeper understanding of current anti-aging science and methodologies that ultimately empower patients to lead longer, healthier lives.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; nutritional-in-terventions-for-accelerated-aging-laurel-sterling ; nutritional-in-terventions-for-accelerated-aging-laurel-sterling ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/odhfdnlp/brand-logo-carlson-labs.png ; brand-logo-carlson-labs ; Sponsor logo image for Carlson ; Carlson ; 63caae5f-cb97-43a3-83b5-faffc84eb8b0 ; 100,126,112,117,118,111,102 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Nutritional Interventions for Accelerated Aging (Carlson Labs) 07272023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Nutrigenomics_-_Finding_a_Personalized_Path_to_Wellness_(Nutrigenomics)_01132022.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; 9650b714-32d5-4b8e-bbcd-91445285c38a ; Adaptogenic Herbs for Strength, Stamina, and Stress Support                                                                                                                             ; Stress can impact many health conditions and play a role in overall mental and physical well-being. Tune in to discover how adaptogens can help restore homeostasis in the body and support overall wellness.                           ; <p>Chronic stress can result in a multitude of issues ranging from fatigue and difficulty focusing to an increased risk for many health conditions. Adaptogens have been used for centuries to help the body adapt to stressors and to generate a balancing effect. But can adaptogenic herbs impact the hectic and stress-filled lives of individuals living in the modern world?</p><br> <p>Join renowned herbalist and ethnobotanist David Winston to learn how adaptogens work to help restore homeostasis and promote mental and physical well-being. Some of the highlights to be covered include:</p><br> <ul><li>What is and what is not an adaptogen</li><li>The role of adaptogens in cognitive and immune health</li><li>The unique qualities of and clinical applications for adaptogenic herbs</li><li>Companion herbs used with adaptogens: nervines, nootropics, and restorative tonics</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; phytoestrogens-and-phytoprogestins ; phytoestrogens-and-phytoprogestins ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/1smn0xi1/brand-logo-herbalistandalchemist.png ; brand-logo-herbalistandalchemist ; Sponsor logo image for Herbalist & Alchemist ; Herbalist & Alchemist ; 1317feb9-9b4a-41ed-9fd3-68a059c0ad08 ; 100,117,118,104,115,121,112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Adaptogenic Herbs for Strength, Stamina, and Stress Support (Herbalist & Alchemist) 07242023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/A_Whole_Systems_Approach_to_Influencing_the_Physiological_Impact_of_Stress_(XYMO.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_16,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18
                     ; 2bd0066d-5919-49a1-b102-eea9f859a7a0 ; Semaglutide Adjuncts and Natural GLP-1 Management                                                                                                                                       ; Maintaining a healthy weight is important to overall wellness. In Part 1 of this 6-session series, Dr. Burdette reviews the role of semaglutide in weight management, how to minimize side effects, and alternative therapy options.    ; <p>Join naturopathic physician and the education director for XYMOGEN, Dr. Cheryl Burdette, for 6 additional informative sessions highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will review the science and clinical applications for formulas in different health categories, informing attendees how to best use individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results.</p><br> <p>Popularized by celebrities as an “off-label” solution to weight management, the GLP-1 agonist known as semaglutide has taken the market by storm. Although indicated for glycemic control, semaglutide also triggers the parts of the brain that suppress appetite and signal feelings of fullness. Is it safe? What are the downsides? What is a practical clinical application for use with other weight management strategies? In Session 1 of this 6-session webinar series, Dr. Burdette will give an overview of natural adjuncts that can minimize potential side effects and alternatives that also function as natural GLP-1 agonists.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; semalglutide-adjuncts-and-natural-glp-1-management ; semalglutide-adjuncts-and-natural-glp-1-management ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 103,119,105,115 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver, How XYMOGEN Sharpens Your Aim - Part II (XYMOGEN) 07182023.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Restoring_Microbial_Vitality_(Zahler)_04202023_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_25,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; 14e57ce1-24a5-427a-8d2f-16fac285056d ; Grow a Strong Membership-Based Integrative Practice                                                                                                                                     ; Considering opening your own integrative medicine practice or looking for ways to grow an existing one? Gain valuable insights and learn new strategies to help lay an unshakeable foundation for a successful practice.                ; <p>Join us for a timely discussion on how to build an unshakeable foundation for your practice using proven methods. Practitioners will learn how to incorporate key value-added strategies and systems, decrease burnout, increase personal satisfaction, and infuse personal uniqueness into a practice. The implementation of Dr. Matteoli and Scott Rattigan’s methods will lay the groundwork for a successful integrative membership-based practice that supports its patients while pushing ahead of the competition.</p><br> <p>You will also learn:</p><br> <ul><li>The 3 primary patient appointments needed for streamlined practice efficiency</li><li>The 6 important documents that every patient should receive</li><li>Critical telemedicine best practices, including: <li>What to consider when practicing across state lines</li><li>How to safeguard a virtual practice</li></li><li>A unique and tested financial system that could result in significant tax savings</li><li>How to organize receivables and manage payables with confidence</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; grow-a-strong-membership-matteoli ; grow-a-strong-membership-matteoli ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/ozrfj2ud/logo_origins_incubator.png ; logo_origins_incubator ; Sponsor logo image for Origins Incubator ; Origins Incubator ; cf9312e5-896b-4bf9-b6aa-31f595a8bba8,a1c92d00-bbe8-4563-8cbb-e58d39824a56 ; 128 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Grow a Strong Membership-Based Integrative Practice (Origins Incubator) 08112022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Going_Green_-_The_Appeal_of_Phytonutrient-Rich_Green_Drinks_(Zahler)_08242023.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_27
                     ; e14fd329-3fc0-451f-9fac-38321077180a ; Advances for Healthy Brain Aging                                                                                                                                                        ; As the global aging population grows, healthcare practitioners are seeking innovative ways to support healthy brain aging. Join Dr. Alan Snow for a deep dive into nootropics, such as cat's claw, that may support neural health.*     ; <p>The global population of the “oldest old” is expected to more than triple by 2050. This rise in the aged population is pulling healthcare practitioners into the realm of nootropics, such as cat’s claw (Uncaria tomentosa), to counter age-related memory challenges and other neural health concerns. The complexities associated with the aging mind are myriad and often misunderstood. Through an expanded understanding of the latest clinical discoveries, practitioners can streamline decisions and develop strong integrative wellness plans for their patients.</p><br> <p>Join Dr. Alan Snow, renowned neuroscientist and researcher, for a deep dive into the critical advancements in our understanding of neural structures and the botanicals that support neural health, particularly while aging.</p><br> <p>During this webinar, Dr. Snow will cover:</p><br> <ul><li>More than 15 years of cat’s claw research and the discovery of PTI-00703 extract</li><li>The trilogy of memory loss—the real reasons behind age-related memory decline</li><li>Incorporation of natural brain health products into patient protocols, including examples from the Percepta Professional®</li>  <p>Don’t miss this exciting, research-packed webinar that has the potential to be immediately helpful to the growing aged patient population.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; advances-for-healthy-brain-snow ; advances-for-healthy-brain-snow ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/xsbbzdjc/brand-logo-cognitive-clarity.png ; brand-logo-cognitive-clarity ; Sponsor logo image for Cognitive Clarity ; Cognitive Clarity ; ec2a5050-996d-4531-8564-94c82fe89006 ; 100,112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Advances for Healthy Brain Aging (Cognitive Clarity) 06212023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Adaptogenic_Herbs_for_Strength,_Stamina,_and_Stress_Support_(Herbalist_&_Alchemi.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18
                     ; a6916705-e4cd-407f-a970-77b0aa39474a ; Managing Hyperandrogenism in Women of Reproductive Age                                                                                                                                  ; Hyperandrogenism commonly occurs in women of reproductive age and can impact fertility. Tune in as Dr. Stephanie Nishek discusses recommendations to shift the holistic care of hyperandrogenic women when trying to conceive.          ; <p>An excess level of circulating androgenic hormones, primarily testosterone, is known as hyperandrogenism. This condition can affect children and adults, but it most commonly occurs in females of reproductive age and can impact fertility. Naturopathic and functional medicine experts can help establish a healthy foundation to address symptoms in hyperandrogenic women, but should the recommendations shift for this population when trying to conceive?</p><br> <p>Join naturopathic physician Stephanie Nishek for this informative webinar that will review the essential aspects of a holistic approach to exploring and resolving hyperandrogenism in women of reproductive age. Topics covered will include:</p> <ul><li>The role of androgens and causes of excessive levels</li><li>Symptoms of hyperandrogenism</li><li>Dietary, nutritional, and lifestyle management pillars for symptom support</li><li>Fertility-specific support for hyperandrogenic females</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; bioidentical-hormones-empowering-the-menopause-transition ; bioidentical-hormones-empowering-the-menopause-transition ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/iijplnxm/brand-logo-wisewomanherbals.png ; brand-logo-wisewomanherbals ; Sponsor logo image for Wise Woman Herbals ; Wise Woman Herbals ; eb992c1b-fb50-435e-ab7e-d834ba016b07 ; 117,102,105,115,125,100,112,121,129 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Managing Hyperandrogenism in Women of Reproductive Age (Wise Woam Herbals) 06152023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Managing_Blood_Pressure_and_Cardiac_Rhythm_With_Herbal_Medicine_(Restorative_For.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_20,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_22
                     ; 80fde79b-0ad8-4784-a3c5-a1a4a45373d2 ; Omega-3 Supplements: Optimizing Results for Your Patients                                                                                                                               ; Omega-3s are essential for physiological function but cannot be synthesized in the body. Join Julie Hawkes to learn how incorporating supplements into patient wellness protocols can optimize omega-3 intake.                          ; <p>Omega-3s are essential for physiological function: they must be obtained through foods or supplements as they cannot be synthesized in the body. Scientific evidence has linked the intake of omega-3 to better overall health, but the average consumer does not get enough omega-3 from diet alone. Many individuals who are aware of the benefits of omega-3 turn to the wide range of available dietary supplement products to boost their intake. As healthcare practitioners, the challenge is: How do you help your patients make the best choices to ensure they get the best results?</p><br> <p>Join Julie Hawkes, product educator for Barlean’s, a pioneering omega-3 company with a strong history of leadership and innovation. Julie will share unique insights into the omega-3 category and the Barlean’s brand. Some of the highlights to be covered include:</p><br> <ul><li>The basics of omega-3 oils and their place in the dietary fat spectrum</li><li>Different delivery options for omega-3 supplementation</li><li>Oil emulsions and bioavailability</li><li>Science-driven omega-3s for various health conditions</li><li>Customizing patient protocols to yield results</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; omega-3-supplements ; omega-3-supplements ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/0onpdsy3/brand-logo-barleans.png ; brand-logo-barleans ; Sponsor logo image for Barlean's ; Barlean's ; c436ed42-920c-49bb-aa0d-6d6232a52a36 ; 105,126,110,104,112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Omega-3 Supplements (Barlean's) 05182023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Nutritional_Triage_(Innate)_08302022_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_10,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18
                     ; f8aa0914-ed87-4817-a4e6-c213a28f0356 ; Butyrate: Clinical Applications for the Gut, Brain, and Body                                                                                                                            ; Butyrate is critical to multiple aspects of human health but may be lacking in many patients. Join Justine Stenger to learn about the critical roles of butyrate and why supplementation could be optimal for your patients’ health.    ; <p>Butyrate is a short-chain fatty acid critical to multiple aspects of human health. It can diminish as we age, potentially contributing to difficult-to-diagnose conditions. Butyrate influences energy metabolism, neurological health, inflammation, and immune function and tolerance, making low levels problematic for many internal systems. Fortunately, appropriate supplementation can help boost butyrate levels.</p><br> <p>Join Justine Stenger, holistic nutrition specialist and therapeutic chef, for this researched-based presentation outlining the clinical importance and profound health benefits of butyrate. Justine will specifically address the clinical applications of supplementary butyrate in the following areas:</p><br> <ul><li>Prophylactic use</li><li>Inflammatory response</li><li>Gut-associated health challenges</li><li>Neurological health concerns</li> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; optimizing-patient-gut-brain-responses ; optimizing-patient-gut-brain-responses ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/ni1davme/brand-logo-bodybio.png ; bodybio-logo ; Sponsor logo image for Bodybio ; Bodybio ; ab80b818-7c33-405c-88de-d439bdbd448b ; 103,115,109,102,119,100,112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Butyrate Clinical Applications for the Gut, Brain, and Body (BodyBio) 05042023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Bioidentical_Hormones_-_Empowering_the_Menopause_Transition__(Quicksilver_Scient.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13
                     ; 092306b8-9db2-495b-9bf7-bc12ac87dfb0 ; Evaluating Non-Pharmacological Approaches to Children’s Health                                                                                                                          ; Common clinical conditions that impact children are on the rise and can be linked to poor nutrition. Join Dr. Matt Hand to review non-pharmacological, therapeutic approaches to support the pediatric population.                      ; <p>In recent years, practitioners have seen an increase in common clinical conditions impacting children. Many of these challenges can be linked to kids consuming inadequate nutrient levels necessary to fuel their growth and enable them to thrive. Whether it is trouble sleeping, headaches, gut discomfort, or stress and behavioral issues, reports of these complaints are reaching near-epidemic proportions among the pediatric population.</p><br> <p>Join Dr. Matt Hand, pediatric integrative healthcare advocate, for an informative webinar highlighting non-pharmacological, therapeutic approaches to children’s health that are based on clinical data. Dr. Hand will share his experience and expertise regarding:</p><br> <ul><li>Quality and innovation in dietary supplements for children</li><li>Clinical protocols to nourish kids’ foundational health and foster healthy behavior and sleep</li><li>Insights into the rationale for the development of Little DaVinci® premium formulations</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; evaluating-non-pharmacological-approaches-hand ; evaluating-non-pharmacological-approaches-hand ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/j3dmcl0y/brand-logo-davinci.png ; brand-logo-davinci ; Sponsor logo image for DaVinci Laboratories ; DaVinci Laboratories ; 2d9e3be0-f57c-43dd-84ef-7fd101996682 ; 107 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Evaluating Non-Pharmacological Approaches to Children’s Health (DaVinci Laboratories) 04272023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Disease_Begins_in_the_Gut,_But_Often_Doesn’t_Stay_There_(The_School_of_Applied_F.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_104,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_27,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_20
                     ; 6f0b2cf7-6e73-4d7c-996a-f84c04922a54 ; Restoring Microbial Vitality                                                                                                                                                            ; Microbial dysbiosis can wreak havoc on the body’s internal systems. Join Kenn Israel to learn from real-world examples of how to create a microbiome reset in your patients and get their gut health back on track.                     ; <p>The human body contains trillions of microbes, most of which are beneficial and vital to supporting healthy physiological functions. However, internal and external factors can create dysbiosis in this finely tuned microbial community, including stress, an unhealthy diet, food sensitivities, antibiotics, immune-suppressed conditions, intestinal infections, parasites, and inflammation.</p><br> <p>Join Kenn Israel, a respected 30-year veteran of the natural products industry, for a presentation with unique insights into tuning up microbe imbalances. Using real-world examples, Kenn will share from his experiences with a special focus on ParaGuardÔ by Zahler, a novel brand with a strong history of leadership and innovation in the dietary supplement marketplace. This webinar will highlight:</p><br> <ul><li>Physiological roles of microbial flora</li><li>Symptoms of dysbiosis</li><li>Challenges that cause microorganism imbalance</li><li>Solutions for a microbiome reset</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; restoring-microbial-vitality-israel ; restoring-microbial-vitality-israel ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/05ybufow/brand-logo-zahler.png ; brand-logo-zahler ; Sponsor logo image for Zahler ; Zahler ; 0b1e0a7f-7976-46a8-8614-764224a37ba0 ; 115,108,109,100,113,102 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Restoring Microbial Vitality (Zahler) 04202023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Probiotic_Use_for_Support_of_Urovaginal_Health_(Jarrow_Formulas)_11162021_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19
                     ; 65839238-61c3-444a-a0ca-c7b87221338d ; The Testosterone SWITCH: A Scientific Approach to Naturally Revitalize Testosterone                                                                                                     ; Testosterone contributes to many functions in the body beyond libido and stamina, and unbalanced levels can disrupt numerous activities. Tune in to learn the 3 “switches” in the body that support natural testosterone restoration.   ; <p>Testosterone naturally declines with age, and an unbalanced level can cause impairment in testosterone-dependent functions. In males, the androgenic hormone testosterone is commonly known for its physiological function of regulating libido and stamina : however, it also plays a role in muscle mass and strength, bone mass, fat distribution, mental performance, energy, red blood cell production, and sperm development. Given the wide range of testosterone-dependent functions, countering low levels can support overall health and well-being.</p><br> <p>Join Dr. Kyl Smith, renowned author of The Testosterone SWITCH, as he presents a science-based approach to transforming the health of your male patients. Dr. Smith will share 5 years of his research, which focused on the 3 main “switches” in the male body that turn testosterone off, and he will explain how flipping them on can support natural testosterone restoration. Attendees will learn powerful steps to help patients measurably increase testosterone levels to revitalize their health and masculinity.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; the-testosterone-switch ; the-testosterone-switch ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/g0lpoaca/progressivelabssponsor.png ; progressivelabssponsor ; Sponsor logo image for Progressive Laboratories ; Progressive Laboratories ; fc9fe8d3-b4fc-4396-808f-c327d66e1a5f ; 118,112,101,103,104 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/The Testosterone SWITCH - A Scientific Approach to Naturally Revitalize Testosterone (Progressive Laboratories) 04202023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/The_Science_and_Clinical_Application_of_Collagen_Peptides_(Vital_Proteins)_01182.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_20,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; bd9aa4f8-e103-438b-adc0-b81005394b3b ; Arrows In Your Quiver Webinar Series: Managing Cytokines                                                                                                                                ; The body releases cytokines to act as messengers for cell-to-cell communication when coordinating an immune response. In this final session, Dr. Burdette reviews how to regulate cytokines and optimize immune function.               ; <p>Join naturopathic physician and the education director for XYMOGEN, Dr. Cheryl Burdette, for an informative 12-part series highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will review clinical applications for each specialty category and inform attendees how to utilize individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results.</p><br> <p>Cytokines are important messengers the immune system releases to communicate with cells and coordinate the immune response. As “master regulators,” cytokines control both upregulation and downregulation of the cytokine system, and aberrations in their signaling pathways can lead to cellular damage and impact overall health. In this final session of the 12-part series, Dr. Burdette will review how to regulate cytokines and modulate immune function.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; managing-cytokines ; managing-cytokines ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 108,100 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver 12-Part Series - Managing Cytokines (XYMOGEN) 04132023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver_12-Part_Series_-_A_Functional_Approach_to_Diabetic_Markers.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19
                     ; 0a5a470c-2945-4e83-b803-6d80b53aab32 ; Arrows In Your Quiver Webinar Series: Management of the Glycemic Inflammatory Load                                                                                                      ; Blood glucose management is not just important for people living with diabetes. Join Dr. Burdette for Part 11 of this series to learn clinical strategies for managing blood sugar and its impact on overall health and wellness.       ; <p>Join naturopathic physician and the education director for XYMOGEN, Dr. Cheryl Burdette, for an informative 12-part series highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will review clinical applications for each specialty category and inform attendees how to utilize individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results.</p><br> <p>Much has been learned in the past decade about the impact of tightly controlled blood glucose management. As a result, many conditions in the diabetic continuum have been found to improve, including pre-diabetes, hypoglycemia, polycystic ovary syndrome, and even pain secondary to inflammation. Join Dr. Burdette for Part 11 of this 12-part series, where she will review clinical strategies for managing blood sugar as part of the strategy for the overall improvement of an individual’s health.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; management-of-the-glycemic-inflammatory-load ; management-of-the-glycemic-inflammatory-load ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 103,119,108 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver 12-Part Series - A Functional Approach to Diabetic Markers and Oxidative Stress (XYMOGEN) 04062023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver_12-Part_Series_-_How_to_Beat_the_Bellyache__(XYMOGEN)_0316.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_25
                     ; 4b30fc38-1465-4954-a863-3b1867b72efd ; Arrows In Your Quiver Webinar Series: Managing Histamine Intolerance                                                                                                                    ; Histamine intolerance can negatively affect the digestive, cardiovascular, nervous, and skeletal systems.  In Part 10, Dr. Burdette will unlock the mysteries of histamine and discuss ways to decrease histamine production.           ; <p>Join naturopathic physician and the education director for XYMOGEN, Dr. Cheryl Burdette, for an informative 12-part series highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will review clinical applications for each specialty category and inform attendees how to utilize individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results.</p><br> <p>The complex and diverse physiology of histamine has been widely studied. Histamine intolerance can affect digestive, integumentary, cardiovascular, nervous, skeletal, and other body systems, leading to various symptomatic complaints that are often difficult to address. In Part 10 of this 12-part series, Dr. Burdette will review the major routes for histamine elimination and strategies to decrease production.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; managing-histamine-intolerance ; managing-histamine-intolerance ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 116,108,100 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver 12-Part Series - Histamine Management (XYMOGEN) 03302023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver_12-Part_Series_-_Managing_Cytokines_(XYMOGEN)_04132023_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,