                     ; 07d19933-2b3f-4287-ad93-3240377acea2 ; Arrows In Your Quiver Webinar Series: The Multifaceted Biological Role of Enzymes                                                                                                       ; Enzymes catalyze and regulate many biochemical reactions in the body. In Part 6, Dr. Burdette unveils the various uses for supplemental enzymes and how clinical enzyme therapy can boost physiological functions.                      ; <p>Join naturopathic physician and the education director for XYMOGEN, Dr. Cheryl Burdette, for an informative 12-part series highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will review clinical applications for each specialty category and inform attendees how to utilize individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results.</p><br> <p>Enzymes are commonly associated with assimilating nutrients from food: however, they have a wide range of essential physiological functions. From allergies and food sensitivities to hormonal imbalances and behavioral issues, enzymes catalyze and regulate many biochemical reactions in the body. In Part 6 of this 12-part series, Dr. Burdette will review the various uses for supplemental enzymes and how to clinically utilize enzyme therapy.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; the-multifaceted-biological-role-of-enzymes ; the-multifaceted-biological-role-of-enzymes ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 108,115,100 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver 12-Part Series - The Multifaceted Biological Role of Enzymes (XYMOGEN) 03022023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrow_in_Your_Quiver_12-Part_Series_-_The_Ins_and_Outs_of_Vitamin_K_and_D_(XYMOG.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12
                     ; 19fcb97f-7177-4712-9867-ebc0110aa8d5 ; Arrows In Your Quiver Webinar Series: Natural Pain Management                                                                                                                           ; Natural remedies are often considered supplementary treatments for pain management. In Part 5 of this series, Dr. Burdette discusses clinically applicable natural pain management strategies that address various conditions.          ; <p>Join naturopathic physician and the education director for XYMOGEN, Dr. Cheryl Burdette, for an informative 12-part series highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will review clinical applications for each specialty category and inform attendees how to utilize individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results.</p><br> <p>Integrative therapies are a known adjunct to managing occasional discomfort associated with overworked muscles. However, are these natural remedies as clinically applicable as acute treatments? In part 5 of this 12-part series, Dr. Burdette will focus on strategies used in her practice for natural pain management associated with various conditions.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; natural-pain-management ; natural-pain-management ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 102,126,108 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver 12-Part Series - Pain Management  (XYMOGEN) 02232023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrow_in_Your_Quiver_12-Part_Series_-_Maxing_the_Mitochondria_(XYMOGEN)_02022023.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_24,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; f20587ed-0930-4700-8e56-1e40ee99d20a ; Arrows In Your Quiver Webinar Series: The Collagen Story                                                                                                                                ; The natural aging process includes declining collagen production leading to integrity reduction in connective tissues. In Part 4, nutrients to help increase collagen and genes that enhance collagen production are reviewed.          ; <p>Join naturopathic physician and the education director for XYMOGEN, Dr. Cheryl Burdette, for an informative 12-part series highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will review clinical applications for each specialty category and inform attendees how to utilize individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results.</p><br> <p>Collagen is an abundant protein that plays an essential structural role in supporting the strength and resilience of tissues. The biosynthesis of collagen begins to decline with the natural aging process, leading to reduced integrity in connective tissues, such as skin, tendons, bones, and cartilage. In Part 4 of this 12-part series, Dr. Burdette will review nutrients that serve as building blocks for increasing collagen and those that turn on genes to enhance collagen production.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; the-collagen-story ; the-collagen-story ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 102,126,108 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver 12-Part Series - The Collagen Story (XYMOGEN) 02162023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver_12-Part_Series_-_Amplify_Your_Exercise_(XYMOGEN)_03232023_.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_25,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; ba275088-59fa-46b0-bbaa-3a9d3cb90b34 ; Arrows In Your Quiver Webinar Series: Building an Immune Forcefield                                                                                                                     ; Bacterial, fungal or viral pathogens can create difficult-to-manage symptoms and impair the immune system. In part 3, Dr. Burdette reviews clinical applications for symptom management and maintaining a strong immune resilience.     ; <p>Join naturopathic physician and the education director for XYMOGEN, Dr. Cheryl Burdette, for an informative 12-part series highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will review clinical applications for each specialty category and inform attendees how to utilize individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results.</p><br> <p>Whether bacterial, viral, or fungal, pathogens can wreak havoc on the immune system, presenting various symptoms that can be difficult to manage. In Part 3 of this 12-part series, Dr. Burdette will review tried-and-false clinical applications for maintaining strong immune resilience and managing acute symptoms stemming from each major pathogen category.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; cellular-senescence-and-the-anti-aging-power-of-senolytics ; cellular-senescence-and-the-anti-aging-power-of-senolytics ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 100,115 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrows in Your Quiver 12-Part Series - Bust the Biofilm, Beat the Bacteria, Build the Person (XYMOGEN) 02092023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Advances_for_Healthy_Brain_Aging_(Cognitive_Clarity)_06212023_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; 3519f200-0527-4f62-94da-1e195a769130 ; Arrows In Your Quiver Webinar Series: Mitochondrial Energy                                                                                                                              ; Neurologic, cardiovascular, and energy issues can stem from problems in the mitochondria. Part 2 of this series focuses on the physiological functions of mitochondria and evidence-based tools for enhancing energy production.        ; <p>Mitochondrial Energy Join naturopathic physician and the education director for XYMOGEN, Dr. Cheryl Burdette, for an informative 12-part series highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will review clinical applications for each specialty category and inform attendees how to utilize individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results.</p><br> <p>Neurologic, cardiovascular, and energy issues often stem from problems rooted in the mitochondria, a part of the cellular structure known as “the powerhouse of the cell.” In Part 2 of this 12-part series, Dr. Burdette will review the physiological functions of the mitochondria and provide evidence-based tools for supporting the antioxidant and cytoprotective activity of mitochondrial cells to enhance energy production.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; mitochondrial-energy ; mitochondrial-energy ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 102,116,112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrow in Your Quiver 12-Part Series - Maxing the Mitochondria (XYMOGEN) 02022023_1_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver_12-Part_Series_-_Histamine_Management_(XYMOGEN)_03302023_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_01,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_24,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_29,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; 80d305c5-7cc3-4580-b08c-eab744a3266b ; Arrows In Your Quiver Webinar Series: The Ins and Outs of Vitamins K and D                                                                                                              ; Vitamins K and D greatly benefit overall well-being. Dr. Burdette gives an overview of the clinical applications for and the conditions that warrant supplemental use of these vitamins and the various dose ranges.                    ; <p>The Ins and Outs of Vitamins K and D Join naturopathic physician and the education director for XYMOGEN, Dr. Cheryl Burdette, for an informative 12-part series highlighting XYMOGEN’s professional formulas. Dr. Burdette will review clinical applications for each specialty category and inform attendees how to utilize individual products in their practice to achieve optimal patient results.</p><br> <p>Supplemental vitamins K and D have individually well-documented physiological benefits, as well as complementary benefits for bone and cardiovascular health. In Part 1 of this 12-part series, Dr. Burdette will give an overview of the clinical applications for and the conditions that warrant supplemental use of these fat-soluble vitamins and the merits of various dose ranges. Vascular elasticity and regulation of T-cell function related to K and D will also be reviewed.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; the-ins-and-outs-of-vitamins-k-and-d ; the-ins-and-outs-of-vitamins-k-and-d ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 105,100,104 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Arrow in Your Quiver 12-Part Series - The Ins and Outs of Vitamin K and D (XYMOGEN) 01262023_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver_12-Part_Series_-_The_Collagen_Story_(XYMOGEN)_02162023_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_05,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_17,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_24,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; bfea50ad-0742-438d-ad8d-97ce6b456b30 ; Catalysts for Transforming Wellness                                                                                                                                                     ; Enzymes are usually linked to digestive health, but they play a bigger role in lasting wellness. Tune in to learn how enzymes can help alleviate allergies, food sensitivities, hormonal imbalances, behavioral issues, and more.       ; <p>In recent years, there has been an epidemic-like increase in allergies, food sensitivities, hormonal imbalances, behavioral issues, and other health-related problems. Through their role in catalyzing and regulating biochemical reactions in the body, supplemental enzymes may help alleviate these types of conditions. Digestive enzymes are energy-rich protein molecules that help break down food and release nutrients for energy, cell growth, and repair. Enzymes significantly impact a person’s digestive and immune health, and enzyme activity can be influenced by an individual’s genetics, lifestyle, environment, and diet.</p><br> <p>In this presentation, industry enzyme expert Amy Rawls will review the critical role of enzymes as more than just digestive support. She will discuss the connections between nutrition and digestive development and the part that enzyme therapy may play in achieving lasting wellness. You will learn how enzymes contribute to:</p><br> <ul><li>Digestive support</li><li>Cellular health</li><li>A healthy inflammatory response</li><li>Health maintenance and overall wellness</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; enzymes-catalysts-for-tranforming-wellness ; enzymes-catalysts-for-tranforming-wellness ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/xncf4yc0/brand-logo-transformationenzyme.png ; transformation-logo ; Sponsor logo image for TransFormation ; TransFormation ; 6896d481-8cfd-4191-b0e2-6235e15e7ecc ; 116,115,100 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Enzymes - Catalysts for Transforming Wellness (Transformation Enzyme) 12152022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Butyrate_Clinical_Applications_for_the_Gut,_Brain,_and_Body_(BodyBio)_05042023_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_07,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_10,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19
                     ; 693b6a21-143d-4998-8651-fc1f382e38af ; Lab and Genetic Testing to Create Protocols for Iron-Related Health Problems                                                                                                            ; Undiagnosed and untreated high iron levels are the root of many health problems. Dr. Christy Sutton explains how genetic testing and understanding lab values can inform precision-based health plans for patients with iron overload.  ; <p>The silent epidemic of undiagnosed high iron levels has been linked to the root cause of many health problems. Hemochromatosis is primarily a hereditary condition that causes iron overload in the body leading to tissue and organ damage. Iron overload can also be secondary to other disorders and is often overlooked as a contributing factor to a patient’s symptoms. Healthcare providers can now use lab and genetic testing to provide the data needed to identify iron overload and create customized nutrition and lifestyle protocols to manage related health issues.</p><br> <p>Join Dr. Christy Sutton to learn how the integration of genetic testing and understanding lab values create a precision-based health plan for patients with iron overload. Some of the highlights to be covered include:</p><br> <ul><li>Correctly testing for and understanding hemochromatosis genes</li><li>Symptoms and problems associated with irregular iron patterns</li><li>Iron levels and the inflammatory response</li><li>Clinical protocols for the management of iron-related health problems</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; lab-and-generic-testing ; lab-and-generic-testing ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/5rr…nen/labrongenomics_brand_logo_webinar_sponsor.png ; labrongenomics_brand_logo_webinar_sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for Labrogenomics ; Labrogenomics ; 2ecf7d93-2f1d-4234-8eb4-a4987236287d ; 128 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Laboratory & Genetic Testing of Iron Overload, Hemochromatosis, and Anemia of Inflammation (Labrogenomics) 12012022_1_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Is_Mushroom_Extract_a_Match_for_HPV_(American_BioSciences)_05102022_1.vtt" ;
                     ; 76124bd9-3a35-41b8-a24a-1ac88a67bfe4 ; Nephrological Health and Microcirculation, Improving Filtration for Health                                                                                                              ; High blood pressure can negatively impact the body in many ways, including constricting the kidney’s blood vessels. Join Dr. Cheryl Burdette in exploring clinical interventions to support renal health and proper blood filtration.   ; <p>As the kidney’s functional unit, nephrons comprise a dense network of blood vessels that act as the body’s purification system. Over time, uncontrolled high blood pressure can cause these arteries to narrow, weaken, or harden, resulting in a lack of blood flow to kidney tissue. Arterial damage results in the nephrons not receiving essential oxygen and nutrients, which can cause an inability to filter blood and regulate fluid, hormones, acids, and salts. If blood pressure and kidney damage continue to spiral negatively, kidney failure can result.</p><br> <p>Join Dr. Cheryl Burdette for an informative presentation that will examine the interconnections between kidney function and regulation of blood pressure as well as clinical interventions to improve renal health. Dr. Burdette will highlight:</p><br> <ul><li>The role of the kidney as an organ of detoxification</li><li>Conditions associated with kidney dysfunction</li><li>The use of lab values to manage renal health</li><li>Nutrients that bolster nephron health</li><li>Early warning signs of hypertension and its impact on kidney health</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; nephrological-health-and-microcirculation-improving ; nephrological-health-and-microcirculation-improving ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 109,105 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Nephrological Health and Microcirculation, Improving Filtration for Health (XYMOGEN) 11302022_1_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Navigating_Mold_Toxicity_and_Revolutionizing_Recovery_(BodyBio)_01042024.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_16
                     ; 8d109fc8-330c-4548-b76a-c7a51174d48d ; Nutrigenomics: Finding a Personalized Path to Wellness                                                                                                                                  ; Nutrigenomics uses genetic testing to understand the interaction between genes, nutrition, and health. World-renowned expert Dr. Yael Joffe outlines how to translate genetic testing results into customized wellness plans.           ; <p>Genetics make up the baseline code by which the human body functions. Genetic testing can be used as a tool to help predict how an individual’s body responds to internal and external stimuli. The results can help practitioners understand what is happening on a cellular level and assist them in creating more comprehensive and tailored care plans for their patients.</p><br> <p>Join world-renowned nutrigenomics expert Dr. Yael Joffe for a deep dive into the power of genetic testing. Key topics covered in this informative webinar will include:</p><br> <ul><li>Genetic testing 101</li><li>Translating test results into a wellness plan</li><li>How to marry a genetic blueprint with a supplement regimen</li></ul> <p>Dr. Joffe will also address the science and efficacy behind 3X4 Genetics and what makes her company stand out in the rapidly evolving discipline of nutrigenomics testing.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; nutrigenomics ; nutrigenomics ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 1c59e7f9-6e8c-42c5-beec-66dabe381cbf ; 128 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Nutrigenomics - Finding a Personalized Path to Wellness (Nutrigenomics) 01132022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Nourishing_Fertility_-_An_Expert’s_Secrets_Revealed_(Restorative_Formulations)_0.vtt" ;
                     ; be62f935-6a3e-467d-ae6d-6fe1ba3e037c ; Cell-to-Cell Chatter: Communication and Its Role in Human Health                                                                                                                        ; Identifying the root cause of health challenges can be difficult. Kim Stevens explores the gut as the foundation for human health, the intercellular and microbial communications that influence health, and the vast microbiome.       ; <p>The root cause of modern health challenges can be difficult to identify. Understanding that human health potential is intimately linked to cellular and microbial communication dynamics can help healthcare professionals find answers. Gut bacteria communicate and coordinate their activities through chemical signals, which affect everything from maintaining microbiota populations and the gut microenvironment to resisting infection. The bidirectional dialogue between human cells and microbiome cohabitants can also influence various downstream physiological signaling pathways.</p><br> <p>Join Kim Stevens in exploring the vastness of the microbiome and the importance of its terrain with respect to the gut being foundational to human health. Ms. Stevens will also examine the enormous, deeply rooted roles that intercellular and microbial communications play in modern health challenges.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; clinical-interventions-for-food-sensitivities ; clinical-interventions-for-food-sensitivities ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/o01lhk5v/brand-logo-ion.png ; brand-logo-ion ; Sponsor logo image for ION* ; ION ; 72f91c7f-3fdc-40ee-b8eb-42ef56858b09 ; 115,112,100,116,102 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Cell-to-Cell Chatter - Communication and Its Role in Human Health (ION) 10272022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Causes_and_Solutions_for_Noncancerous_Breast_Conditions_(Wellena)_11202023.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18
                     ; 045cfb9a-cf1f-4e8a-8c53-c4b344e77137 ; The Endocannabinoid System in Stress Response Regulation                                                                                                                                ; Dysregulation of the HPA axis can increase stress and induce widespread physiological changes. Tune in to understand how the ECS and the HPA axis interact and how CBD may help nurture ECS modulation to support homeostasis.          ; <p>Stress is a stealthy enemy. When chronic, it can induce widespread physiological changes. The endocannabinoid system (ECS) acts as a protective buffer against this adversary through its neuromodulatory action on the hypothalamic–pituitary–adrenal (HPA) axis.</p><br> <p>Join Dr. Meletis for this intriguing discussion of the latest science surrounding the stress response at the intersection of the ECS and HPA axis. Attendees will explore how nurturing the ECS modulates HPA axis activity toward homeostasis of stress hormones and how this impacts immune responsiveness, pain, and stress relief. The use of cannabidiol (CBD) and its impact on the ECS will be tied in with special emphasis on fear conditioning and mood changes.</p><br> <p>Some of the main learning areas of this webinar include:</p><br> <ul><li>How the HPA axis is intimately impacted by the ECS</li><li>The interplay between the microbiome and endocannabinoid receptors</li><li>Endocannabinoid deficiency and its relationship to immune and adrenal competence</li><li>How to support endocannabinoid tone</li><li>Clinical pearls to help guide and support ECS modulation</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; endocannabinoid-system-in-stress-response ; endocannabinoid-system-in-stress-response ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 7757fa5b-9b4e-4f3a-a612-37d982da03de ; 125 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/The Endocannabinoid System in Stress Response Regulation (TruGen3) 09082022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/The_Benefits_of_Moringa_-_Separating_Fact_from_Fiction_(Kuli_Kuli)_09092021_1.vtt" ;
                     ; 3a71b6e8-a70b-4353-9dd6-7d3affd35584 ; Nutritional Triage                                                                                                                                                                      ; Human physiology has evolved a “triage” response to micronutrient shortages in the body. Join James Doherty in examining the combination of nutritional supplements with whole food factors to support nutritional restoration.         ; <p>Human physiology has evolved a “triage” response to shortages of micronutrients. When a vitamin or mineral is scarce that vitamin or mineral is conserved for use by the proteins that are essential for short-term survival. This rationing is at the expense of proteins utilized for long-term health, like those that protect DNA. In this scenario, the triage response can be directly impacted through combining vitamins and minerals with whole-food factors, thus optimizing their availability and effectiveness.</p><br> <p>Join James Doherty for this thought-provoking examination of peer-reviewed studies that explore:</p><br> <ul><li>The scientific basis of Dr. Bruce Ames’ nutritional triage theory on vitamin/mineral availability and age-associated chronic disease</li><li>Why vitamin and mineral supplementation alone may be inadequate</li><li>Vital factors found in whole foods that can increase the effectiveness of vitamins and minerals</li><li>Scientific findings that support a broader definition of vitamins and minerals</li> <p>James will illustrate with examples from INNATE Response nutritional supplements, a premium line that delivers whole foods with added nutrients to support the body’s innate restorative processes.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; overfed-undernourished-meletis-trugen ; overfed-undernourished-meletis-trugen ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 0ea4e61e-bcc5-40fc-8769-5c012807b3cf ; 128 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Nutritional Triage (Innate) 08302022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Nutritional_Interventions_for_Accelerated_Aging_(Carlson_Labs)_07272023.vtt" ;
                     ; 3a736fc7-a72e-4882-acbd-0c31f7fc64c4 ; Histamine Metabolism Through the Lens of Gene and Nutrient Panels                                                                                                                       ; Excess histamine intake or poor histamine metabolism can be a root cause of various systemic symptoms. Tom Malterre shares his expertise in gene and nutrient panel interpretation for restoring histamine balance.                     ; <p>What is the connection between hives, post-nasal drip, intestinal issues, sleep disturbances, and anxiety? It may surprise some to know that excess histamine intake or poor histamine metabolism is often at the crux of these symptoms. What practitioners must determine is if foods are the main concern, if there are genetic variations or key nutrients deficiencies that are contributing to these challenges, or if there is an underlying issue, such as gut microbiome imbalance.</p><br> <p>Through examining hundreds of gene panels and thousands of nutrient analysis panels, Tom Malterre has become an expert in identifying often-overlooked connections. In this webinar, he will share his niche clinical experience and interpretive methods and bring to light proven protocols. Tom’s unique insights on histamine metabolism and the beneficial effects of restoring balance within this system bring new hope to patients with mysterious symptom constellations.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; histamine-metabolism-through-lens-of-gene ; histamine-metabolism-through-lens-of-gene ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 16f199c5-5039-47f4-9d6b-71de752f9c9c ; 100 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Histamine Metabolism Through the Lens of Gene and Nutrient Panels (Seeking Health) 08232022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Harnessing_Cellular_Senescence_(Neurohacker_Collective)_08032023.vtt" ;
                     ; b8302117-86c0-4a88-afae-d52d5d4257fa ; Grow a Strong Membership-Based Integrative Practice                                                                                                                                     ; Growing and maintaining a solid, membership-based integrative practice requires more than medical knowledge. Learn strategies to bolster your clinic to the pinnacle of success while preserving the highest level of patient care.     ; <p>Join us for a timely discussion on how to build an unshakeable foundation for your practice using proven methods. Practitioners will learn how to incorporate key value-added strategies and systems, decrease burnout, increase personal satisfaction, and infuse personal uniqueness into a practice. The implementation of Dr. Matteoli and Scott Rattigan’s methods will lay the groundwork for a successful integrative membership-based practice that supports its patients while pushing ahead of the competition.</p><br> <p>You will also learn:</p><br> <ul><li>The three primary patient appointments needed for streamlined practice efficiency</li>The six important documents that every patient should receive</li><li>Critical telemedicine best practices, including: <li>What to consider when practicing across state lines</li><li>How to safeguard a virtual practice</li></li><li>A unique and tested financial system that could result in significant tax savings</li><li>How to organize receivables and manage payables with confidence</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; grow-a-strong-membership-based-integrative-practice ; grow-a-strong-membership-based-integrative-practice ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; cf9312e5-896b-4bf9-b6aa-31f595a8bba8,a1c92d00-bbe8-4563-8cbb-e58d39824a56 ; 128 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Grow a Strong Membership-Based Integrative Practice (Origins Incubator) 08112022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Going_Green_-_The_Appeal_of_Phytonutrient-Rich_Green_Drinks_(Zahler)_08242023.vtt" ;
                     ; 3c5bc22b-93cf-4694-808a-5e9a6cbcec3b ; Finding Balance: The Power of Electrolytes                                                                                                                                              ; Maintaining electrolyte balance is crucial to physical performance levels. Tune in to understand the physiological roles of electrolytes and the severe impact their imbalance can have on bodily systems, especially GI function.      ; <p>Maintaining electrolyte balance is critical to physical performance. Understanding the physiological roles of electrolytes, including maintaining fluid balance, transmitting nerve impulses, and supporting involuntary muscle contraction as well as how their relative concentrations influence biochemistry, is essential for diagnosing problems that may be attributable to subclinical electrolyte imbalance. Individuals with too high or too low electrolyte concentrations commonly experience headaches, fatigue, or vague gastrointestinal issues, such as vomiting and diarrhea, and they sometimes experience more serious health problems. All of these can be triggered by factors that affect electrolyte balance, such as fluid loss due to intense exercise and adherence to strict, low-carb diets. In this dynamic webinar, biochemist, athlete, and self-proclaimed “nutrition tinkerer” Robb Wolf shares his personal health journey about how crippling GI issues in his 20s led to applying the science behind adopting a low-carb, ketogenic-style diet rich in electrolytes, which changed his life.</p><br> <p>The material covered will include:</p><br> <ul><li>Dietary, health, and lifestyle conditions that warrant increased electrolytes</li><li>Keto-induced metabolic changes resulting in electrolyte imbalance</li><li>The science behind safe electrolyte replacement strategies</li><li>The biochemistry of how sugar affects electrolyte absorption</li><li>The great salt debate—a close look at the science behind essential salt levels</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; finding-balance-power-of-electrolytes ; finding-balance-power-of-electrolytes ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 49ede820-c9d2-4ecd-8c93-44b96f26474f ; 103,115,111 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Finding Balance - The Power of Electrolytes (LMNT) 07282022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Fibroid_Causation_and_Treatment_-_An_Integrative_Approach_(XYMOGEN)_03222022_1.vtt" ;
                     ; b822cf19-5c1f-47d7-9d86-7aaba9fd5458 ; Telomeres and Immune Senescence                                                                                                                                                         ; Telomeres are linked to cellular aging, and slowing the natural shortening of telomeres can greatly impact health status. Dr. Joseph Raffaele discusses how activating telomerase through supplementation can support immune health.    ; <p>An understanding of the link between telomeres, the protein structures that protect and maintain the integrity of DNA, and cellular aging has continued to evolve since first being observed in the 1930s. Telomere length is an indicator of health status and biological age, with shorter telomeres being associated with dysfunction and cellular aging, including the aging of immune cells. The benefit of slowing or potentially reversing the natural shortening of telomeres has therefore become an area of great interest.</p><br> <p>Join Dr. Raffaele as he shares his expertise in telomere biology and describes a means for activating telomerase, an enzyme that has been shown to lengthen telomeres and improve immune health biomarkers in humans.</p><br> <p>In this webinar, Dr. Raffaele will review:</p><br> <ul><li>The correlation between telomere length and immune health</li><li>The significance of telomere biology to overall health</li>The evidence base for and the most recent studies on telomerase activation</li><li>Lab markers that can be used to assess epigenetic age and immune cell health</li><li>How to incorporate supplements for telomere support into treatment plans</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; cellular-senescence-and-the-anti-aging-power-of-senolytics ; cellular-senescence-and-the-anti-aging-power-of-senolytics ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 4ef5dbac-4db2-4f00-87b3-e9737ee98ed3 ; 116,100 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Telomeres and Immune Senescence (T.A. Sciences) 06162022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Targeting_the_Trilogy_of_Memory_Loss_(Cognitive_Clarity)_03082022-.vtt" ;
                     ; 6e39f9f9-c09c-40f0-9472-96caf55ac838 ; Natural Therapies and Male Hormones: The Untapped Potential                                                                                                                             ; Hormone balance is a focus of women’s health, but how does hormone imbalance impact male physiological processes? Tune in to understand how botanical therapies can bolster male sex hormones and support men’s overall well-being.     ; <p>Hormone balance is vital for overall health and well-being. Fluctuations in hormones can affect a range of physiological processes and result in changes to weight, libido, energy, and cognition. Although maintaining hormone equilibrium may be more frequently discussed in regard to women’s health, male hormone modulation can safely and effectively contribute to an improved quality of life in individuals with unbalanced hormone levels.</p><br> <p>Join naturopathic physician Cheryl Burdette as she shares her discerning clinical insights and taps into the potential of botanical therapies for modulating sex hormones. The highlights will include:</p><br> <ul><li>An evidence-based review of the safety and efficacy of botanicals that modulate testosterone, estrogen, progesterone, and sex hormone binding globulin</li><li>An evaluation of underlying supportive systems such as adrenal and thyroid and their influence on reproductive hormones</li><li>A review of testosterone metabolism and the management of dihydrotestosterone, another male sex hormone</li><li>A review of common hormone testing profiles and how to evaluate results</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; male-hormones ; male-hormones ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 117,118 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Natural Therapies and Male Hormones - The Untapped Potential (XYMOGEN) 05192022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Natural_Testosterone_Management_(XYMOGEN)_10262021_1.vtt" ;
                     ; 45742f56-8a9d-4efd-ba31-4411c085b575 ; Is Mushroom Extract a Match for HPV?                                                                                                                                                    ; High-risk strains of the human papillomavirus (HPV) are the primary cause of infections leading to cervical and other cancers. Join Dr. Judith Smith to learn how mushroom extract can help the body dispel high-risk HPV infections.   ; <p>Almost 100% of cervical cancers are associated with the human papillomavirus (HPV). High-risk strains of HPV can lead to persistent infections that progress to cervical and other cancers. The relationship between HPV and its potential to progress to cervical cancer is better understood due to a growing body of research, and now a prospective means for clearing high-risk HPV infection is emerging.</p><br> <p>Join renowned HPV researcher Dr. Judith Smith for a summary of her pioneering research into the use of a mushroom extract to modulate the host immune system and help the body dispel high-risk HPV infections. You will not want to miss this webinar in which Dr. Smith will explain:</p><br> <ul><li>What is high-risk HPV and who is at risk?</li><li>HPV and progression to cancer</li><li>The evaluation and impact of mushroom extract on HPV host immunity</li><li>Lifestyle modifications, key nutrients, and botanical compounds for immune support</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; mushroom-extract ; mushroom-extract ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; cff2f519-c82b-4892-a40b-199060e09dbf ; 130 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Is Mushroom Extract a Match for HPV (American BioSciences) 05102022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver,_How_XYMOGEN_Sharpens_Your_Aim_-_Part_II_(XYMOGEN)_0907202.vtt" ;
                     ; 6290e8ed-4fc7-4e61-82fe-e5ab44283eca ; The Real Scoop on Collagen Supplementation                                                                                                                                              ; Collagen comprises 30% of the body’s protein, making it vital for skin elasticity and joint flexibility, mobility, and functionality. Tune in to learn the importance of incorporating collagen supplementation into treatment plans.   ; <p>Collagen is one of the most important substances in the body, comprising 30% of total protein. As we age, the biosynthesis of collagen begins to decline. In addition, intakes of dietary collagen are typically low throughout a person’s lifetime. These factors contribute to an overall reduction in collagen, which is associated with loosening and thinning of the skin, reduction of joint flexibility, and a gradual decrease in joint mobility and functionality. Collagen supplementation is a viable option to counter the effects of declining collagen.</p><br> <p>Join Ayla Barmmer and Jake Kocinski for a deep dive into collagen science. Focus with be given to:</p><br> <ul><li>Examining the uniqueness of bioactive collagen peptides</li><li>Reviewing related scientific literature</li><li>Learning how to incorporate collagen peptides into patient treatment plans</li></ul> <p>The presenters will also discuss Vital Proteins® Professional, a clinically proven bioactive collagen peptide line of products. This new line was developed by a team of leading functional nutrition experts and is available exclusively through healthcare professionals.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; the-real-scoop-of-collagen ; the-real-scoop-of-collagen ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; fa87ec35-2395-4a2e-b611-c163397e0310,a1db3739-0503-426d-b0d6-846044d1ad8a ; 103,126 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/The Real Scoop on Collagen Supplementation (Vital Proteins) 05042022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/The_Global_Health_Effects_of_Climate_Change_-_Raising_Awareness_Through_Fact_and.vtt" ;
                     ; 3a08c261-626c-454f-b362-9bbd8e01bb87 ; What’s in Your Mushroom Supplement?                                                                                                                                                     ; Mushrooms can be integral in achieving whole-body wellness, but their supplemental forms vary. Explore these health-supporting allies with Dr. Mark Kaylor as he provides a roadmap for choosing the right mushroom supplement.         ; <p>There is a wide array of qualitative differences between similar mushroom supplements. It can be tricky for healthcare professionals to know that they are prescribing the right mushroom, that it’s in a bioavailable form, and that it contains the anticipated range of active constituents. Join Mark Kaylor for an in-depth discussion on medicinal mushrooms—from raw materials to finished products—and heighten your mushroom knowledge!</p><br> <p>Medicinal mushrooms are amazing, health-supporting allies, and the information in this webinar will enable healthcare professionals to confidently recommend formulas that possess the full spectrum of healing gifts that mushrooms offer.</p><br> <p>In this discussion, Mark will cover:</p><br> <ul><li>The intricacies of mushroom ingredient development</li><li>How to choose a quality mushroom product and why it matters</li><li>The fundamental health and healing qualities of widely prescribed medicinal mushrooms</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; mushroom-supplement ; mushroom-supplement ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; df9468eb-3258-4dd0-957f-4d1c148b7be3 ; 100 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/What’s in Your Mushroom Supplement (Mushroom Wisdom) 04122022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Turmeric_and_Curcumin_-_Clinical_Advances_(NaturPro_Scientific)_05062021_1.vtt" ;
                     ; 55a3a99a-e467-4ee2-9238-fdaa2a7b25e3 ; Nourishing Fertility: An Expert’s Secrets Revealed                                                                                                                                      ; Struggling with fertility is not uncommon, and the more we discuss it, the more we can understand it. Learn firsthand how to help combat fertility challenges and what nutrients best support conception.                               ; <p>Infertility issues affect one in every six couples. These are devastating, and treatment is expensive. Couples who are struggling with infertility often want to be assured that they are doing everything possible to improve their chances of becoming pregnant the old-fashioned way. Fueling their bodies with nutrient-rich foods and cultivating healthy lifestyle habits are two controllable factors that can greatly benefit couples who are experiencing fertility challenges.</p><br> <p>Join naturopathic doctor Aumatma Shah for an information-filled webinar. She will share tidbits from her best-selling book Fertility Secrets: What your Doctor Didn’t Tell You About Baby-Making and discuss:</p><br> <ul><li>Factors that contribute to infertility</li><li>Dietary and lifestyle habits to preserve and fuel fertility</li><li>Clinical pearls from her own experiences with infertility patients</li><li>Recommendations for evidence-based nutrients and herbs that support conception</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; nourishing-fertility ; nourishing-fertility ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 6b606cef-fb7b-40a7-a147-c4c13b61b7b5 ; 117,118 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Nourishing Fertility - An Expert’s Secrets Revealed (Restorative Formulations) 04072022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver,_How_XYMOGEN_Sharpens_Your_Aim_-_Part_II_(XYMOGEN)_1221202.vtt" ;
                     ; 706f0b70-abfe-4144-bae9-71f80cc27231 ; A Breakthrough in Diabetes Care                                                                                                                                                         ; Diabetes, the largest epidemic of the 21st century, too often leads to a lifetime of struggle against potentially life-threatening complications. Learn about diabetes interventions and how to incorporate a more natural approach.    ; <p>Cardiovascular disease, stroke, kidney failure, retinopathy, neuropathy, cognitive impairment, functional disability, amputations, and heart failure: these diabetes complications are on the rise! It is therefore no surprise that diabetes mellitus has been named the largest epidemic of the 21st century.</p> <br> <p>Much has been learned in the past decade about diabetes interventions, including the impacts of various classes of medications. Prof. Raz Itamar has been a leader in this research. In this revealing webinar, he will share his vast knowledge and provide an in-depth look at the efficacy and safety of diabetes medications as well as the use of integrative therapies. You will gain an even greater clinical understanding of how to act early and safely to achieve your own breakthroughs in the care of diabetes patients.</p> <br> <p>Topics include:</p> <ul><li>The need for early diagnosis</li><li>The importance of normalizing blood glucose levels</li><li>Information on hypoglycemic drugs with cardiorenal protection</li><li>How to successfully implement an integrative model</li><li>A natural approach to type 2 diabetes with real-world data</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; diabetes-breakthrough ; diabetes-breakthrough ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 3e3161ac-9c93-4ad9-87b6-337fac1d406f ; 119 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/A Breakthrough in Diabetes Care (CuraLife) 03302022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/A_Breakthrough_in_Diabetes_Care_(CuraLife)_03302022_1.vtt" ;
                     ; 558fdb66-1eee-4aed-8702-115f4cf1c110 ; Dietary Nitrates, Nitric Oxide, and Heart Health                                                                                                                                        ; Hypertension is commonly known as the “silent killer” due to the significant impact of high blood pressure on the human body. Tune in to learn how nitric oxide can decrease blood pressure and benefit heart health.                   ; <p>Nearly half of the adult population in the United States has hypertension, a major risk factor for cardiovascular disease and the leading cause of mortality. There are many physiological factors involved in the maintenance of healthy blood pressure, one of which is the presence of an endogenously produced cellular signaling molecule called nitric oxide (NO). The predominant pathway for the generation of NO is the conversion of dietary nitrate to nitrite, a transformation that ultimately results in biologically active NO. The dietary consumption of foods that enhance NO production, such as dark leafy greens and beets, is often inadequate, a factor that has been correlated with low plasma NO levels and endothelial dysfunction.</p> <br> <p>Join Penny Kris-Etherton, renowned author and professor of nutritional science, as she reviews the literature about the discovery of NO as a signaling molecule, the recommended ways of increasing NO, and the importance of NO in clinical care. Dr. Kris-Etherton will highlight the research linking increases in dietary nitrate levels to decreases in blood pressure and make a case for the consumption of foods that boost NO production to benefit heart health.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; dietary-nitrates ; dietary-nitrates ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 63ac594d-4507-4917-9f43-4d9eaf8f67f7 ; 105 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Dietary Nitrates, Nitric Oxide, and Heart Health (HumanN) 03222022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Chronic_Bacterial_and_Viral_Diseases_-_Clinical_and_Laboratory_Diagnosis_and_Eff.vtt" ;
                     ; 5596d178-d768-4df9-8080-5e5e59eb2500 ; Fibroid Causation and Treatment: An Integrative Approach                                                                                                                                ; A great majority of women will develop and suffer from uterine fibroids in their lifetime. Tune in as Dr. Allan Warshowsky outlines how to address the underlying imbalances and systemic dysfunction that can lead to fibroids.        ; <p>It’s estimated that 70% to 80% of women will develop uterine fibroids in their lifetime. They can vary in size and number, and while usually benign, fibroids can swell a woman’s uterus to the size of a basketball and cause an array of symptoms, such as: </p> <br> <ul><li>Heavy and prolonged menstrual bleeding</li><li>Bleeding between periods</li><li>Pelvic pain</li><li>Bladder infections</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Backache or leg pains</li><li>Infertility</li></ul><p>Fibroids are the leading reason why women undergo hysterectomies. While many doctors recommend surgery as the answer, Dr. Allan Warshowsky, author and fibroid expert, has developed an innovative program that brings new hope for less invasive fibroid treatment. He combines Western medicine and holistic sciences to address the underlying imbalances and systemic dysfunction that can lead to fibroids and the significant health issues associated with them. You don’t want to miss this important webinar and Dr. Warshowsky’s guided tour through the natural treatment of fibroids.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; fibroid-causation ; fibroid-causation ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; d9315525-11e2-46e4-9e70-d743f018e260 ; 117 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Fibroid Causation and Treatment - An Integrative Approach (XYMOGEN) 03222022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Exploring_the_Promise_of_Red_Light_Therapy_(Fringe)_04252024.vtt" ;
                     ; 853088fb-5173-4f5f-8e8a-565200ad41be ; Targeting the Trilogy of Memory Loss                                                                                                                                                    ; The aging process affects the strength and longevity of the body and the mind. Renowned brain aging and Alzheimer’s researcher Dr. Alan Snow reviews how to incorporate natural protocols to support healthy brain aging.               ; <p>What are the real reasons we lose memory as we age? Join Dr. Alan Snow, renowned brain aging and Alzheimer’s disease researcher, for a deep dive into critical advancements in the understanding of neurodegenerative structures associated with brain-aging and the natural discoveries that address them. For 30 years, Dr. Snow has led research teams to pursue the most effective plant-based ingredients to target these structures and support the aging brain.</p><br><p>During this webinar, Dr. Snow will: </p><br><ul><li>Review over 15 years of his research into cat’s claw (Uncaria tomentosa) and discovery of the PTI-00703 extract</li><li>Educate about the role of beta-amyloid fibrils (brain plaques) and paired helical filaments (tau tangles) in age-related memory loss and how PTI-00703 cat’s claw interacts with them</li><li>Examine the recent publication that demonstrates the superior performance of PTI-00703 cat’s claw compared to other brain-aging ingredients</li></ul><p>You won’t want to miss this research and data-packed webinar that has the potential to be immediately useful as well as relevant to many of the patients you see daily, not to mention friends and family. Dr Snow will also discuss ways to incorporate natural oral nootropic products, with examples that include Percepta Professional, into patient protocols for healthy brain aging.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; targeting-memory-loss ; targeting-memory-loss ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; ec2a5050-996d-4531-8564-94c82fe89006 ; 112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Targeting the Trilogy of Memory Loss (Cognitive Clarity) 03082022-.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Spotlight_on_XYMOGEN_Series_-_Part_I_(XYMOGEN)_01252024.vtt" ;
                     ; 14a64a0d-6e77-4ada-8b97-efeebfe268be ; Prenatal Nutrition: Setting the Stage for a Healthy Pregnancy and Outcome                                                                                                               ; Prenatal nutrition is critical to the healthy development of the baby and the overall well-being of the mother. Take a deep dive into the world of prenatal supplements and learn which nutrients are vital to a healthy pregnancy.     ; <p>It is well-known that prenatal nutrition sets the foundation for a healthy pregnancy outcome for both mother and baby. With so many prenatal supplement options available, what are the criteria for choosing the right supplement? Why is the right prenatal selection crucial for mom’s health and baby’s development? Join Kenn Israel, a respected 30-year veteran of the natural products industry, for a presentation with unique insights into the importance of prenatal vitamins and which nutrients are critical.</p><br><p>Kenn will share his broad depth of knowledge on formulating prenatal products and focus on what to look for regarding quality and efficacy. This webinar will also provide an opportunity to gain an understanding of the rationale for the optimal prenatal formulations offered by Zahler, a novel brand with a strong history of leadership in the formulation of evidence-based dietary supplements. Key topics covered will include: </p><br> <ul><li>Folate versus folic acid</li><li>Benefits of DHA for both mom and baby</li><li>Other important prenatal nutrients</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; prenatal-nutrition ; prenatal-nutrition ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 0b1e0a7f-7976-46a8-8614-764224a37ba0 ; 117,127 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Prenatal Nutrition - Setting the Stage for a Healthy Pregnancy and Outcome (Zahler) 02282022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Powered_by_the_Hive_and_Backed_by_Science_-_Using_Bee_Products_to_Support_Wellne.vtt" ;
                     ; 021f2c8b-4e3b-4310-9a16-3f6efb6734cf ; The Global Health Effects of Climate Change: Raising Awareness Through Fact and Fiction                                                                                                 ; Climate change has been linked to a decline in biodiversity and can also impact ecological balance. Dr. Richard Horowitz discusses global climate change and how the loss of biodiversity is increasing tick-borne disorders.           ; <p>Biodiversity is the coexistence of species within their ecosystems and is necessary to sustain life. Biodiversity loss is driven by factors such as humans destroying habitats through unsustainable farming and overfishing as well as factors like pollution, pesticides, and the introduction of non-native species. Climate change has now been linked to an observed decline in biodiversity.</p><br><p>Dr. Richard Horowitz may be best known as a pioneer in the fight against tick-borne disorders, but he is also passionate about biodiversity and the potential effects of its decline on global health. He is the author of a sci-fi adventure novel that illuminates the science, identifies the problems, and offers practical solutions for our unprecedented climate emergency.</p><br><p>Guiding us through the discovery of unique and novel concepts that raise awareness, Dr. Horowitz will help us prepare for the global health effects of climate change. During this provocative two-hour webinar, he will offer his insights into: </p><br><ul><li>The effects of climate change on rising levels of tick-borne disorders</li><li>How environmental toxicity is linked to global climate change</li><li>Global climate change science merged with a preview of the mythological parables from his book Starseed R/evolution: The Awakening </li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; global-health-effects-of-climate-change ; global-health-effects-of-climate-change ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 36066998-d75e-4e22-83bd-53a416b5e22f ; 128 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/The Global Health Effects of Climate Change - Raising Awareness Through Fact and Fiction 02232022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/The_Endocannabinoid_System_in_Stress_Response_Regulation_(TruGen3)_09082022_1.vtt" ;
                     ; 17f84173-b850-4ea0-bded-bdf881947e53 ; The Science and Clinical Application of Collagen Peptides                                                                                                                               ; Dietary intake of collagen-rich foods is generally low, but collagen can still be naturally replenished. Join Jeffrey Bland, PhD, and Jake Kocinski, RD, to delve into the science and clinical applications of collagen peptides.      ; <p>Collagen is the most abundant structural protein in the body, making up approximately 30% of total protein composition. Bones, joints, muscles, tendons, ligaments, and the skin are some of the tissues that are dependent upon collagen for their structure. As dietary intake of collagen-rich foods is typically low in the general population, many people use collagen supplements to stimulate collagen production or to replenish age-related collagen loss. Compared to other forms of supplemental collagen, peptides have a lower molecular weight, which contributes to their easy digestion, absorption, and increased bioavailability.</p><br><p>You will not want to miss functional medicine legend Dr. Jeffrey Bland joined by registered dietitian and collagen expert Jake Kocinski as they delve into the science and clinical applications of collagen. This dynamic webinar will cover: </p><br> <ul><li>The fundamentals of collagen and uniqueness of collagen peptides</li><li>An evidence-based review of the scientific collagen peptide literature to date</li><li>How to integrate collagen peptides into a patient’s treatment plan</li><li>A Q and A session</li></ul> <p>Vital Proteins® Professional, a new product line exclusive to practitioners, will also be introduced with recommendations on how to incorporate this group of products into clinical protocols for targeted patient benefits.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; science-and-clinical-application-of-peptides ; science-and-clinical-application-of-peptides ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 3de92961-2ccd-4883-8c45-2c1bf8b61f5e,a1db3739-0503-426d-b0d6-846044d1ad8a ; 103,126 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/The Science and Clinical Application of Collagen Peptides (Vital Proteins) 01182022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/The_Role_of_Bioactive_Colloidal_Silver_in_Gut_Health_-_A_Homeopathic_View_(Natur.vtt" ;
                     ; 4b82adfd-b23d-47ae-9fd0-022f088bf620 ; The Role of Bioactive Colloidal Silver in Gut Health: A Homeopathic View                                                                                                                ; The gut microbiome is a finely tuned microbial community that helps maintain bacterial symbiosis and overall wellness. Learn how bioactive colloidal silver benefits gut health during dysbiosis and affects microbiome diversity.      ; <p>The microbiome encompasses a vast ecosystem, including diverse bacterial species that maintain symbiosis with their human host and are credited with influencing overall wellness. Research on the microbiota of the gut has revealed a role in digestion, nutrient metabolism, immune health, gut mucosal barrier integrity, and much more. When the finely tuned microbial community in the gut becomes unbalanced, a host of uncomfortable symptoms and health issues can result.</p><br><p>Join homeopathic practitioner Robert Scott Bell as he considers the role of colloidal silver in supporting gut health. You will learn: </p><br> <ul><li>The potential use of silver hydrosol in gut dysbiosis and overall wellness</li><li>The effect of silver on microbiome diversity</li><li>The importance of nanotechnology for absorption and excretion of metals</li><li>The history, safety, and clinical efficacy of a professional bioactive silver formulation</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; disease-begins-in-the-gut_-but-often-doesn-t-stay-there ; disease-begins-in-the-gut_-but-often-doesn-t-stay-there ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; ce91b804-90e4-4ac2-b93a-23da1eebf272 ; 115 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/The Role of Bioactive Colloidal Silver in Gut Health - A Homeopathic View (Natural Immunogenics) 01112022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/The_Real_Scoop_on_Collagen_Supplementation_(Vital_Proteins)_05042022_1.vtt" ;
                     ; 84fb2316-f54d-420d-af0f-481487517da0 ; Powered by the Hive and Backed by Science: Using Bee Products to Support Wellness                                                                                                       ; Bees are an integral part of the global ecosystem, but bee products can be equally beneficial to the human body. Learn about the medicinal properties of bee products and their benefits to the body, inside and out.                   ; <p>If asked the question, “What do bees make?” most people would answer “honey,” but the fact is that the fruit of a bee’s labor also includes many other useful substances. Bee products have been consumed as a food source and used for a wide range of medicinal purposes since ancient times. In addition to sustaining a role in traditional medicine, bee products have been subjected to modern laboratory and clinical investigations, and a wide body of evidence has emerged supporting the benefits, ranging from an inhibitory effect on various species of bacteria to topical application for wound healing. With hundreds of naturally occurring compounds that vary depending on the plants on which the bees feed, the complex chemical composition of bee products makes them well suited as modern and accessible remedies.</p><br><p>Join bee product experts Carly Stein and Daniel Clark as they share their knowledge about sustainable beekeeping, the power of bee products, and the science behind it all. You will learn about: </p><br> <ul><li>Propolis – the defender of the hive</li><li>Bee pollen – the hive’s nutrient powerhouse</li><li>Royal jelly – the brain-boosting food of the queen bee</li><li>Honey – nature’s most delicious remedy</li><li>The role of bee products in supporting wellness</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; powered-by-the-hive ; powered-by-the-hive ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; d6abc4e5-0cfc-4bc7-a945-9308b8ef1640,622b703f-beff-401b-9fbd-cc5310e16461 ; 128 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Powered by the Hive and Backed by Science - Using Bee Products to Support Wellness (Beekeeper's Naturals) 12072021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver,_How_XYMOGEN_Sharpens_Your_Aim_-_Part_II_(XYMOGEN)_1109202.vtt" ;
                     ; c769d71c-ccaa-40d3-a680-8f8d3c0408e6 ; Overview: Natural Approaches to Mental Health                                                                                                                                           ; Mental health disorders don’t discriminate based on age, gender, or ethnicity. Tune in to learn how naturopathic, holistic treatments can help address the root cause of mental health disorders, not simply treat the symptoms.        ; <p>According to the National Alliance on Mental Illness, approximately one in five American adults and one in six youth ages 6 through 17 experience a mental health disorder each year. These staggering statistics encompass a broad range of symptoms that affect a person’s thinking, feeling, or mood and potentially impact a person’s ability to relate to others and perform daily functions. Naturopathic management of mental health employs holistic treatment of the whole person, addressing the root cause and the multiple factors that can lead to the deterioration of emotional well-being versus just treating the symptoms.</p><br><p>Join naturopathic doctor Philip Rouchotas for this webinar presentation full of concise clinical guidance based on natural approaches to mental health. Dr. Rouchatas will cover current best practices in intake, diagnosis, prescription interactions, and natural health remedies.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; natural-approaches-to-mental-health ; natural-approaches-to-mental-health ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 17040002-5680-4356-8d1c-bf25169ff2ef ; 112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Overview - Natural Approaches to Mental Health (NFH) 11302021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Overfed_Yet_Undernourished_-_Optimizing_Nutrient_Intakes_(TruGen3)_08172023.vtt" ;
                     ; 7e9e120b-1508-499c-9f7d-4f4077366af4 ; Probiotic Use for Support of Urovaginal Health                                                                                                                                          ; Probiotic use can extend beyond just balancing the gut microflora. Learn how probiotics help promote an optimal balance in the female urovaginal microbiome.                                                                            ; <p>The microbiome has garnered the attention of the scientific community in recent years with a plethora of published research that supports the efficacy of probiotic use to balance gut microflora. But did you know that the microbiome and the research that supports alterations with probiotic use extend beyond the gut to other areas of the body, including the vagina and urogenital area? Internal and external influences, including stress, unhealthy diet, food sensitivities, antibiotics, and environmental factors, can disturb the balance of this finely tuned microbial community. In fact, most women will experience vaginal dysbiosis and symptoms of microflora imbalance at some point in their lifetime.</p><br><p>Join industry veteran Dominique Ostrander as she shares her knowledge about probiotics and their role in promoting optimal balance of the urovaginal microbiome. Key topics covered will include: </p><br> <ul><li>Prophylactic use of probiotics to support urovaginal health</li><li>The primary causes of vaginal dysbiosis and adjuvant probiotic therapy</li><li>How to distinguish evidence-based probiotic claims from unsubstantiated marketing claims</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; probiotic-use-urovaginal ; probiotic-use-urovaginal ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 1847bb71-dc65-46c4-bccf-b17787aa1912 ; 113,115,117 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Probiotic Use for Support of Urovaginal Health (Jarrow Formulas) 11162021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Prenatal_Nutrition_-_Setting_the_Stage_for_a_Healthy_Pregnancy_and_Outcome_(Zahl.vtt" ;
                     ; e42f5c77-caa8-42e5-8f64-4ec75b24ed83 ; A Practitioner’s Guide to the Utilization of Slow-Release Dihydroquercetin                                                                                                              ; Dihydroquercetin (DHQ) is an antioxidant-rich plant flavonoid with more powerful, longer-lasting antioxidant effects than quercetin. Take a journey to better understand slow-release DHQ and how to unlock its botanical benefits.     ; <p>Dihydroquercetin (DHQ) is an antioxidant-rich plant flavonoid commonly found in onions, grapes, green tea, olive oil, and the bark of conifer trees. It has a similar structure to the more commonly known quercetin but with two additional hydrogen atoms which are said to render DHQ a more powerful and longer-lasting antioxidant with an alterative effect. An “alterative effect” means that a constituent may have a secondary action that gradually complements the body’s primary function to restore health and vitality.</p><br><p>You do not want to miss this dynamic webinar with naturopathic doctor Martin Milner as he shares his insights into the biochemistry, pharmacology, indications, contraindications, and varying dosages and delivery forms for the utilization of slow-release DHQ. Dr. Milner will discuss the clinical application of DHQ and its mechanism of action in a range of functions from cardiovascular support to immune modulation. You will learn: </p><br><ul><li>What defines a botanical alterative and adaptogen and the plausibility of DHQ for these actions</li><li>The mechanism of action, rationale, and contraindications for use of supplemental DHQ compared to quercetin in the management of various disorders</li><li>The strengths, weaknesses, and challenges that accompany the implementation and management of a DHQ protocol</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; dihydroquercetin ; dihydroquercetin ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; da4fe670-8950-47a8-8435-f1bee00fc690 ; 100,105,102 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/A Practitioner’s Guide to the Utilization of Slow-Release Dihydroquercetin (Endurance Products) 11022021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/A_Holistic_Approach_to_Managing_the_Menstrual_Cycle_–_A_Woman’s_Fifth_Vital_Sign.vtt" ;
                     ; fa155e54-fdb7-4c2b-9e7c-e2212d88d46a ; Natural Testosterone Management                                                                                                                                                         ; Testosterone is a crucial hormone for men and women that can impact weight, energy, libido, and cognition. Join Dr. Cheryl Burdette as she incorporates the use of botanicals as a natural form of testosterone management.             ; <p>Testosterone is a vital hormone for overall health and well-being. As we age, testosterone production wanes, affecting a range of physiological processes resulting in changes that can include weight gain, lack of energy, decreased libido, and cognitive decline. However, there are steps that can be taken to naturally manage testosterone levels and potentially stave off the undesirable results of its decline.</p><br><p>You do not want to miss this webinar hosted by naturopathic physician Cheryl Burdette as she shares her clinical insights into the natural management of testosterone. Dr. Burdette will evaluate the roles of diet, exercise, stress response, and the microbiome as they relate to maintaining appropriate testosterone levels. The highlights will include: </p><br><ul><li>An evidence-based review of the safety and efficacy of phytoandrogen use</li><li>Recent data developments for selective androgen receptor modulators (SARMS)</li><li>The use of botanicals as adjuncts to bioidentical hormones</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; nat-testosterone-mng ; nat-testosterone-mng ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 117,118 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Natural Testosterone Management (XYMOGEN) 10262021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Moringa_the_Miracle_Tree_-_What_is_the_Scientific_Evidence_(Kuli_Kuli)_08312023.vtt" ;
                     ; 83860ef1-1b9b-4b16-a2ab-b12582c5605a ; Small Intestinal Dysbiosis: Understanding the SIBO Matrix                                                                                                                               ; A healthy GI tract plays a significant role in gut microbiome balance, and SIBO can cause considerable GI discomfort. Tune in to learn how to clinically manage the SIBO matrix and retain normal GI function and balance.              ; <p>A normally functioning gastrointestinal (GI) tract can control microbiome balance in the small and large intestines through various mechanisms. However, circumstances such as antibiotics, disease, or surgery can slow the passage of food and waste and create a breeding ground for microbiome bacteria that can lead to excess bacterial growth. Small intestinal bacteria overgrowth (SIBO) occurs when bacteria normally found in the colon have proliferated in the small intestine causing abdominal discomfort and a range of GI symptoms.</p><br><p>Join internationally recognized SIBO expert Dr. Nirala Jacobi to gain an understanding of the breakdown of gut-protective mechanisms that can lead to acute, chronic, or relapsing SIBO. Dr. Jacobi will dive deep into the underlying causes of SIBO, such as: </p><br><ul><li>Dysmotility and other enteric nervous system dysfunction</li><li>Dysbiosis and hysteresis</li><li>Digestive deficits and immune dysfunction</li><li>Structural defects</li></ul><p>This webinar will offer participants insight into the intricate workings of the small intestinal microbiome that impact the SIBO matrix and how to manage them clinically.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; disease-begins-in-the-gut_-but-often-doesn-t-stay-there ; disease-begins-in-the-gut_-but-often-doesn-t-stay-there ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 661575fb-7ce1-4216-a83a-c95fc2307e9a ; 115 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Small Intestinal Dysbiosis - Understanding the SIBO Matrix (The Biome Clinic) 10222021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Arrows_in_Your_Quiver,_How_XYMOGEN_Sharpens_Your_Aim_-_Part_II_(XYMOGEN)_0718202.vtt" ;
                     ; 1733853a-0af6-4941-9518-e7ab09ec4cb9 ; A Whole Systems Approach to Influencing the Physiological Impact of Stress                                                                                                              ; Stress plays a role in the pathology and exacerbation of many health conditions, yet it is not often considered in treatment protocols. Dr. Cheryl Burdette examines the impact of stress and clinical protocols for its management.    ; <p><b>Stress plays a role in the pathology and exacerbation of many health conditions. However, stress management is regularly overlooked and often not considered a critical part of treatment protocols.</b>Stress can aggravate skin and gastrointestinal issues and lead to an increased risk for cardiovascular conditions and certain immunocompromised states: yet, it <b>is seldom regarded as a treatable symptom with potentially adverse effects on overall health and wellness.</b>Regardless of the source of a patient’s stress, key endpoints are useful for evaluating the effects of stress and practical, common tools are imperative to managing the extremes of stress.</p><br><p>Join Dr. Cheryl Burdette for an informative presentation that will examine the impact of stress on the cardiovascular, endocrine, and immune systems. Dr. Burdette will highlight: </p><br> <ul><li>Research demonstrating the influence of stress at the cellular and telomere levels</li><li>How stress manifests in common conditions associated with aging</li><li>Clinical protocols to counteract an environment of emotional, physical, and biochemical stressors</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; unraveling-trauma-and-ptsd-natural-adjuncts-of-support ; unraveling-trauma-and-ptsd-natural-adjuncts-of-support ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 23017e30-7dba-4209-9808-ab0533ddc0b3 ; 105,116,100,101,125 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/A Whole Systems Approach to Influencing the Physiological Impact of Stress (XYMOGEN) 10202022_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/A_Practitioner’s_Guide_to_the_Utilization_of_Slow-Release_Dihydroquercetin_(Endu.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_01,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_04,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_28,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_16,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_27,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_24,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_29,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_22
                     ; 961aee88-5802-4742-9ee2-1a364fb55685 ; Mood, Mind, and Memory: The Critical Role of DHA and Lutein in Brain Health                                                                                                             ; The aging process causes a reduction in brain size, interfering with cognition and eye health. Dr. Michael Nelson discusses how DHA and targeted supplements can support neurologic function and overall brain and eye wellness.        ; <p>A reduction in the overall size of the brain occurs as part of the aging process, a phenomenon that is directly related to the storage of fat in the brain. The predominant essential fatty acid found in brain tissue is docosahexaenoic acid (DHA), which comprises about 90% of the essential fatty acid in the brain and ~20% of its total lipid content. The prevalence of DHA in brain tissue ranks it among the most crucial molecules for determining the brain’s integrity and ability to perform.</p><br><p>Another factor affecting neurological function is oxidative stress. An overproduction of free radicals can cause cellular damage to fatty brain tissues, but antioxidant chaperones play a role in counteracting this process. A bioaccumulation of the carotenoid lutein has been associated with antioxidant benefits that protect DHA from oxidation.</p><br><p>Join doctor of chiropractic care Michael Nelson for an informative webinar highlighting the role of DHA and the carotenoid lutein in supporting neurological function throughout the life span. The key points Dr. Nelson will highlight include: </p><br> <ul><li>How DHA and lutein support blood-brain barrier integrity and cellular health in the central nervous system</li><li>The correlation between intake of lutein and macular pigmentation</li><li>The use of eye exams to predict early onset of neurodegenerative conditions</li><li>Targeted supplements to support brain and eye health</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; mood-mind-and-memory ; mood-mind-and-memory ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; d4ad9563-f016-411f-8e87-8fc7aceafec9 ; 112 ; "Mood, Mind, and Memory: The Critical Role of DHA and Lutein in Brain Health" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Melatonin_-_Beyond_Sleep_(Symphony_Natural_Health)_11082023.vtt" ;
                     ; a410c94c-be05-468a-ba81-091f0877cae3 ; A Holistic Approach to Managing the Menstrual Cycle – A Woman’s Fifth Vital Sign                                                                                                        ; Understanding a woman’s menstrual cycle is vital to diagnosing various health disorders. Tune in as Dr. Stephanie Nishek explains how to use the menstrual cycle as a tool in a holistic approach to health and wellness.               ; <p>The menstrual cycle is a key indicator of a woman’s health. From irregularity to a heavy flow and associated pain, this essential cycle offers insight into a variety of health conditions. This is why the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists advises health practitioners to consider the menstrual cycle as the “fifth vital sign”—meaning it is as important a health indicator as blood pressure, pulse rate, respiratory rate, and body temperature.</p><br> <p>Join naturopathic physician Stephanie Nishek for this informative webinar that will review the exploration and resolution of menstrual symptoms as essential aspects of a holistic approach to health and wellness. Topics covered will include: </p><br><ul><li>Fundamental menstrual cycle physiology</li><li>Disorders that can be flagged by an irregular cycle</li><li>The influence of endocrine organs on the menstrual cycle</li><li>Holistic strategies to address common menstrual complaints</li></ul> <p>You do not want to miss Dr. Nishek’s “physiology before pharmacology” approach to helping patients restore menstrual cycle balance!</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; female-health ; female-health ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; eb992c1b-fb50-435e-ab7e-d834ba016b07 ; 117 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/A Holistic Approach to Managing the Menstrual Cycle – A Woman’s Fifth Vital Sign (Wise Woman) 09302021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/A_Breakthrough_in_Diabetes_Care_(CuraLife)_03302022_1.vtt" ;
                     ; 7811b39d-d28e-4869-92cc-76590bf58e5d ; Managing Mood Disorders                                                                                                                                                                 ; Mood disorders impact millions of people yearly, and major depression is the leading cause of disability worldwide. Tune in as Dr. Todd Born unravels the mystery behind mood disorders and discusses clinically based interventions.   ; <p>Mental health issues that affect an individual’s emotional state in which they experience periods of extreme happiness, sadness, or both are known as mood disorders. At some point, over 20% of adults in the U.S. will experience a mood disorder. The World Health Organization projected in a 2008 publication that major depression, the third leading cause of the global disease burden at that time, would rank first by the year 2030. Currently, clinicians are significantly challenged when diagnosing and managing these affective disorders due to variations in patient presentation, the unpredictable prognosis of mood disorders, and the inconsistency of patient response to treatment. With the projected growth of disease burden, clinician capacity to diagnose and prescribe effective treatments will be strained even further.</p><br><p>Join naturopathic physician Todd Born as he takes you on a journey of how to unravel the mystery of mood disorders. Dr. Born will share an evaluation of the evidence and guide you through clinically based interventions designed to improve outcomes and lead patients with mood disorders down the road to reclaiming their lives.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; managing-mood-disorders ; managing-mood-disorders ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; bd43aa90-eb51-47fb-aa73-4fe0e15ac1e6 ; 112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Managing Mood Disorders (Allergy Research Group) 09162021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Managing_Mood_Disorders_(Allergy_Research_Group)_09162021_1.vtt" ;
                     ; ef5a1017-9b15-416d-8294-19ec48354d53 ; The Benefits of Moringa: Separating Fact from Fiction                                                                                                                                   ; Moringa is a super food widely used to combat malnutrition, but it has also been promoted as a panacea in some cultures. Delve into the research behind this plant and learn the truth about its nutritional benefits.                  ; <p>Moringa (M oleifera) is a tree native to areas of India, South Asia, and Africa. In some cultures, moringa is known as the “miracle tree” or “tree of life,” monikers that can be attributed to the nutritive value and medicinal benefits of the leaves, bark, flowers, fruit, seeds, and roots. Because of its tolerance to severe drought and mild frost conditions, its nutritional value, and the fact that it is inexpensive and easy to grow, moringa is cultivated throughout the world and is used as a food source in the fight against malnutrition.</p><br><p>There is clarity to be found amid the confounding reports in scientific journals and the claims promoting moringa as a panacea. Join nutritional biochemist Dr. Jed Fahey and moringa advocate Lisa Curtis, founder of Kuli Kuli, as they share their collective expertise regarding moringa.</p><br><p>What you will learn: </p><br> <ul><li>The nutritional profile and clinical benefits of moringa</li><li>How to identify and locate high-quality moringa</li><li>How to separate fact and fiction concerning moringa claims</li><li>What the research really shows about the use of moringa for various health conditions</li></ul><p>The speakers will close with recommendations for incorporating moringa into a daily dietary plan.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; moringa-the-miracle-tree_fahey ; moringa-the-miracle-tree_fahey ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 2588a0ac-0a77-4ef9-b95a-2ad04b1cff69,d7a98abe-d03b-4968-b112-2591852877c3 ; 102,119,103 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/The Benefits of Moringa - Separating Fact from Fiction (Kuli Kuli) 09092021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/The_“Allergic_Puzzle”_in_Modern_Times_(Guna_Biotherapeutics)_03212024.vtt" ;
                     ; 1b8e7131-c52b-413d-b230-4cfec5b74ae4 ; Solving for Antidepressant-Induced Nutrient Depletions: Science-Based Solutions                                                                                                         ; Medications, especially those designed to increase neurotransmitter activity, can create nutrient imbalances in the body. Learn how to identify medication-induced nutrient depletions and design full-spectrum wellness plans.         ; <p>It is inevitable that many of us will need medication at some point, necessary medication that may successfully treat a condition but may simultaneously create side effects that can affect patient compliance. This possibility, in addition to imbalances created by drug-nutrient interactions, can present challenges to integrative practitioners when creating holistic wellness plans. One of these challenges is referred to as medication-induced nutrient depletions (M.I.N.D.™).</p><br><p>Join Sarah Morgan, co-founder and CEO of Even, and Jill Carnahan, MD, board-certified integrative medicine physician, as they dive into responsible and innovative solutions for medication-induced nutrient depletions. In this third episode of an ongoing series, Sarah and Dr. Carnahan will cover interactions with commonly prescribed antidepressant drugs. You will learn: </p><br><ul><li>Pleiotropic effects of antidepressants</li><li>Common side effects/complaints from antidepressant users</li><li>M.I.N.D. related to antidepressants</li><li>How to create, implement, and monitor full-spectrum wellness plans for antidepressant users</li></ul> <p>Don’t miss this opportunity to learn first-hand how science and nutrition come together to bring wellness to patients and bridge the nutrition gap that can be created by pharmaceutical treatments.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; solving-for-antidepressant-induced ; solving-for-antidepressant-induced ; PUBLISHED ; ; ; ; ; 6bee80ff-990a-4b5a-a312-7950fd0a000f,af2261d6-4822-4d75-bce3-baf25a2be9fc ; 112 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Solving for Antidepressant-Induced Nutrient Depletions - Science-Based Solutions (EVEN) 09022021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Small_Intestinal_Dysbiosis_-_Understanding_the_SIBO_Matrix_(The_Biome_Clinic)_10.vtt" ;
                     ; e53ad620-50ee-4768-a0f2-9188d7ee7a29 ; Gut-Lung Axis: The Impact of Dysbiosis on Pulmonary Health                                                                                                                              ; Chronic lung conditions exhibit an altered pulmonary microbiome. Join Dr. Jocelyn Strand for a deep dive into the gut–lung axis to gain a clearer understanding of how gut dysbiosis may affect pulmonary health.                       ; <p>It is well established that the composition of the microflora in our gut is a factor in the development of many illnesses and is affected by genetic predisposition, diet, state of bacterial colonization, and exposure to substances that may disrupt the microbial balance. However, did you know that chronic lung conditions exhibit an altered pulmonary microbiome? The concept of the gut-lung axis posits that dysbiosis in the intestinal microbiota community may have a profound effect on pulmonary health.</p><br><p>Join Dr. Jocelyn Strand as she discusses the gut-lung axis and new clinical evidence supporting how the interrelationships between oral and gastrointestinal health influence respiratory health.</p><br><p>Attendees will learn: </p><br><ul><li>The significance of interplay between the microbiomes of the mouth, lungs, and GI tract </li><li>How the GI microbiome influences the development of systemic immunity</li><li>Clinical strategies and botanical support for a healthy microbiome</li></ul> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; gut-lung-axis-strand ; gut-lung-axis-strand ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/sfmmbp2q/brand-logo-biocidin.png ; brand-logo-biocidin ; Sponsor logo image for Biocidin Botanicals ; Biocidin Botanicals ; c8f9abd7-e6f5-4fb9-9945-9e3dbc6c8c8e ; 108,115,100,113,125,102,109 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/The Role of Dysbiosis in Pulmonary Health (Biocidin Botanicals) 06102021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Growing_a_Strong_Membership-Based_Integrative_Practice_(OriginsIncubator)_071320.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_08,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_09,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_19,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_20
                     ; feb27ea3-e6d8-4a22-8b00-ea2e2048d59c ; Compromised Immunity as a Comorbidity with Acute Infection                                                                                                                              ; Compromised immunity associated with chronic conditions can be overlooked when a patient contracts an acute infection. Join to learn common links between immunity and acute infections as well as some adapted treatment principles.   ; <p>Compromised immunity, particularly in patients with chronic conditions like Lyme disease, creates a unique circumstance when patients acquire acute infections. Integrative practitioners are faced with the challenge of treating patients that are already weakened and also with the reality that most of the medical reports on acute infection in patients with comorbidities concern patients with cardiovascular and metabolic conditions. When patients with Lyme disease—a group already underrepresented in the medical record—acquire an acute infection, they are at high risk for severe symptoms, hospitalization, and atypical response to standards of care. Understanding the nuances between chronic diseases like Lyme disease and acute illness is critical to providing responsive care that incorporates the whole, unique individual—a hallmark of integrative medical practice.</p><br><p>In this cutting-edge lecture, renowned Lyme expert, internist, and author Dr. Richard Horowitz will examine common pathophysiologic links between Lyme disease and acute infections and apply similarly adapted treatment principles. Don’t miss this opportunity to participate in this webinar and gain a first-hand understanding of how to best support the overlooked patient populations suffering from rare and underdiagnosed chronic illnesses.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; compromised-immunity-as-a-comorbidity-horowitz ; compromised-immunity-as-a-comorbidity-horowitz ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/awzkhjx0/xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 36066998-d75e-4e22-83bd-53a416b5e22f ; 100,101,108,109 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Chronic Bacterial and Viral Diseases - Clinical and Laboratory Diagnosis and Effective Integrative Treatment Strategies (XYMOGEN) 05112021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Clinical_Solutions_Using_Physiological_Regulating_Medicine_(GUNA_Biotherapeutics.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13
                     ; 42ecb7fa-bebd-4365-9d8a-62262f1ac441 ; Turmeric and Curcumin: Clinical Advances                                                                                                                                                ; The differences between the benefits of turmeric, curcumin, and curcuminoids are commonly misunderstood. This education webinar covers common questions, recent research, and potential clinical applications for future use.           ; <p>Curcumin from turmeric is one of the most extensively investigated constituents of natural origin. The benefits of curcumin are broadly validated with over 2,100 articles published in 2020 alone. Yet, scientific challenges still exist for accurately assessing curcumin ingredients.</p><br><p>Industry ingredient and curcumin expert Blake Ebersole offers unique insights into how to answer these challenges. You will learn: </p><br> <ul><li>How curcumin absorption claims are evaluated</li><li>The primary considerations that define the quality of turmeric and curcumin products</li><li>The commonly misunderstood differences between turmeric, curcumin, and curcuminoids</li> <p>Join us with speaker Blake Ebersole to expand your knowledge of turmeric, curcumin, and curcuminoids. He will cover frequently asked questions and share unique industry insights. Blake will also review recently published research and potential clinical applications for future use.</p> ; OVER_1_HOUR ; false ; tumeric-and-curcumin-clinical-advances ; tumeric-and-curcumin-clinical-advances ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/va1pxdot/naturpro-logo-webinar-sponsor.png ; naturpro-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for NaturPro Scientific ; NaturPro Scientific ; 1e09d66f-4b45-408a-ae6a-17cba309b59a ; 108,126,100,102,111,112,116 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Turmeric and Curcumin - Clinical Advances (NaturPro Scientific) 05062021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/The_Testosterone_SWITCH_-_A_Scientific_Approach_to_Naturally_Revitalize_Testoste.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_32,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_12,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_14,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_18,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21
                     ; 66903117-a09d-48b0-a210-bfc85c0b2d38 ; Testosterone and Prostate Cancer: What Is the Connection?                                                                                                                               ; Prostate cancer treatment, such as androgen deprivation therapy, can cause lower testosterone in the body. Tune in as Dr. Matthew Stanizzi discusses developing a prostate cancer treatment plan and testosterone's role.               ; <p>Prostate cancer is not a singular illness, and it can present many clinical scenarios with a wide range of variables. Understanding how prostate cancer is classified, staged, and graded is vital to determining an appropriate treatment protocol for each individual. As part of the standard of care for prostate cancer treatment, androgen deprivation therapy (ADT) reduces testosterone levels and is effective at controlling prostate cancer growth, but it has known, common side effects. Recognizing when testosterone is indicated or when ADT may be the best option are important components of developing a treatment plan for prostate cancer. </p><br><p>Don’t miss this dynamic presentation delivered by expert urologist Dr. Matthew Stanizzi as he details the background and latest scientific data related to the use and risks of testosterone for prostate cancer patients. Dr. Stanizzi will discuss treatments used when ADT is employed and recent evidence that will help to answer frequently asked questions regarding the role of testosterone in the cause and growth of prostate cancer.</p> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; false ; testosterone-and-prostate-cancer ; testosterone-and-prostate-cancer ; PUBLISHED ; https://media.umbraco.io/webs-courteous-wombat/ukujgjzx/biorestore-sponsor-image.png ; biorestore-sponsor-image ; Sponsor logo image for BioRestore ; BioRestore ; 970c92be-1c64-437a-adcb-79e9c40c8c2f ; 118,101 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Prostate Cancer and Testosterone - What's the Connection (BioRestore) 04222021_1.mp4" ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinar Captions/Telomeres_and_Immune_Senescence_(T.A._Sciences)_06162022_1.vtt" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_11,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_13,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_16,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_27,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
                     ; c536efd8-aefd-4162-8ec1-ecef441167c0 ; Heart Health and Obesity: Unlocking Metabolic Vulnerability                                                                                                                             ; Cardiometabolic health is crucial to overall health and well-being. Join Dr. Regina Druz for a discussion on managing cardiometabolic risk factors like obesity and developing a patient-care strategy to improve cardiac health.       ; <p>Cardiometabolic health is a strong predictor of a healthy cardiac outcome. New evidence continues to emerge, helping researchers and practitioners gain a deeper understanding of the significant influence that managing cardiometabolic risk factors, like obesity, can have in maintaining and improving cardiac health. In this informative webinar, renowned integrative cardiologist Regina Druz will introduce attendees to the major trials of obesity management that were published in 2024. Merging current research with her extensive clinical acumen, Dr. Druz will provide participants with the tools to develop a patient-care strategy to improve cardiac health through a structured cardiometabolic approach. Key takeaways will include: </p><br> <ul><li>How cardiometabolic conditions and their risk factors influence cardiac outcomes</li><li>Significant conclusions from recent obesity management research</li><li>Interventions, protocols, and diet and lifestyle modifications that support cardiometabolic health</li></ul> ; UNDER_1_HOUR ; true ; reginadruz ; reginadruz ; PUBLISHED ; ; xymogen-logo-webinar-sponsor ; Sponsor logo image for XYMOGEN ; Xymogen ; 5622754d-67b5-43af-b3b0-910d50847c2a ; 105 ; "https://webwholescriptstorage.blob.core.windows.net/wholescriptvideos/Webinars/Heart Health and Obesity - Unlocking Metabolic Vulnerability (XYMOGEN) 04292025.mp4" ; "" ; Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_02,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_03,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_06,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_15,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_21,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_29,Z_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_26
